Ray>>\"\n ]\n}\n\n##### 9: 31_1872-02-23_pna_sn82016419_00212472967_1872022301_0373.json  kinds=['report', 'report'] fields=['place_type', 'people']\n=== 31_1872-02-23_pna_sn82016419_00212472967_1872022301_0373.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/f458df066eab2f4a9e7b39f7.jpg']\nheadline: \n---\nPractical JoKEs.-They had a\nterrifying sen sation in a boarding\nhouse in Davenport, Iowa, the other\nevening, the result of the penchant\nof lady for little fun. This lady\nput on a ghostly mask, donned a\ncoat of her husbands, and, creeping\nsoftly to the door of another lady,\npushed it ajar, and, with a groan,\nput her head i'll the opening. The\noccupant turned, and looked, and\ngave Il shrek, and fell to the floor\nin spasns. The fun maker saw the\nresult of her sport, and swooned\naway. The noise made by the vic\ntim caused rush of other boarders\nto the scene, who appreciated the\nsituation at once. 1t was with\ngreat difficulty that the frightened\nlady was restored to consciousness,\nand after that she was in crazed\nstate of mind for several hours.\nMeantime the other lady was taken\nto her room, where Testoratiyes\nbrought her to her senses. She in\nquired as to the condition of her\nfriend, and, when some one told her\nthe facts, she tainted again, remain\ning in an alarming condition so long\nthat her husband and all about her\nwere filled with the direst appre-\ntensions. Both ladies were unable\nto leaYe their rooms the next day.\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"Practical JoKEs.-They had a\",\n \"rules\": [\n  7\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E6\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"a boarder in a ghostly mask frightens another into spasms\",\n \"place\": \"a boarding house in Davenport, Iowa  <<in a boarding house in Davenport, Iowa>>\",\n \"place_state\": \"Iowa  <<Davenport, Iowa>>\",\n \"seen\": \"a head in a ghostly mask, with a groan  <<put on a ghostly mask>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"hoax  <<the penchant of lady for little fun>>\",\n \"specific_place\": \"the boarding house  <<in a boarding house in Davenport, Iowa>>\",\n \"place_type\": \"inn_or_hotel  <<in a boarding house in Davenport, Iowa>>\",\n \"precision\": \"building  <<in a boarding house in Davenport, Iowa>>\",\n \"people\": [\n  \"the lady frightened  <<The occupant>>\",\n  \"the lady in the mask  <<This lady put on a ghostly mask>>\"\n ]\n}\n--- SECOND: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"This lady put on a ghostly mask\",\n \"rules\": [\n  7\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E6\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"prankster in a ghostly mask frightened a boarder and was found out\",\n \"place\": \"a boarding house in Davenport, Iowa  <<a boarding house in Davenport, Iowa>>\",\n \"place_state\": \"Iowa  <<Iowa>>\",\n \"seen\": \"a ghostly mask  <<a ghostly mask>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"hoax  <<the penchant of lady for little fun>>\",\n \"specific_place\": \"a boarding house  <<a boarding house>>\",\n \"place_type\": \"house  <<a boarding house>>\",\n \"precision\": \"building  <<a boarding house>>\",\n \"people\": [\n  \"another lady  <<another lady>>\"\n ]\n}\n\n##### 10: 40_1879-01-04_p1_sn85042459_00280769009_1879010401_0005.json  kinds=['other', 'idiom'] fields=[]\n=== 40_1879-01-04_p1_sn85042459_00280769009_1879010401_0005.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/edd1faed275dca265628e6c8.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/b747928fc7fb3be6c0965ddb.jpg']\nheadline: Joo Jefferson.\n---\nOne wonders that the man is not\nentirely subservient 20 the actor,\nwrites a correspondent about Jeffer-\nson. Indeed, in private life, the\nsame tones, and even at times the\nbroken accent, are noticeable. That\nhe has good reason to be attached\nto his part, even \"a man of success\"\nwould admit, for it has brought\nhim, so I am told by an intimate\nfriend, over $1,nOO,0O0.\n\n\nIn private lifo he is very jolly,\nalways in good spirits, and in man\nners, while inclining to the brusque,\nthose of a gentleman. / had never\nseen him off the stage until last\nweek, and it must be confessed that\nno woman was ever so completely\nmetamorphosed by \"make up\" as\nour venerable jefferson. A little\nover the medium height, with q\nwell-knit frame and tendency to\nstoutness, regular and rather small\nfeatures, smooth face, and, in spite\nof his fifty years, thick, dark hair\nwithout a thread of silver. In\ndress. very plain, and wearing no\nJCW anu 40 L lClll al htt pclOIt,\nin voice and accent \"Rir,\" and,\nthat indeed, was the only recogniz.\nable point.\n\n\nWhile In Chicago he makes his\nhome at his fatber-in-law's, who\nresides In comfortable style on\nMichigan Avenue. 1t will be re-\nmembered that eleven years ego\nthe great actor married Miss\nWarren, of Buffalo, a lady who,\nthough not a member of the pro-\nfession, comes from an old and\nhighly respectable theatrical fami.\nly, and is u niece of ex-Mayor frice\nof this city. A blonde, aud very\n| graceful, she ia intellectual and\naccomplished, and has won many\nfriends through her charming\nmanners and generous heart.\n\n\nMr.. and Mrs. Jefferson have two\nbright little children, q son and\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"other\",\n \"kq\": \"always in good spirits\",\n \"rules\": [],\n \"slices\": [],\n \"note\": \"a profile of Joe Jefferson; spirits and medium in their ordinary senses\"\n}\n--- SECOND: {\n \"kind\": \"idiom\",\n \"kq\": \"always in good spirits\",\n \"rules\": [\n  10\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E2\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"good spirits: mood\"\n}\n\n##### 11: 68_1856-07-30_p1_sn82015753_00212475385_1856073001_0834.json  kinds=['other', 'idiom'] fields=[]\n=== 68_1856-07-30_p1_sn82015753_00212475385_1856073001_0834.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/e055166cc9b45672a559f54d.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/f592