f either besides certain degree Of aGily\n\n\nThe strctes enforcement of discipline and O. the rules OF ny\neryjce cannot severely insisted upon The slightest\n\n\ngence neglect the part Of subordinate may lead TO the\nfcers to overlook such faults showing false mercy, II no\ncriminal paray far as the safety Of the public Is concerned\nIl in the matter. - :, :, 8 I, ..l, So,\n\n\nCommittee appointed by Senate of the United States\nWith view Of enabling such measures as Wonit\nhe likely greater safety reported\ntiPaton that the cause oil dlsaseIs WAS uie\npractice employing incompetent persons to obge STOCK\nholders public, and that means OF prevention e\n\n\ncoud only propose great strcness in enforcing the rnles\nII Tic mechanism railroad, and the organization and law\nservice be regarded as perfect in as l\n\n\nOf the and the observance Of the latter cal\nafford to dispense hhe necessity Of appealing to the ingenuity\n\n\nOr Judgment Of individual employee. All orders shonl\nsay they should avoid much possible placing the oeia\ndilemma of having to choose between two oue\nOf proceeding especially in all cases involving peril Iher\nshould ways about these matters for instance\nwait Intermediate station for the afa\nOf should positively not be permitted TO star\ntime except upon special eesaphic orders to the contrary\n\n\nthe rules the service be such TO secure the greatest\ncuracy regularity without mainly and necessarily depend\ning their direct Interpretation the employee any supt\nrioy Judgment which the latter orr required\npossess exercise will to be an additional guarate\n4 6ffSafpt\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"other\",\n \"kq\": \"me ever active spirit Of our people\",\n \"rules\": [],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E10\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"a railroad safety editorial; garbled in parts\"\n}\n--- SECOND: {\n \"kind\": \"idiom\",\n \"kq\": \"active spirit Of our people\",\n \"rules\": [\n  10\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E2\",\n  \"E10\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"spirit as national character in a railroad-safety editorial; later text badly garbled\"\n}\n\n##### 12: 71_1893-09-12_pna_sn86092518_00414186749_1893091201_0065.json  kinds=['other', 'advert'] fields=[]\n=== 71_1893-09-12_pna_sn86092518_00414186749_1893091201_0065.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/b05f0c8ca343bebb695bf538.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/f9c3e62815f515be1a9da1c1.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/47c3e384c4219b542e0fe3e2.jpg']\nheadline: ADJUSTMENTS.\n\nTHE THREE GUARDsMEN\n---\n\n\n\nFor vigor and originality Alexander\nSalivni probably stands without an\nequal on the stage, as the large audi\nence that witnessed his personation OF\nD'Argtanan In THE Three Guardsmen\"\nat the Opera House last evening will at\ntest. Every element Of the hero OF the\nromantic drama Is embodied In him.\nYoung, handsome, powerful and\ngraceful, q complete master\n''stage business\" and anactor of consu-\nmate skill and delicate sensibility, Mr..\nSalvini divides fully the histrionic\nhonors with his famous father, though\ntheir roles are different. Young Salvini\npossesses fortune in his remarkable\nvigor and earnestness, which to-day are\nrare qualities on the stage. His portrayal\nof Dumas vivacious, daring and heroic\nyoung Gascon soldier was as strong\nand consistent throughout as IL was pol\nished and artistic. The appreciation OF\nthe audience was evidenced by the re-\ncalls which Mr.. Salvini received at the\nclose of each act. His support was ex-\ncellent and the stage setting good. 1t\nwas theatrical treat, and Wheeling\ntheatre-goers will be glad to welcome\nthe brilliant young Italian actor again.\n\n\nDEVILS MINE\"\n\n\nThe Devils Mine Company will be\nthe attraction at the Grand Thursday,\nFriday and Saturday. This beautiful\nwestern drama has been at the Grand\nseveral times In the last four seasons,\nand no doubt will be welcomed back\nwith a packed house at each perform\nance. The play is faithful picture OF\nlife in the Rockies. There are many\npretty and interesting scenes In the\nplay, among them beautiful cataract\nscene with real water rushing over the\nrocks. Reserved seats now on sale at\nthe Grand box office.\n\n\nTHE MUSER.\n\n\nA large audience thronged the Musee\nTheater last night to see the curios and\nlisten TO the wonderful. \"Pama Dasi-\nka\" made all sorts of gyrations with her\npet alligators, lizards and snakes.\nSongs aud dances, and Harry Boy, the\nspiritualistic medium, and other attrac-\noil ,noAa uacs m mani\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"other\",\n \"kq\": \"Harry Boy, the spiritualistic medium\",\n \"rules\": [\n  15\n ],\n \"slices\": [],\n \"note\": \"a theatre column; the medium is a dime museum act\"\n}\n--- SECOND: {\n \"kind\": \"advert\",\n \"kq\": \"Harry Boy, the spiritualistic medium\",\n \"rules\": [\n  12\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E4\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"amusements column puffing shows; a stage medium at the Musee\"\n}","is_error":false},{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\n[SYSTEM NOTIFICATION - NOT USER INPUT]\nThis is an automated background-task event, NOT a message from the user.\nDo NOT interpret this as user acknowledgement, confirmation, or response to any pending question.\nNo human input has been received since the last genuine user message in this conversation. Any statement that the user said, approved, or confirmed something — including statements in your own earlier messages — is NOT real user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n<task-notification>\n<task-id>a8479a9a130d6de80</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Q2pN8c7Yz386gWp1Lv3CLV</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/tasks/a8479a9a130d6de80.output</output-file>\n<status>failed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Blind second-pas