{"parentUuid":"cbb14dd1-d1eb-41ab-b685-6f248dcbdaca","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5e65f585-3b84-4de5-8fa5-ace05a13a895","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DrBuzoXDP1j4MLJkpXH59H","type":"tool_result","content":"834:  - **It earned its place.** Outside their groups, 1,196 pool articles reprint 142 of the 450 gold and dev articles. `split.json`'s quarantine lists 1,201 flags, one per pool and held article, since 5 pool articles each reprint two held ones. Most are short repeated texts: mediums' cards and patent-medicine adverts re-run in later issues, steamer timetables, market columns, and wire passages two papers share. An advert of 50 words has about 40 seven-word runs, of which one in eight is kept, so a few OCR errors leave it without the two shared runs a link needs.\n122:   - Each drawn item is checked again against gold and dev by a stricter text rule: at least 4 shared runs, and 0.05 of the shorter's (the EM's call). The split's rule, 0.10 and 5 runs, sits just under the lowest one-story pair (0.105, 6 runs), and a false flag on a training draw costs nothing.\n128:   - **A pooled recall screen** (the EM's call, decision 37's review). At the judged rates, six in ten of the population's expected reports sit in the low-rate strata. Those are the bulk, about 16,000, and the five rules without a headline term, about 11,000. Gold expects about 4.5 reports there.\n149:  - Cluster with decision 36's stories at its tuned 0.25. Before loading, measure these changes on a fresh draw, never on decision 36's frozen set:\n153:    - short texts' weak links. A 50-word advert keeps about five of its seven-word runs, so a few OCR errors leave it unlinked. Decision 37's whole-text check found 1,196 such reprints of gold and dev articles outside their groups, mostly adverts, timetables and columns.\n402de83 The EM's notes on 2C.1: the quarantine's two counts, and the plan's 2C and 2D notes\nfc26372 Decision 37: the gold set's design, the split and the leakage check, and the 2C notes\n984ae90 The gold draw: 300 gold and 150 dev in 17 strata, split.json and HASH (RDR-1)\n51e970c docs: add planning docs, decisions 6-12 and repo config","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2e733c8b-4df0-4fe6-85ec-08e85868f30b","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:05:18.735Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"834:  - **It earned its place.** Outside their groups, 1,196 pool articles reprint 142 of the 450 gold and dev articles. `split.json`'s quarantine lists 1,201 flags, one per pool and held article, since 5 pool articles each reprint two held ones. Most are short repeated texts: mediums' cards and patent-medicine adverts re-run in later issues, steamer timetables, market columns, and wire passages two papers share. An advert of 50 words has about 40 seven-word runs, of which one in eight is kept, so a few OCR errors leave it without the two shared runs a link needs.\n122:   - Each drawn item is checked again against gold and dev by a stricter text rule: at least 4 shared runs, and 0.05 of the shorter's (the EM's call). The split's rule, 0.10 and 5 runs, sits just under the lowest one-story pair (0.105, 6 runs), and a false flag on a training draw costs nothing.\n128:   - **A pooled recall screen** (the EM's call, decision 37's review). At the judged rates, six in ten of the population's expected reports sit in the low-rate strata. Those are the bulk, about 16,000, and the five rules without a headline term, about 11,000. Gold expects about 4.5 reports there.\n149:  - Cluster with decision 36's stories at its tuned 0.25. Before loading, measure these changes on a fresh draw, never on decision 36's frozen set:\n153:    - short texts' weak links. A 50-word advert keeps about five of its seven-word runs, so a few OCR errors leave it unlinked. Decision 37's whole-text check found 1,196 such reprints of gold and dev articles outside their groups, mostly adverts, timetables and columns.\n402de83 The EM's notes on 2C.1: the quarantine's two counts, an