{"parentUuid":"d1fdc2e9-0dee-47a7-90d6-a6b90580144c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaqWmNrUR3b5kbDHNQCT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JPjx37fvEoXgYsq9YEU92e","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 108,125p \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md\" | cut -c1-300","description":"Read the 2C section of the build plan"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":257,"cache_read_input_tokens":671416,"output_tokens":169,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":19},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":257,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":169,"cache_read_input_tokens":671416,"cache_creation_input_tokens":257,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":257},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JPjx37fvEoXgYsq9YEU92e":{"command":"sed -n 108,125p \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md\" | cut -c1-300","description":"Read the 2C section of the build plan"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"e642f6b3-a980-40f8-b7f0-9ecac79be27f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgaqWkhAtAMrV7pHCCAiS","requestRef":"a694ab6c-4c81-4408-ac4d-0811b80e6101","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3db14d2f-307b-436d-9417-2e2a535897db","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:05:43.739Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"3db14d2f-307b-436d-9417-2e2a535897db","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5e65f585-3b84-4de5-8fa5-ace05a13a895","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JPjx37fvEoXgYsq9YEU92e","type":"tool_result","content":"### 2C: the reader\n**Persona:** ML specialist.\n1. Write `POLICY.md`, build the gold set, freeze it and hash it.\n   - Gold, dev and train split by the most inclusive grouping: connected components over eval A's links and the body probe's links (decisions 36 and 37). `scripts/check_leakage.py` compares whole texts too, and the training pool takes at most one printing per story.\n   - The draw (`scripts/gold_draw.py`, decision 37): 300 gold and 150 dev articles in 17 strata, each with its inclusion weight, in `eval/gold/split.json` and `HASH`. Dev has gold's design and is labelled by hand under `POLICY.md` too, so model selection aims at gold's truth.\n   - The gold set's term strata include each of lexicon v2's five rules. That's how ouija, kept with 0 reports in its 6 sampled candidates, gets measured (decision 31).\n   - `POLICY.md` settles delusions and hallucinations with one rule. Eval A counts a 1904 defendant pointing at an \"imaginary\" spectre in court as a report, and a 1909 lunacy hearing's spooks as other. Its interval barely moves either way.\n   - It also settles claims of spirit control and of a felt presence of the dead. Decision 30 counts two such articles as borderline reports, and they are half of the reports it found.\n   - And decision 31's two borderline kinds: a claim inside a narrative whose truth is doubtful, and a particular claim told inside a general essay. It confirms or overrules counting a first-person claim of communication with a named dead person, made in a lecture or an interview.\n   - A story place that is only a town resolves from a county or state the text gives, or from its dateline. Otherwise it stays unresolved. It never falls back on the paper's state, which put 2 of decision 34's 9 towns in the wrong place. Measure the rule on the gold set.\n2. Build the labelling page (`scripts/label_gold.py`, local only).\n3. Label gold and dev before seeing any model output, with a blind second pass on gold to measure agreement. Then freeze them: `HASH` gains the labels' sha256.\n4. Teacher labels for the training pool, with the leakage check passing.\n   - The training draw comes from `split.json`'s pool, at most one printing per story, and `check_leakage.py` is extended to check that draw.\n   - Each drawn item is checked again against gold and dev by a stricter text rule: at least 4 shared runs, and 0.05 of the shorter's (the EM's call). The split's rule, 0.10 and 5 runs, sits just under the lowest one-story pair (0.105, 6 runs), and a false flag on a training draw costs nothing.\n5. Baselines: a keyword rule, and base 4B both zero-shot and few-shot.\n6. LoRA training on Tinker, iterating on the dev split until improvements stop. Each iteration is recorded.\n7. Eval B, ablations B1 to B10, and edge-case slices E1 to E14.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"46b4fba6-6fb7-43c5-b8b4-63b29eee36fb","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:05:44.687Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"### 2C: the reader\n**Persona:** ML specialist.\n1. Write `POLICY.md`, build the gold set, freeze it and hash it.\n   - Gold, dev and train split by the most inclusive grouping: connected components over eval A's links and the body probe's links (decisions 36 and 37). `scripts/check_leakage.py` compares whole texts too, and the training pool takes at most one printing per story.\n   - The draw (`scripts/gold_draw.py`, decision 37): 300 gold and 150 dev articles in 17 strata, each with its inclusion weight, in `eval/gold/split.json` and `HASH`. Dev has gold's design and is labelled by hand under `POLICY.md` too, so model selection aims at gold's truth.\n   - The gold set's term strata include each of lexicon v2's five rules. That's how ouija, kept with 0 reports in its 6 sampled candidates, gets measured (decision 31).\n   - `POLICY.md` settles delusions and hallucinations with one rule. Eval A counts a 1904 defendant pointing at an \"imaginary\" spectre in court as a report, and a 1909 lunacy hearing's spooks as other. Its interval barely moves either way.\n   - It also settles claims of spirit control and of a felt presence of the dead. Decision 30 counts two such articles as borderline reports, and they are half of the reports it found.\n   - And decision 31's two borderline kinds: a claim inside a narrative whose truth is doubtful, and a particular claim told inside a general essay. It confirms or overrules counting a first-person claim of communication with a named dead person, made in a lecture or an interview.\n   - A story place that is only a town resolves from a county or state the text gives, or from its dateline. Otherwise it stays unresolved. It never falls back on the paper's state, which put 2 of decision 34's 9 towns in the wrong place. Measure the rule on the gold set.\n2. Build the labelling page (`scripts/label_gold.py`, local only).\n3. Label gold and dev before seeing any model output, with a blind second pass on gold to measure agreement. Then freeze them: `HASH` gains the labels' sha256.\n4. Teacher labels for the training pool, with the leakage check passing.\n   - The training draw comes from `split.json`'s pool, at most one printing per story, and `check_leakage.py` is extended to check that draw.\n   - Each drawn item is checked again against gold and dev by a stricter text rule: at least 4 shared runs, and 0.05 of the shorter's (the EM's call). The split's rule, 0.10 and 5 runs, sits just under the lowest one-story pair (0.105, 6 runs), and a false flag on a training draw costs nothing.\n5. Baselines: a keyword rule, and base 4B both zero-shot and few-shot.\n6. LoRA training on Tinker, iterating on the dev split until improvements stop. Each iteration is recorded.\n7. Eval B, ablations B1 to B10, and edge-case slices E1 to E14.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e642f6b3-a980-40f8-b7f0-9ecac79be27f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2c-reader","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3db14d2f-307b-436d-9417-2e2a535897db","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
