{"parentUuid":"b20bfa62-1a5d-4fe2-8e9e-ab3d9c8e3c3f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5e65f585-3b84-4de5-8fa5-ace05a13a895","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011gA1qWaxt8zxhB2tJYmJcV","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"db4e7307-ce98-44cd-a5c5-48d951b1ac7b","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:05:53.384Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md","oldString":"3. Label gold and dev before seeing any model output, with a blind second pass on gold to measure agreement. Then freeze them: `HASH` gains the labels' sha256.","newString":"3. Label gold and dev before seeing any model output, with a blind second pass on gold to measure agreement. Then freeze them: `HASH` gains the labels' sha256.\n   - Done in decision 38. `labels.jsonl` and `dev_labels.jsonl` hold one label per article, the ruling where the passes disagreed. The second pass is in `second_pass.jsonl`, and each dispute's two labels and ruling are in `adjudication.jsonl`. Evals read only the two label files, and `check_leakage.py` checks their hashes.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":117,"oldLines":6,"newStart":117,"newLines":7,"lines":["    - A story place that is only a town resolves from a county or state the text gives, or from its dateline. Otherwise it stays unresolved. It never falls back on the paper's state, which put 2 of decision 34's 9 towns in the wrong place. Measure the rule on the gold set."," 2. Build the labelling page (`scripts/label_gold.py`, local only)."," 3. Label gold and dev before seeing any model output, with a blind second pass on gold to measure agreement. Then freeze them: `HASH` gains the labels' sha256.","+   - Done in decision 38. `labels.jsonl` and `dev_labels.jsonl` hold one label per article, the ruling where the passes disagreed. The second pass is in `second_pass.jsonl`, and each dispute's two labels and ruling are in `adjudication.jsonl`. Evals read only the two label files, and `check_leakage.py` checks their hashes."," 4. Teacher labels for the training pool, with the leakage check passing.","    - The training draw comes from `split.json`'s pool, at most one printing per story, and `check_leakage.py` is extended to check that draw.","    - Each drawn item is checked again against gold and dev by a stricter text rule: at least 4 shared runs, and 0.05 of the shorter's (the EM's call). The split's rule, 0.10 and 5 runs, sits just under the lowest one-story pair (0.105, 6 runs), and a false flag on a training draw costs nothing."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b20bfa62-1a5d-4fe2-8e9e-ab3d9c8e3c3f","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
