ake and seeing only file names.","+  - A usage limit stopped seven of them partway, and each was resumed in its own blind context.","+  - Each agent checked its labels against its packet's texts alone. Then all 330 went through `checked()` into `eval/gold/second_pass.jsonl`, never into the label files the evals read.","+- **Agreement, before any ruling** (`eval/results/phase2c/agreement.json`). Rates come with Wilson intervals, and κ with a bootstrap of 2,000 resamples:","+","+  | | Articles | Kind | κ on kind | Report or not | κ on report |","+  |---|---|---|---|---|---|","+  | gold | 300 | 271 (86.5–93.2%) | 0.88 (0.84–0.92) | 296 (96.6–99.5%) | 0.95 (0.89–0.99) |","+  | dev sample | 30 | 25 (66–93%) | 0.79 (0.61–0.95) | 30 (89–100%) | 1.00 |","+  | both | 330 | 296 (86–93%) | 0.87 (0.83–0.91) | 326 (96.9–99.5%) | 0.95 (0.90–0.99) |","+","+  - **On the 45 gold articles both passes call reports,** each field agrees:","+    - outcome 43 (85–99%)","+    - place_state 42 (82–98%)","+    - precision 40 (77–95%)","+    - place, specific place and place type 39 each (74–94%)","+    - seen 37 (69–91%)","+    - people 26 (43–71%)","+","+    The dev sample has 4 such reports.","+  - **When a field agrees:**","+    - Both passes leave it empty.","+    - Outcome, place_type, precision and place_state: the same value.","+    - Place, seen and the specific place: quotes that overlap in the text, or the same value.","+    - People: each person's quote overlaps one of the other pass's, both ways.","+  - **People is the loosest field.** Most of its disagreements are a person one pass adds who didn't see or claim anything: a reporter, an editor, or a crowd told of it afterwards.","+- **The rulings** (`eval/gold/adjudication.jsonl`): 69 articles disagreed, 61 of them in gold. 34 were on kind, and 35 on fields alone.","+  - Each ruling went through `checked()` and replaced its article's label. The record keeps the first pass's label, the second's, the ruling and its reason.","+  - 58 uphold the first pass, 6 take the second's call, and 5 mend fields.","+  - **16 of the 34 kind disagreements were one question:** spirit or medium in an ordinary sense, \"in good spirits\" or \"an advertising medium\". The first pass called these `other`, the second `idiom`. The ruling is `other`, since `POLICY.md`'s idioms are figures about ghosts.","+  - **The second pass's call was taken six times:**","+    - Basingstoke's haunted clock, a report told with a closing quip (rule 8), which makes gold's 46th report","+    - a spiritualist society's display notice, an advert","+    - a puff for the paper's own Sunday story, an advert","+    - a camp meeting's \"séance behind the woodshed\", a figure for a whipping","+    - spiritualists on cremation in a Catholic note, `other`","+    - a stated house as a place type","+  - **Fields were emptied where a value wasn't stated:** \"claimed to be haunted\" states nothing seen, and a clerk's workplace isn't where his sittings were.","+  - **`POLICY.md` version 3,** dated, adds the two clarifications the rulings settled, which every label already follows. Spirit or medium in an ordinary sense is `other` (rule 10), and a display notice of meetings and messages is an advert (rule 12).","+- **The freeze** (`1e64421`):","+  - `eval/gold/HASH` lists the sha256 of `labels.jsonl` and `dev_labels.jsonl` beside `split.json`'s, committed before any model output.","+  - The two files hold exactly 300 and 150 labels, one per article. Each is the first pass's label where the passes agreed, and the ruling where they didn't. All pass `checked()` (`second_pass.py frozen`).","+  - `check_leakage.py` now checks every file `HASH` lists.","+  - Gold's final kinds: 46 reports, 89 other, 66 fiction, 60 idiom, 30 adverts, 9 religious. Dev's: 32 reports, 44 other, 31 fiction, 26 idiom, 10 adverts, 7 religious.","+- **Gold's reports by stratum** (`eval/results/phase2c/gold_measures.json`), against the draw's expectation:","+","+  | Stratum | Gold | Reports | Expected |","+  |---|---|---|---|","+  | E8: phantom ships, trains and lights | 8 | 0 | 0.0 (0.0–6.3) |","+  | E6: hoaxes and pranksters | 8 | 3 | not judged |","+  | E12: not in English | 7 | 0 | 0.0 (0.0–3.4) |","+  | before 1850 | 20 | 0 | 0.0 (0.0–4.1) |","+  | ouija, term in the headline | 8 | 2 | 2.5 (1.0–4.6) |","+  | ouija, none in the headline | 12 | 0 | 0.7 (0.4–1.3) |","+  | seance, term in the headline | 10 | 2 | 3.1 (1.3–5.8) |","+  | seance, none in the headline | 12 | 1 | 0.7 (0.4–1.3) |","+  | spirit_phrase, term in the headline | 10 | 7 | 3.1 (1.3–5.8) |","+  | spirit_phrase, none in the headline | 12 | 3 | 0.7 (0.4–1.3) |","+  | spiritualism, term in the headline | 10 | 1 | 3.1 (1.3–5.8) |","+  | spiritualism, none in the headline | 12 | 1 | 0.7 (0.4–1.3) |","+  | spirit+medium, term in the headline | 6 | 4 | 1.8 (0.8–3.5) |","+  | spirit+medium, none in the headline | 14 | 0 | 0.9 (0.5–1.5) |","+  | v1 terms only, term in the headline | 80 | 20 | 17.1 (6.1–38.1) |","+  | v1 terms only, none in the headline | 46 | 2 | 0.8 (0.3–2.3) |","+  | near misses | 25 | 0 | 0.0 (0.0–0.3) |","+  | **all** | **300** | **46** | **35.3 (14.0–86.5)** |","+","+  - The 46 sit inside the expected range, above its centre.","+  - E6, which nothing judged, adds 3.","+  - The rules' headline strata hold 16 against about 13.6 expected, and the low-rate rule strata 5 against about 3.7.","+  - At 46 reports, a field right in 39 of them has a Wilson interval of about 72–92%.","+- **The weighted report rate** (Σ weight × report / Σ weight, over candidates and near misses): 0.97%, with a stratified bootstrap interval of 0.38–1.81%.","+- **The story-place rule, as code** (`gold_measures.story_state`), was written and tested before the freeze and run once after it.","+  - It takes a state named after a comma in the place's quote. Else, a town from the quote named elsewhere with a state after a comma. Else, the dateline's state. It never takes the paper's state.","+  - On gold's 34 reports with a place, it agrees with the labelled `place_state` on 31 (77–97%): 7 the same state, 24 both empty.","+  - It never gives a wrong state. Its 3 misses are states the OCR prints after a period (\"Allentown. Pa\", \"Springfield. Ohio\") or apart from the place's quote (Georgia).","+  - **The paper's state**, decision 34's fallback, matches only 2 of the 10 labelled states (6–51%). Most of the papers print no state, or are elsewhere.","+- **Slices on the frozen labels, gold then dev:**","+","+  | E1 | E2 | E3 | E4 | E5 | E6 | E7 | E8 | E9 | E10 | E11 | E12 | E13 | E14 |","+  |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+  | 3, 4 | 35, 15 | 32, 9 | 11, 2 | 30, 26 | 12, 3 | 23, 10 | 8, 5 | 115, 44 | 12, 9 | 9, 3 | 7, 3 | 1, 1 | 21, 9 |","+","+  - E9 comes from the grouping: 159 of the 450 are in a group of two or more.","+  - E1 and E13 are too thin to measure alone.","+- **The grouping missed one reprint within gold:** the comic sketch of a backwoods preacher is printed twice in gold. Two printings within gold don't leak into training, and both are labelled `fiction`."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/DECISIONS.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"c3149e56-7696-4cd0-bfba-7db27e1aead2","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2c-reader","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"pr