{"parentUuid":"84dca045-d0d7-47cc-baed-4a85c666a5d2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgaqj6NS5L2ZaVDQPyKre","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"2C.2: GATE PASSED\n\nEverything is committed and pushed. `git ls-remote` matches HEAD at a8cb601, and the tree is clean. `make test` passes (379 tests) and `make lint` is clean.\n\n- **Labels:** all 300 gold and 150 dev pass `checked()`, and each file holds exactly one label per article in its split. The freeze is at 1e64421. Its `HASH` lines cover exactly those 300 and 150 labels, and `check_leakage.py` now checks every file `HASH` lists.\n- **Second-pass rows** are kept out of the frozen files, in `eval/gold/second_pass.jsonl` (330 labels). `adjudication.jsonl` keeps each dispute's two labels, the ruling and its reason.\n- **Agreement before rulings:** on gold, kind matches in 271 of 300 (κ 0.88, 0.84–0.92). Report-or-not matches in 296 of 300 (κ 0.95). People is the weakest field (26 of 45).\n- **Rulings:** all 69 disputes are ruled. 58 uphold the first pass, 6 take the second's call and 5 mend fields. POLICY version 3 adds two dated clarifications from them, which every label already follows.\n- **Gold measures:** 46 reports against the 35.3 expected, and a weighted report rate of 0.97%. The story-place rule agrees on 31 of 34 places with no wrong state; the paper's state matches 2 of 10.\n- **Blindness:** seven agents were resumed in their own blind contexts after the usage limit. One saw two scratch folders' file names, but no contents.\n\nThe hand-over note is `step-2C.2.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":306,"cache_read_input_tokens":687858,"output_tokens":567,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":306,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":567,"cache_read_input_tokens":687858,"cache_creation_input_tokens":306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":306},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a5453873-a7bc-46d4-b0a0-d3999171d0a0","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgaqj5mxqzaqWF5U6oUVP","requestRef":"7d070d8b-443d-4e3a-9d48-47b541d0307f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"149450a1-ff80-459c-8ce7-d8af6dea5ac2","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:08:34.137Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
