{"parentUuid":"ffb1790b-c051-4d11-b4a0-583c6782a885","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaqyXXRDH6ShAeTerpuZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QTKcC8C621eKbH5poCA5Pn","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Blind rulings, case packet 01","subagent_type":"general-purpose","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You are an independent judge for a newspaper-archive gold set (\"Paper Ghosts\"). Two labellers labelled each of your cases differently under a written policy. Decide each case yourself from the policy and the article text. You don't know who made either label, and neither is presumed right.\n\nPaths (N = 01):\n- Repo root: /Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\n- Policy: <repo>/eval/gold/POLICY.md (version 3). Read all of it first.\n- Your cases: /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/p3/cases01.txt. Each case starts \"##### cNN  disputed: ...\" naming what the two labels disagree on: \"kind\", or report fields such as place, seen, people. Then come the article (a \"crops:\" line of local scan images, the headline and the OCR text), and the two labels as \"--- A:\" and \"--- B:\" JSON.\n- Your texts file, for the check: .../scratchpad/p3/texts01.json\n- Your output: .../scratchpad/p3/out/r01.jsonl\n\nFor each case, write one JSON line:\n{\"case\": \"cNN\", \"kind\": \"<your kind, if kind is disputed>\", \"kind_quote\": \"<span showing it>\", \"fields\": {\"<each disputed field>\": {\"value\": \"...\", \"quote\": \"...\"} or null; for \"people\", a list of {\"value\",\"quote\"}}, \"choice\": {\"kind\": \"A\"|\"B\"|\"neither\", \"<field>\": \"A\"|\"B\"|\"neither\"}, \"reason\": \"<one sentence citing the policy rule>\", \"rule10\": null}\n- Rule on everything listed as disputed. If kind is disputed and you rule \"report\", also give the report's fields as the policy asks. Each value needs an exact quote from the headline or OCR text, OCR errors and all. Line breaks may be written as single spaces. A value the text doesn't state is null.\n- choice says whose label your ruling matches, or \"neither\". You may agree with either label or with neither.\n- Read the crop images where the OCR is unclear.\n- **rule10:** for each case where A and B disagree between \"other\" and \"idiom\", set it to {\"without_v3_bullet\": \"idiom\"|\"other\", \"bullet_right\": true|false, \"why\": \"...\"}. \"without_v3_bullet\" is how you would rule if rule 10's last bullet were absent: the one saying spirit, spirits or medium in an ordinary sense is `other`, added in version 3. \"bullet_right\" is whether you think that bullet is right. Otherwise leave rule10 null.\n\nCheck: from the repo root run\n  uv run python scripts/blind_rulings.py check /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/p3/out/r01.jsonl /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/p3/texts01.json\nFix what it names until it prints \"every ruling checks\".\n\nRules:\n- Open only POLICY.md, your cases file, the crop images it lists, your texts file, and your output.\n- Don't open, list or search anything else in the repo or the scratchpad. That means no eval/gold label files, adjudication.jsonl, second_pass.jsonl, split.json, eval/results, Docs, git history, other packets or outputs, and no p3key folder.\n- No network. Never read or print the repo's .env. The check command is the only script you run.\n\nFinal reply, under 100 words: the output path, how many cases, and counts of choice A, B and neither for kind and for fields."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_in