equestRef":"8c29a672-4f69-4cf1-8735-b8da8b03fdd1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8989d7ae-939a-4047-8786-4fbf2ed3314b","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:12:57.211Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"8989d7ae-939a-4047-8786-4fbf2ed3314b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bc78905f-f97a-4964-afea-9b791531d532","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EDMS8NgUbMZ3AgZdBqqMCT","type":"tool_result","content":"ARCHITECTURE.md\nBRIEF.md\nBUDGET.md\nBUILD-PLAN.md\nDECISIONS.md\nIDEAS.md\nPRD.md\nRESUME.md\nSRS.md\nUI-IDEAS.md\nls: BUDGET.md: No such file or directory\nDocs/BUDGET.md\n\"\"\"The storage budget's measurements (decision 32, rule 8): full `reports` documents, with their\nreal text, their reprint clusters' printings, a BinData embedding, and reader fields whose quotes\nare real sentences of the article. They are built for a seeded 1,000 of lexicon v2's candidates,\nand for the judged reports that v2 makes candidates.\n\n1. Offline, with bson.encode: the bytes of each document by part, with each of rule 6's levers\n   turned off, and with each further lever on: bbox_list packed as BinData, paper, place and\n   state in a title lookup by LCCN, display_headline derived at read time, and an int8 embedding.\n2. Atlas's own data and index sizes, for the 1,000 loaded 500 at a time into a scratch\n   collection with the reports validator and indexes. The collection is dropped afterwards.\n3. Each database's use of M0's storage: data size plus index size, as Atlas counts it.\n4. How many stories fit at the top of decisions 30 and 31's intervals.\n\nWrites eval/results/phase2b/budget.json, which Docs/BUDGET.md reads.\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport random\nimport re\nimport statistics\nimport time\nimport uuid\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom concurrent.futures import ProcessPoolExecutor\nfrom datetime import UTC, datetime\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport bson\nimport numpy as np\nimport zstandard\nfrom bson.binary import Binary, BinaryVectorDtype\nfrom pymongo import MongoClient\n\nfrom paperghosts.cluster.reprints import clusters, keys\nfrom paperghosts.config import setting\nfrom paperghosts.ingest.crops import MEMBER, crop_urls\nfrom paperghosts.ingest.headline import display_headline\nfrom paperghosts.schemas import DIMENSIONS, Report\nfrom paperghosts.store.db_init import INDEXES\nfrom paperghosts.store.printings import printing\nfrom paperghosts.store.validators import validator\n(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*.py\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:127:   - Eval B also has the reader screen the random reservoirs, for a recall bound that doesn't rest on flag words (decision 30). The Tinker credit check sets how many it reads.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:136:   - Lexicon v2 makes the reader's job 1,236,122 candidates, 17.7% more than v1's (decision 31). The Tinker credit check weighs that before the pass starts.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:138:   - If the credit check finds that every candidate doesn't fit, stop. Bring the EM the shortfall, and the skip rule's loss, measured on a seeded draw of skipped members read beside their first printings.\nDocs/RESUME.md:54:  - v2 has 974,399 distinct stories. Decision 36's skip rule would have made the reader's job 1,002,205 printings, but the EM's call keeps the reader on every triaged candidate.\nDocs/RESUME.md:82:- **The reader reads every triaged candidate, 1,236,122** (the EM's call on decision 36). Stories stay the unit for display and counts. The Tinker credit check weighs the job before 2C's full pass, and a shortfall goes to the EM and the owner.\nDocs/RESUME.md:140:- The reader's job is 1,236,122 candidates, 17.7% more than v1's. The Tinker credit check weighs that before the full pass.\nDocs/RESUME.md:168:- Tinker credits. Only the console shows the balance.\nDocs/DECISIONS.md:358:- Cost: no money, only machine time and 340.4 GB of downloads. The reader's job grows from 1,050,459 candidates to 1,236,122 (+17.7%). The Tinker credit check weighs that before the full pass.\nDocs/DECISIONS.md:792:    - The skip rule would leave 233,917 printings unread, and 38,127 of them run past the 600 words the shingles see.\nDocs/DECISIONS.md:796:    - If 2C's Tinker credit check finds that every candidate doesn't fit, the step stops. The EM gets the shortfall, and the skip rule's loss measured on a seeded draw of skipped members read beside their first printings. That trade-off is the owner's.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"59dd3dd3-7c50-4c50-a5ac-4a204c4a13e2","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:12:58.670Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"ARCHITECTURE.md\nBRIEF.md\nBUDGET.md\nBUILD-PLAN.md\nDECISIONS.md\nIDEAS.md\nPRD.md\nRESUME.md\nSRS.md\nUI-IDEAS.md\nls: BUDGET.md: No such file or directory\nDocs/BUDGET.md\n\"\"\"The storage budget's measurements (decision 32, rule 8): full `reports` documents, with their\nreal text, their reprint clusters' printings, a BinData embedding, and reader fields whose quotes\nare real sentences of the article. They are built for a seeded 1,000 of lexicon v2's candidates,\nand for the judged reports that v2 makes candidates.\n\n1. Offline, with bson.encode: the bytes of each document by part, with each of rule 6's levers\n   turned off, and with each further lever on: bbox_list packed as BinData, paper, place and\n   state in a title lookup by LCCN, display_headline derived at read time, and an int8 embedding.\n2. Atlas's own data and index sizes, for the 1,000 loaded 500 at a time into a scratch\n   collection with the reports validator and indexes. The collection is dropped afterwards.\n3. Each database's use of M0's storage: data size plus index size, as Atlas counts it.\n4. How many stories fit at the top of decisions 30 and 31's intervals.\n\nWrites eval/results/phase2b/budget.json, which Docs/BUDGET.md reads.\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport random\nimport re\nimport statistics\nimport time\nimport uuid\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom concurrent.futures import ProcessPoolExecutor\nfrom datetime import UTC, datetime\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport bson\nimport numpy as np\nimport zstandard\nfrom bson.binary import Binary, BinaryVectorDtype\nfrom pymongo import MongoClient\n\nfrom paperghosts.cluster.reprints import clusters, keys\nfrom paperghosts.config import setting\nfrom paperghosts.ingest.crops import MEMBER, crop_urls\nfrom paperghosts.ingest.headline import display_headline\nfrom paperghosts.schemas import DIMENSIONS, Report\nfrom paperghosts.store.db_init import INDEXES\nfrom paperghosts.store.printings import printing\nfrom paperghosts.store.validators import validator\n(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*.py\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:127:   - Eval B also has the reader screen the random reservoirs, for a recall bound that doesn't rest on flag words (decision 30). The Tinker credit check sets how many it reads.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:136:   - Lexicon v2 makes the reader's job 1,236,122 candidates, 17.7% more than v1's (decision 31). The Tinker credit check weighs that before the pass starts.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:138:   - If the credit check finds that every candidate doesn't fit, stop. Bring the EM the shortfall, and the skip rule's loss, measured on a seeded draw of skipped members read beside their first printings.\nDocs/RESUME.md:54:  - v2 has 974,399 distinct stories. Decision 36's skip rule would have made the reader's job 1,002,205 printings, but the EM's call keeps the reader on every triaged candidate.\nDocs/RESUME.md:82:- **The reader reads every triaged candidate, 1,236,122** (the EM's call on decision 36). Stories stay the unit for display and counts. The Tinker credit check weighs the job before 2C's full pass, and a shortfall goes to the EM and the owner.\nDocs/RESUME.md:140:- The reader's job is 1,236,122 candidates, 17.7% more than v1's. The Tinker credit check weighs that before the full pass.\nDocs/RESUME.md:168:- Tinker credits. Only the console shows the balance.\nDocs/DECISIONS.md:358:- Cost: no money, only machine time and 340.4 GB of downloads. The reader's job grows from 1,050,459 candidates to 1,236,122 (+17.7%). The Tinker credit check weighs that before the full pass.\nDocs/DECISIONS.md:792:    - The skip rule would leave 233,917 printings unread, and 38,127 of them run past the 600 words the shingles see.\nDocs/DECISIONS.md:796:    - If 2C's Tinker credit check finds that every candidate doesn't fit, the step stops. The EM gets the shortfall, and the skip rule's loss measured on a seeded draw of skipped members read beside their first printings. That trade-off is the owner's.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"3e0bf5ea-3a6a-465e-93b9-79ff172890af","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2c-reader","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8989d7ae-939a-4047-8786-4fbf2ed3314b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
