{"parentUuid":"f2821615-871a-466e-b7ad-843ceeb176c0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bc78905f-f97a-4964-afea-9b791531d532","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017YXsLwisjdyKArNusVZf1n","type":"tool_result","content":"tinker 0.36.0\n.tinker.base_models [{'name': 'Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'trainable': True, 'sampleable': True, 'max_context_length': 32768}, {'name': 'Qwen/Qwen3.5-35B-A3B-Base', 'trainable': True, 'sampleable': True, 'max_context_length': 65536\n.tinker.credits.value None\n.tinker.credits.reason the API reports usage and estimated gross cost, not the remaining balance\n.tinker.lora_weights_download.documented True\n.tinker.lora_weights_download.how save_weights_external, then RestClient.get_external_weights_urls gives a signed URL per file (tinker SDK 0.36.0)\n.tinker.lora_weights_download.verified False\n.tinker.lora_weights_download.verify_in Phase 2C, after the first training run\n24:**5. One main tool (Tinker); the others support it. MongoDB Atlas, not Tiger Data. No .tech domain.**\n25:Week 2's partner winners each made one partner the core of the product and proved it under failure. Our Week 2 entry, Cubby, spread thin uses across seven partners and won nothing. So the depth goes into the Tinker reader, and Atlas, Temporal, Render and Sentry each get one real job.\n60:- Tinker: the route the Tinker CLI's login uses to check a key. A plain HTTP call skips the SDK's 2.5 s import and its session, so the SDK arrives later, with the Tinker facts.\n358:- Cost: no money, only machine time and 340.4 GB of downloads. The reader's job grows from 1,050,459 candidates to 1,236,122 (+17.7%). The Tinker credit check weighs that before the full pass.\n796:    - If 2C's Tinker credit check finds that every candidate doesn't fit, the step stops. The EM gets the shortfall, and the skip rule's loss measured on a seeded draw of skipped members read beside their first printings. That trade-off is the owner's.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"21b