at whose house the meeting was, so only the \n  outcome: mine=hoax <<these rappng humbugs>>\n       judge=explained <<picture Of deusos and nfatuaton>>\n  specific_place: mine=Mrs. Cackley's in Sixth Avenue <<Mrs Clacklsys in Sixth avenue>>\n       judge=-\n  place_type: mine=house <<Mrs Clacklsys in Sixth avenue>>\n       judge=-\n  precision: mine=building <<Mrs Clacklsys in Sixth avenue>>\n       judge=town <<the spiritual circles in New York>>\nc57 18_1871-03-04_pna_sn85040344_00271769593_1871  (irst pass upheld: the barracks are named; Major Hamilton and Capt. Gord)\n   judge: The text breaks off before the ghost, so it never says the incident happened in the barracks or who saw it; the only stated claimant is the friend who narrated it, and values are never inferred.\n  specific_place: mine=the officers' barracks <<In one of these barracks>>\n       judge=-\n  place_type: mine=public_building <<In one of these barracks>>\n       judge=-\n  precision: mine=building <<In one of these barracks>>\n       judge=-\n  people: mine=Major Hamilton <<Major Hamilton>> | Capt. Gordon <<Capt. Gordon>>\n       judge=an old friend and correspondent of the writer, who tells the incident <<an old friend and correspondent of mine>>\nc58 29_1894-09-24_p4_sn94053256_00271762963_18940  (irst pass upheld: the denial names Mrs. Sullivan; 'the occupants' are t)\n   judge: The Globe story claimed the occupants, Mrs. Sullivan, and the writer (the crop reads 'The statement that I remained on watch and heard the noises') as witnesses, so all three are people of the claim l\n  people: mine=Mrs. Florence Sullivan <<Mrs Florence Sullivan>>\n       judge=the occupants of the house <<the occupants of my house>> | Mrs. Florence Sullivan <<Mrs Florence Sullivan>> | Daniel O'Connor, said by the s\nc60 8_1883-04-21_p1_sn86076999_00415627385_188304  (irst pass upheld: the same letter from the spirit world)\n   judge: seen is what was received as the text says it, the communication from the dead father, and B's span states it with the father named.\n  seen: mine=a letter from the spirit world, from his dead father <<a letter from the spirit world>>\n       judge=a communication from his deceased father <<received this communi. cation from his deceased father>>\nc62 6_1876-05-14_p1_sn88064616_00295878605_187605  (irst pass upheld: the monkey's ghost haunting the house is what the tex)\n   judge: seen holds what was experienced as the text says it, the vanishing food and annoyances, not the haunting itself, which is the claim.\n  seen: mine=a dead monkey's ghost haunting the house: food vanishing, annoyances, a fire <<the monkeys ghost began to haunt the house>>\n       judge=food placed on the tables mysteriously disappeared, and strange annoyances <<Food placed on the tables mysteriously Disappeared, and strange\nc64 5_1913-06-21_p1_sn85066387_00280768601_191306  (irst pass upheld: the constable suggested the plumbing but found nothin)\n   judge: The noises are the recurring phenomenon the household and watchers heard; the constable's search found nothing and the plumbing is only a guess still to be checked, so no cause is given and the outcom\n  seen: mine=a shadowy white form of Charles H. Firebaugh, who died in the house; clanking chains and groans <<a shadowy white form>>\n       judge=weird echoes of clanking chains, mysterious moans and ghostly groans <<weird echoes Of clanking chains. mysterious means and ghostIy groans>\nc65 71_1893-09-12_pna_sn86092518_00414186749_1893  (irst pass upheld: a review of the bill; the medium is a dime-museum act)\n   judge: An amusements column of theatre notices and puffs, with reserved seats on sale and the medium as a stage attraction, is advert under rules 7 and 12.\n  KIND mine=other judge=advert | An amusements column of theatre notices and puffs, with reserved seats on sale and the medium as a stage attraction, is advert under rules 7 and 12.\nc66 9_1919-07-09_p1_sn89081128_0028076677A_191907  (irst pass upheld: he was touring the battlefields when he saw it)\n   judge: The town is left blank in the text and crop, and the experience's place is not named, so place stays empty.\n  place: mine=touring the Franco-German war's battlefields <<left England to visit the battlefelds>>\n       judge=-\nc68 6_1921-12-31_pna_sn82014519_00414218945_19211  (irst pass upheld: the figure leapt from the old barn by the road)\n   judge: The chase happened on the road, which the text names as where the incident happened; the barn only borders it.\n  specific_place: mine=an old barn by the road <<an old barn>>\n       judge=a lonely road just off the turnpike <<a lonely road just off the turnpike>>\nc69 20_1879-04-11_pna_sn83032041_00212477710_1879  (irst pass upheld: the account's sighting is the apparition the young me)\n   judge: seen is what was seen and heard as the text says it, and the lights and sounds are the phenomenon behind the haunting the whole account turns on.\n  seen: mine=a bright circular light, and apparitions of a hanged man and a murdered girl <<bright. circular light became visible>>\n       judge=strange lights and stranger sounds <<saw strange lights and heard stranger sounds>>\ncases differing: 30","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ee3a6372-ac8e-4ca4-b8ae-09dbff08b731","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2c-reader","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote