{"parentUuid":"daf4f630-55e1-43fe-97c0-3acfa51a8ee3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bc78905f-f97a-4964-afea-9b791531d532","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KDz7nsqRyXzoidPvyfiwXg","type":"tool_result","content":"- **The rulings** (`eval/gold/adjudication.jsonl`): 69 articles disagreed, 61 of them in gold. 34 were on kind, and 35 on fields alone.\n  - Each ruling went through `checked()` and replaced its article's label. The record keeps the first pass's label, the second's, the ruling and its reason.\n  - 58 uphold the first pass, 6 take the second's call, and 5 mend fields.\n  - **16 of the 34 kind disagreements were one question:** spirit or medium in an ordinary sense, \"in good spirits\" or \"an advertising medium\". The first pass called these `other`, the second `idiom`. The ruling is `other`, since `POLICY.md`'s idioms are figures about ghosts.\n  - **The second pass's call was taken six times:**\n    - Basingstoke's haunted clock, a report told with a closing quip (rule 8), which makes gold's 46th report\n    - a spiritualist society's display notice, an advert\n    - a puff for the paper's own Sunday story, an advert\n    - a camp meeting's \"séance behind the woodshed\", a figure for a whipping\n    - spiritualists on cremation in a Catholic note, `other`\n    - a stated house as a place type\n  - **Fields were emptied where a value wasn't stated:** \"claimed to be haunted\" states nothing seen, and a clerk's workplace isn't where his sittings were.\n  - **`POLICY.md` version 3,** dated, adds the two clarifications the rulings settled, which every label already follows. Spirit or medium in an ordinary sense is `other` (rule 10), and a display notice of meetings and messages is an advert (rule 12).\n- **The freeze** (`1e64421`):\n  - `eval/gold/HASH` lists the sha256 of `labels.jsonl` and `dev_labels.jsonl` beside `split.json`'s, committed before any model output.\n  - The two files hold exactly 300 and 150 labels, one per article. Each is the first pass's label where the passes agreed, and the ruling where they didn't. All pass `checked()` (`second_pass.py frozen`).\n  - `check_leakage.py` now checks every file `HASH` lists.\n  - Gold's final kinds: 46 reports, 89 other, 66 fiction, 60 idiom, 30 adverts, 9 religious. Dev's: 32 reports, 44 other, 31 fiction, 26 idiom, 10 adverts, 7 religious.\n- **Gold's reports by stratum** (`eval/results/phase2c/gold_measures.json`), against the draw's expectation:","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"513bdde0-b591-4900-a4d5-dbf220ea44ca","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:17:15.641Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"- **The rulings** (`eval/gold/adjudication.jsonl`): 69 articles disagreed, 61 of them in gold. 34 were on kind, and 35 on fields alone.\n  - Each ruling went through `checked()` and replaced its article's label. The record keeps the first pass's label, the second's, the ruling and its reason.\n  - 58 uphold the first pass, 6 take the second's call, and 5 mend fields.\n  - **16 of the 34 kind disagreements were one question:** spirit or medium in an ordinary sense, \"in good spirits\" or \"an advertising medium\". The first pass called these `other`, the second `idiom`. The ruling is `other`, since `POLICY.md`'s idioms are figures about ghosts.\n  - **The second pass's call was taken six times:**\n    - Basingstoke's haunted clock, a report told with a closing quip (rule 8), which makes gold's 46th report\n    - a spiritualist society's display notice, an advert\n    - a puff for the paper's own Sunday story, an advert\n    - a camp meeting's \"séance behind the woodshed\", a figure for a whipping\n    - spiritualists on cremation in a Catholic note, `other`\n    - a stated house as a place type\n  - **Fields were emptied where a value wasn't stated:** \"claimed to be haunted\" states nothing seen, and a clerk's workplace isn't where his sittings were.\n  - **`POLICY.md` version 3,** dated, adds the two clarifications the rulings settled, which every label already follows. Spirit or medium in an ordinary sense is `other` (rule 10), and a display notice of meetings and messages is an advert (rule 12).\n- **The freeze** (`1e64421`):\n  - `eval/gold/HASH` lists the sha256 of `labels.jsonl` and `dev_labels.jsonl` beside `split.json`'s, committed before any model output.\n  - The two files hold exactly 300 and 150 labels, one per article. Each is the first pass's label where the passes agreed, and the ruling where they didn't. All pass `checked()` (`second_pass.py frozen`).\n  - `check_leakage.py` now checks every file `HASH` lists.\n  - Gold's final kinds: 46 reports, 89 other, 66 fiction, 60 idiom, 30 adverts, 9 religious. Dev's: 32 reports, 44 other, 31 fiction, 26 idiom, 10 adverts, 7 religious.\n- **Gold's reports by stratum** (`eval/results/phase2c/gold_measures.json`), against the draw's expectation:","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"76b750ab-45b2-4392-8d49-92e8d5f2fd5c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2c-reader","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":6,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"daf4f630-55e1-43fe-97c0-3acfa51a8ee3","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external",