{"parentUuid":"8a97b49e-6798-490f-a46b-6a8b2a5895a9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bc78905f-f97a-4964-afea-9b791531d532","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TdGocfxk5s2fQPKUap6xEk","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# Storage budget: Atlas M0\n5:## What Atlas counts against the cap\n16:## Free space now\n28:## Bytes per story\n60:## The levers\n82:## How many stories fit with full text\n121:## Options for the owner\n     128 Docs/BUDGET.md\n# Storage budget: Atlas M0\n\nMeasured on 2026-10-30 by `scripts/budget_probe.py`, which writes `eval/results/phase2b/budget.json`. Every number here comes from that file or follows from it by arithmetic. The documents are the final 2B.1 models (decision 33). Atlas M0 is the free\n\n## What Atlas counts against the cap\n\n- **The cap:** M0's storage is 0.5 GB, a hard limit. The cluster comparison writes it as \"Storage (Data Size + Index Size) 512 MB\". That is the documents' uncompressed BSON plus their B-tree indexes ([Free Cluster Limits](https://www.mongodb.com/docs\n- **How it's measured:** \"Atlas calculates allocated storage using metrics returned by the dbStats command\" ([FAQ: Storage](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/reference/faq/storage/)).\n- **Search indexes:**\n  - Atlas Search and Vector Search indexes aren't in `dbStats`.\n  - Free clusters have no Search index size metrics ([Review Search Metrics](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/review-atlas-search-metrics/)).\n  - So by the docs, Search indexes don't count against the cap. No page says so outright, though, and M0 can't measure them, so the budget leaves them out and keeps some headroom.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"48ba359e-e016-4a20-b9fd-aea104904e3f","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:23:43.888Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"1:# Storage budget: Atlas M0\n5:## What Atlas counts against the cap\n16:## Free space now\n28:## Bytes per story\n60:## The levers\n82:## How many stories fit with full text\n121:## Options for the owner\n     128 Docs/BUDGET.md\n# Storage budget: Atlas M0\n\nMeasured on 2026-10-30 by `scripts/budget_probe.py`, which writes `eval/results/phase2b/budget.json`. Every number here comes from that file or follows from it by arithmetic. The documents are the final 2B.1 models (decision 33). Atlas M0 is the free\n\n## What Atlas counts against the cap\n\n- **The cap:** M0's storage is 0.5 GB, a hard limit. The cluster comparison writes it as \"Storage (Data Size + Index Size) 512 MB\". That is the documents' uncompressed BSON plus their B-tree indexes ([Free Cluster Limits](https://www.mongodb.com/docs\n- **How it's measured:** \"Atlas calculates allocated storage using metrics returned by the dbStats command\" ([FAQ: Storage](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/reference/faq/storage/)).\n- **Search indexes:**\n  - Atlas Search and Vector Search indexes aren't in `dbStats`.\n  - Free clusters have no Search index size metrics ([Review Search Metrics](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/review-atlas-search-metrics/)).\n  - So by the docs, Search indexes don't count against the cap. No page says so outright, though, and M0 can't measure them, so the budget leaves them out and keeps some headroom.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"2467874e-36b2-4094-837a-ff4a67912869","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2c-reader","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":3},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotra