{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","id":"795be91e-beee-478c-8412-251baeb8ac61","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:30:20.536Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"7b35af0d1ba22d1b1b7d4c91038d50b583ea5d544dd1607adac5368903cb8a35","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"e8218869-a3ef-47d4-a64d-2fd6c3f379cc","keep":520,"tail":["d55a16d588cbf0236a6098c945a6ee1d266857cea775cf6d334b95a46b5cc561","79a4d1d08ec77f5272ad1a965c05a70008fc5978bde624a918303c250481f170"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",521,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"8846c90e4d0f3fd05b1c8b0dd994c20277a48d2594128092f133cfd017c72bd0"}
{"parentUuid":"61ef697a-937b-47f4-8d3b-8d401232404f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgasPsmMc34wk9RHDmTMw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019BCruESQnjeK4ggTqGozF2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && cat >> Docs/BUDGET.md <<'EOF'\n\n# Tinker credit budget (2C.3)\n\nMeasured on 2026-10-31 by `scripts/credit_check.py`, which writes `eval/results/phase2c/credit_check.json`, and by the teacher's two dev rounds (`eval/results/phase2c/teacher_dev_r1.json` and `_r2.json`). Rates come from Tinker's billing records for this account. Every other number follows by arithmetic.\n\n## What Tinker reports\n\n- **No balance.** The API reports usage and an estimated cost per hourly bucket (`AdminClient.get_billing_usage`), but not the credit left, which only the console shows. **The owner has to read the balance there.**\n- **Spent before 2C.3:** $5.89 over the last 52 days, mostly 4B training ($3.92) and 397B sampling ($1.23).\n- **Rates per million tokens:**\n\n  | Model | Prompt (cached, uncached) | Generated | Training |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | Qwen3.5-397B-A17B, the teacher | $0.60, $3.00 | $7.50 | — |\n  | Qwen3.5-4B, the student | $0.066, $0.33 | $1.005 | $0.737 |\n\n- Billing lags the requests by more than an hour, so the 50-article run's own cost isn't billed yet. Its cost here is its tokens times these rates.\n\n## Per article, measured\n\n- **The sample:** a seeded 50 of the 1,229,780 candidates in the pool.\n- **The teacher** reads the instructions and `POLICY.md` in full, then the article. On dev's 150 articles that's 9,392 prompt and 105 generated tokens an article. **Cost:** $0.0290 uncached, or about $0.0076 if Tinker caches the policy prefix the articles share.\n- **4B reading,** with the instructions alone and no policy: 948 prompt and 67 generated tokens an article. **Cost:** $0.00038, or about $0.00026 cached.\n- 50 articles took 13 s on the teacher and 9 s on 4B, at 16 requests at once.\n\n## The projection\n\n| Job | Size | Cost (cached to uncached) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Teacher on dev, per prompt round | 150 articles | $1.1–4.4 |\n| Teacher on the training draw | 3,000 articles | $23–87 |\n| LoRA training | 3,000 examples × 1,050 tokens × 18 epochs (6 iterations of 3) | $42 |\n| Dev scoring, per iteration | 150 articles | under $0.10 |\n| Eval B, ablations and the pooled screen | about 3,000 gold reads + 38,900 random-reservoir articles | $11–16 |\n| **The full pass** | **1,236,122 candidates** | **$323–470** |\n| **All of it** | | **about $400–620** |\n\n- A draw of 6,000 would add $23–87 more teacher time and $42 more training.\n- **Whether the full pass fits** turns on the balance. At $323–470 it is three quarters of the total.\n- **If it doesn't fit,** the plan's fallback is decision 36's skip rule: read only each story's first printing, about 1,002,205 articles, saving about 19%. Its loss has to be measured on a seeded draw of skipped printings read beside their first ones, which is itself a small spend. I haven't measured it, since that is only needed if the pass doesn't fit.\nEOF\ngit add Docs/BUDGET.md scripts/credit_check.py scripts/teacher.py scripts/training_draw.py scripts/check_leakage.py tests/test_teacher.py tests/test_training_draw.py eval/results/phase2c/credit_check.json eval/results/phase2c/teacher_dev_r1.json eval/results/phase2c/teacher_dev_r2.json && make test 2>&1 | tail -1 && make lint >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo lint-ok","description":"Write the Tinker credit section of BUDGET.md, then test and lint","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1336,"cache_read_input_tokens":824169,"output_tokens":1498,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1336,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1498,"cache_read_input_tokens":824169,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1336,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1336},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019BCruESQnjeK4ggTqGozF2":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && cat >> Docs/BUDGET.md <<'EOF'\n\n# Tinker credit budget (2C.3)\n\nMeasured on 2026-10-31 by `scripts/credit_check.py`, which writes `eval/results/phase2c/credit_check.json`, and by the teacher's two dev rounds (`eval/results/phase2c/teacher_dev_r1.json` and `_r2.json`). Rates come from Tinker's billing records for this account. Every other number follows by arithmetic.\n\n## What Tinker reports\n\n- **No balance.** The API reports usage and an estimated cost per hourly bucket (`AdminClient.get_billing_usage`), but not the credit left, which only the console shows. **The owner has to read the balance there.**\n- **Spent before 2C.3:** $5.89 over the last 52 days, mostly 4B training ($3.92) and 397B sampling ($1.23).\n- **Rates per million tokens:**\n\n  | Model | Prompt (cached, uncached) | Generated | Training |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | Qwen3.5-397B-A17B, the teacher | $0.60, $3.00 | $7.50 | — |\n  | Qwen3.5-4B, the student | $0.066, $0.33 | $1.005 | $0.737 |\n\n- Billing lags the requests by more than an hour, so the 50-article run's own cost isn't billed yet. Its cost here is its tokens times these rates.\n\n## Per article, measured\n\n- **The sample:** a seeded 50 of the 1,229,780 candidates in the pool.\n- **The teacher** reads the instructions and `POLICY.md` in full, then the article. On dev's 150 articles that's 9,392 prompt and 105 generated tokens an article. **Cost:** $0.0290 uncached, or about $0.0076 if Tinker caches the policy prefix the articles share.\n- **4B reading,** with the instructions alone and no policy: 948 prompt and 67 generated tokens an article. **Cost:** $0.00038, or about $0.00026 cached.\n- 50 articles took 13 s on the teacher and 9 s on 4B, at 16 requests at once.\n\n## The projection\n\n| Job | Size | Cost (cached to uncached) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Teacher on dev, per prompt round | 150 articles | $1.1–4.4 |\n| Teacher on the training draw | 3,000 articles | $23–87 |\n| LoRA training | 3,000 examples × 1,050 tokens × 18 epochs (6 iterations of 3) | $42 |\n| Dev scoring, per iteration | 150 articles | under $0.10 |\n| Eval B, ablations and the pooled screen | about 3,000 gold reads + 38,900 random-reservoir articles | $11–16 |\n| **The full pass** | **1,236,122 candidates** | **$323–470** |\n| **All of it** | | **about $400–620** |\n\n- A draw of 6,000 would add $23–87 more teacher time and $42 more training.\n- **Whether the full pass fits** turns on the balance. At $323–470 it is three quarters of the total.\n- **If it doesn't fit,** the plan's fallback is decision 36's skip rule: read only each story's first printing, about 1,002,205 articles, saving about 19%. Its loss has to be measured on a seeded draw of skipped printings read beside their first ones, which is itself a small spend. I haven't measured it, since that is only needed if the pass doesn't fit.\nEOF\ngit add Docs/BUDGET.md scripts/credit_check.py scripts/teacher.py scripts/training_draw.py scripts/check_leakage.py tests/test_teacher.py tests/test_training_draw.py eval/results/phase2c/credit_check.json eval/results/phase2c/teacher_dev_r1.json eval/results/phase2c/teacher_dev_r2.json && make test 2>&1 | tail -1 && make lint >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo lint-ok","description":"Write the Tinker credit section of BUDGET.md, then test and lint","timeout":600000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c5651dce-ac27-4ddd-ae57-1b6a90b37b7e",