{"parentUuid":"b3784013-9a36-4f66-8174-2fd06d34fd8d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"99a9efcd-226c-4aca-a2b3-32bc2d8dcd3e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017Z7S6gZr6CLw3Jzb4YrFWL","type":"tool_result","content":"Docs/SRS.md:39:| RDR-9 | The quote verifier's threshold is calibrated on the gold set. A field whose quote doesn't verify becomes \"not stated\". | Calibration curve, plus unit tests |\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:47:- CI on GitHub Actions: `ruff`, offline `pytest`, a web typecheck and build, and a secret scan.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:134:9. The local export and the offline proof.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:144:- The offline proof passes, and the full-pass counts are recorded.\nDocs/SRS.md:40:| RDR-10 | The tuned student runs locally with no network, on at least 200 articles, and its agreement with the Tinker-served outputs is reported. A guard in the runner blocks sockets, so system network settings are never touched. | `scripts/offline_proof.py` output |\nDocs/SRS.md:47:| GEO-1 | The publication place is parsed from the LCCN title and geocoded offline against GeoNames `cities1000`. A manifest records the source, retrieval date and licence. | Parser tests on at least 200 distinct titles, plus the manifest |\nDocs/SRS.md:103:| WALK-3 | The assignment sheet prints cleanly and works offline. | A print-to-PDF snapshot |\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:9:- **The pipeline (offline, on the owner's Mac, durable on Temporal).** It reads the 340 GB archive, trains and runs the reader, geocodes, loads Atlas, gathers follow-ups and runs the investigator. All AI work happens here. None of it runs when someone visits the site.\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:64:| Reader | Classify each candidate and extract fields, each with a verbatim quote | Qwen 4B student with a LoRA trained on Tinker from teacher labels | Full pass on Tinker sampling; also runs locally offline |\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:66:| Geocoder | Publication place from the LCCN title; article places from the reader | GeoNames `cities1000`, offline, with a manifest | Pipeline |\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:269:scripts/                 one-off checks: keys, crop check, offline proof, numbers sheet\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:279:- **CI (GitHub Actions):** lint, offline tests, a web typecheck and build, and a secret scan, on every push and pull request. CI needs no secrets; tests that need the network are marked and skipped there.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a4a7feb4-5f5a-4638-9d2c-09a7fbabe14c","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:32:46.657Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Docs/SRS.md:39:| RDR-9 | The quote verifier's threshold is calibrated on the gold set. A field whose quote doesn't verify becomes \"not stated\". | Calibration curve, plus unit tests |\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:47:- CI on GitHub Actions: `ruff`, offline `pytest`, a web typecheck and build, and a secret scan.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:134:9. The local export and the offline proof.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:144:- The offline proof passes, and the full-pass counts are recorded.\nDocs/SRS.md:40:| RDR-10 | The tuned student runs locally with no network, on at least 200 articles, and its agreement with the Tinker-served outputs is reported. A guard in the runner blocks sockets, so system network settings are never touched. | `scripts/offline_proof.py` output |\nDocs/SRS.md:47:| GEO-1 | The publication place is parsed from the LCCN title and geocoded offline against GeoNames `cities1000`. A manifest records the source, retrieval date and licence. | Parser tests on at least 200 distinct titles, plus the manifest |\nDocs/SRS.md:103:| WALK-3 | The assignment sheet prints cleanly and works offline. | A print-to-PDF snapshot |\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:9:- **The pipeline (offline, on the owner's Mac, durable on Temporal).** It reads the 340 GB archive, trains and runs the reader, geocodes, loads Atlas, gathers follow-ups and runs the investigator. All AI work happens here. None of it runs when someone visits the site.\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:64:| Reader | Classify ea