{"parentUuid":"62565b00-0790-4bb0-a7d5-5b326af743ee","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"99a9efcd-226c-4aca-a2b3-32bc2d8dcd3e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KHWbRHNxrc4JZ5xYEFyRef","type":"tool_result","content":"9. The local export and the offline proof.\n10. The full pass over all triaged candidates.\n   - Lexicon v2 makes the reader's job 1,236,122 candidates, 17.7% more than v1's (decision 31). The Tinker credit check weighs that before the pass starts.\n   - **Every triaged candidate is read** (the EM's call, decision 36). A member that reads differently from its story's first printing becomes a report of its own, shown as printed inside its story. It counts as different if it's a report where the first printing isn't one, or if it gives another place, date or person.\n   - If the credit check finds that every candidate doesn't fit, stop. Bring the EM the shortfall, and the skip rule's loss, measured on a seeded draw of skipped members read beside their first printings.\n\n**Gate**\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:42:    EXP[\"Static export, at build time\"] --> WEB[\"React static site\"]\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:72:| Static export | Prebuilt JSON for the front page, the town index, each town, each case and the archive chart | Python script reading Atlas | At deploy time |\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:159:### 3.6 Static export and the site\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:160:- `export_static` reads Atlas and writes:\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:260:  store/                 Atlas loader, indexes, validators, static export\nDocs/DECISIONS.md:371:  2. The pipeline is partitioned by year. The year is the Temporal activity, the unit of retry and the cache key. The static export is partitioned by state and then town, with one more file per calendar day for \"Printed on this night\".\n/Users/hotragn/.homebrew/bin/ollama\nNAME                     ID              SIZE      MODIFIED   \ngemma4:26b-a4b-it-qat    2dd70431afed    15 GB     5 days ago    \ngemma4:e4b-it-qa