{"parentUuid":"529a0a42-e3b4-404a-819c-346f06fb6fe7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"99a9efcd-226c-4aca-a2b3-32bc2d8dcd3e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UWJhHrkxM5JKm4VNbdqteJ","type":"tool_result","content":"5 passed in 1.70s","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"1728147a-b942-4869-b1c8-98dfc42c9bd9","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:36:01.543Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"5 passed in 1.70s","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/scripts/teacher.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":47,"oldLines":8,"newStart":47,"newLines":20,"lines":[" - A value the text doesn't state is null. Never infer one."," - outcome is one of explained, hoax, unexplained, unknown. place_type is one of house, church, cemetery, inn_or_hotel, road_or_bridge, public_building, ship, other. precision is one of town, street, building."," ","+How to apply the policy, in its own terms:","+- The kind follows how the article uses its ghost word. If the only ghost, spirit, haunt or spectre in it is a figure of speech, the kind is idiom, whatever the article is about: politics, sport, a profile. other is for names and titles, social events, OCR accidents, ordinary senses of spirit or medium, and essays about ghosts in general.","+- A joke, quip, squib, poem, story, serial or comic sketch is fiction, whatever its subject, even a short one in a column of paragraphs.","+- One particular claim makes a report: a named person, a place or an occasion with a ghost, spirit or manifestation told as having happened. It counts inside an essay, a round-up, a column or an article cut off in the archive. Take the fields from the first claim told in particulars.","+- seen is what was seen, heard or felt: the apparition, the noises or the message, not the house or the occasion.","+- people are those who saw, heard, felt or claimed it, and at a seance the medium and the sitters the text names. Leave out anyone who only reports it, investigates it, is told of it afterwards, or plays the ghost.","+"," THE POLICY"," \"\"\"","+# Round 3's lines above restate POLICY.md; each was prompted by dev's round 2 confusions, never","+# by one article. The kind line: 14 dev idioms called other, among them a political \"Ghost of","+# Major Andre\" and \"CHOLERA SPECTRE\". The fiction line: 7 fictions called other, quips and","+# sketches. The report line: 7 reports called other, claims inside essays and round-ups (rules 6,","+# 16, 17). The seen and people lines: seen right on 7 of 24 reports, people on 6."," "," "," def system_prompt(policy: str | None = None) -> str:"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/scripts/teacher.py"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ccef8b51-4b55-448b-9316-ed7a4d312c1d","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2c-reader","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":3,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"529a0a42-e3b4-404a-819c-346f06fb6fe7","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","session