{"parentUuid":"c064bbb0-5440-4e95-8c94-2707ab9a3529","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgatA86o1z8ufkizwajLY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KvD6jaYU52wrfbRUJjCH4B","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad; cat > $S/local_section.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nd = json.load(open(\"eval/results/phase2c/local_throughput.json\"))\nrows = \"\\n\".join(\n    f\"  | {r['concurrent']} | {r['wall_seconds']:.0f} s | {r['articles_per_hour']:,} | {r['output_tokens'] / d['articles']:.0f} | {r['full_pass_days']} |\"\n    for r in d[\"runs\"])\nbest = max(d[\"runs\"], key=lambda r: r[\"articles_per_hour\"])\nprint(f\"\"\"\n## The free path: the full pass on this Mac\n\nMeasured by `scripts/local_throughput.py` (`eval/results/phase2c/local_throughput.json`). Base Qwen3.5-4B runs in the local Ollama server, which serves it on its MLX runner with nvfp4 weights. It reads the credit check's seeded 50 candidates, with the same 948-token instructions and ChatML as on Tinker.\n\n  | Requests at once | 50 articles took | Articles an hour | Tokens generated an article | Days for 1,236,122 |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|\n{rows}\n\n- **At the best setting,** {best['concurrent']} at once, the full pass takes about **{best['full_pass_days']} days of machine time and no credits.**\n- So the LoRA can be trained on Tinker and the pass run here, with the adapter loaded in Ollama: the plan's step 9 export.\n- **Not measured yet:** whether the nvfp4 weights read as Tinker's do. Step 9 measures that on dev before the pass, as RDR-10 requires.\n- The base model's answers are longer than a trained adapter's will be, since it hasn't learned the format. Generation dominates the time, so this is an upper bound.\n\"\"\")\nPY\necho ok","description":"Write a helper that fills BUDGET.md's local-path section from the result"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":628,"cache_read_input_tokens":863770,"output_tokens":1372,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":593},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":628,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1372,"cache_read_input_tokens":863770,"cache_creation_input_tokens":628,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":628},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KvD6jaYU52wrfbRUJjCH4B":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad; cat > $S/local_section.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nd = json.load(open(\"eval/results/phase2c/local_throughput.json\"))\nrows = \"\\n\".join(\n    f\"  | {r['concurrent']} | {r['wall_seconds']:.0f} s | {r['articles_per_hour']:,} | {r['output_tokens'] / d['articles']:.0f} | {r['full_pass_days']} |\"\n    for r in d[\"runs\"])\nbest = max(d[\"runs\"], key=lambda r: r[\"articles_per_hour\"])\nprint(f\"\"\"\n## The free path: the full pass on this Mac\n\nMeasured by `scripts/local_throughput.py` (`eval/results/phase2c/local_throughput.json`). Base Qwen3.5-4B runs in the local Ollama server, which serves it on its MLX runner with nvfp4 weights. It reads the credit check's seeded 50 candidates, with the same 948-token instructions and ChatML as on Tinker.\n\n  | Requests at once | 50 articles took | Articles an hour | Tokens generated an article | Days for 1,236,122 |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|\n{rows}\n\n- **At the best setting,** {best['concurrent']} at once, the full pass takes about **{best['full_pass_days']} days of machine time and no credits.**\n- So the LoRA can be trained on Tinker and the pass run here, with the adapter loaded in Ollama: the plan's step 9 export.\n- **Not measured yet:** whether the nvfp4 weights read as Tinker's do. Step 9 measures that on dev before the pass, as RDR-10 requires.\n- The base model's answers are longer than a trained adapter's will be, since it hasn't learned the format. Generation dominates the time, so this is an upper bound.\n\"\"\")\nPY\necho ok","description":"Write a helper that fills BUDGET.md's local-path section from the result"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"93504215-1cd5-4a2c-916e-63ef4ec448d4","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgatA7KAaNhmwkTozRGBM","requestRef":"33729be3-62a8-4cd6-b1a8-046bf91a22bd","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1c4b8fad-1523-460a-a058-db93d1ce4aa0","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:40:36.578Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
