{"parentUuid":"40177ab0-f8e2-4531-9d50-c01734ee7f18","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2a214a50-efbb-455a-8523-9f01e035ad20","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FARaa5XfCarpkhVUqdKnJ3","type":"tool_result","content":"{'concurrent': 1, 'wall_seconds': 421.4, 'articles_per_hour': 427, 'prompt_tokens': 59046, 'output_tokens': 3795, 'full_pass_days': 120.6}\n{'concurrent': 4, 'wall_seconds': 201.1, 'articles_per_hour': 895, 'prompt_tokens': 59046, 'output_tokens': 3639, 'full_pass_days': 57.6}\n{'concurrent': 8, 'wall_seconds': 206.1, 'articles_per_hour': 873, 'prompt_tokens': 59046, 'output_tokens': 3762, 'full_pass_days': 59.0}\nexit 0\n\n## The free path: the full pass on this Mac\n\nMeasured by `scripts/local_throughput.py` (`eval/results/phase2c/local_throughput.json`). Base Qwen3.5-4B runs in the local Ollama server, which serves it on its MLX runner with nvfp4 weights. It reads the credit check's seeded 50 candidates, with the same 948-token instructions and ChatML as on Tinker.\n\n  | Requests at once | 50 articles took | Articles an hour | Tokens generated an article | Days for 1,236,122 |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|\n  | 1 | 421 s | 427 | 76 | 120.6 |\n  | 4 | 201 s | 895 | 73 | 57.6 |\n  | 8 | 206 s | 873 | 75 | 59.0 |\n\n- **At the best setting,** 4 at once, the full pass takes about **57.6 days of machine time and no credits.**\n- So the LoRA can be trained on Tinker and the pass run here, with the adapter loaded in Ollama: the plan's step 9 export.\n- **Not measured yet:** whether the nvfp4 weights read as Tinker's do. Step 9 measures that on dev before the pass, as RDR-10 requires.\n- The base model's answers are longer than a trained adapter's will be, since it hasn't learned the format. Generation dominates the time, so this is an upper bound.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"57b14010-8b46-4d8d-8608-b3f7b8e390af","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:48:33.330Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"{'concurrent': 1, 'wall_seconds': 421.4, 'articles_per_hour': 427, 'prompt_tokens': 59046, 'output_tokens': 3795, 'full_pass_days': 120.6}\n{'concurrent': 4, 'wall_seconds': 201.1, 'articles_per_hour': 895, 'prompt_tokens': 59046, 'output_tokens': 3639, 'full_pass_days': 57.6}\n{'concurrent': 8, 'wall_seconds': 206.1, 'articles_per_hour': 873, 'prompt_tokens': 59046, 'output_tokens': 3762, 'full_pass_days': 59.0}\nexit 0\n\n## The free path: the full pass on this Mac\n\nMeasured by `scripts/local_throughput.py` (`eval/results/phase2c/local_throughput.json`). Base Qwen3.5-4B runs in the local Ollama server, which serves it on its MLX runner with nvfp4 weights. It reads the credit check's seeded 50 candidates, with the same 948-token instructions and ChatML as on Tinker.\n\n  | Requests at once | 50 articles took | Articles an hour | Tokens generated an article | Days for 1,236,122 |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|\n  | 1 | 421 s | 427 | 76 | 120.6 |\n  | 4 | 201 s | 895 | 73 | 57.6 |\n  | 8 | 206 s | 873 | 75 | 59.0 |\n\n- **At the best setting,** 4 at once, the full pass takes about **57.6 days of machine time and no credits.**\n- So the LoRA can be trained on Tinker and the pass run here, with the adapter loaded in Ollama: the plan's step 9 export.\n- **Not measured yet:** whether the nvfp4 weights read as Tinker's do. Step 9 measures that on dev before the pass, as RDR-10 requires.\n- The base model's answers are longer than a trained adapter's will be, since it hasn't learned the format. Generation dominates the time, so this is an upper bound.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"df270333-2c7e-4624-a2fe-24cef2ef3010","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2c-reader","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"por