{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","id":"dc34e215-a52c-4947-a0bf-1cafa19832fb","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:50:10.433Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"7b35af0d1ba22d1b1b7d4c91038d50b583ea5d544dd1607adac5368903cb8a35","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"dd03cc33-56b8-464c-870c-5a9eee6a3c43","keep":641,"tail":["6086201c29078ce901db320a1611e9eef8eaf7a84fd8bf41ecca1ec955138a2f","7e8f82c91bf0574f377e5e4d8da4de9755c9398c1c110dd8983d0b258c409637"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",642,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"0d55b14e1905a5d3af2f41a387ae43d3b7e2d3b55d5c7b4bd67c09af0b855672"}
{"parentUuid":"53d66b9f-175c-47e4-9594-fc7f7065af27","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgatubq7Uq1XmZXxuYv7y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"2C.3 interim: the teacher plateaus at 112/150 on kind, so I stopped after round 3. Local 4B would take about 58 days for the full pass, and caching isn't confirmed yet.\n\nEverything is pushed at 7505a00, checked with `ls-remote`, and tests (390) and lint pass. Tinker spend this round was one dev round, about $4.4 at most, inside your $10 cap.\n\n**1. RDR-9 is amended:** the verifier is calibrated on dev, never gold, because a threshold tuned on gold would flatter eval B's field scores.\n\n**2. Teacher rounds on dev.** The kind confusion matrices for rounds 1–3 are in `teacher_confusion.json`. Round 2's biggest cells were the teacher calling things `other`: 14 dev idioms, 7 fictions and 7 reports.\n\n| | Round 1 | Round 2 | Round 3 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Kind (of 150) | 114 | 112 (67–81%) | 112 (67–81%) |\n| Report or not | 139 | 139 | 139 (κ 0.76) |\n| Seen (of reports both called) | 9 of 24 | 7 of 24 | 10 of 23 (26–63%) |\n| People | 5 of 24 | 6 of 24 | 7 of 23 (16–51%) |\n\n- Round 2's gain was a format fix: the teacher had written fields as bare strings, and a worked example of the JSON shape fixed it.\n- Round 3 added five general lines, each a restatement of POLICY, with the dev confusions behind each noted in the code. Idiom rose from 11 to 18, but adverts, religious and other gave back as much.\n- No gain reached its interval's width, so I stopped there.\n- The weak spot for training is report recall: the teacher finds 23 of dev's 32 reports. The 7 it misses are claims inside essays and round-ups.\n\n**3. Caching isn't confirmed yet.** Billing runs about three hours behind: its last bucket is 16:00, and today's runs came after 19:00.\n- Billing does mark each prefill bucket cached or not. This account's earlier teacher runs were 88% cached (658,432 of 746,348 prompt tokens), billed at a fifth of the rate.\n- `credit_check.billed` now splits cached from uncached, so confirming it is one call once billing catches up. Until then BUDGET.md says to plan on the high end.\n\n**4. The free path is too slow to stand alone.** Ollama serves base Qwen3.5-4B on its MLX runner with nvfp4 weights.\n- On the credit check's seeded 50 with the 948-token instructions, it reads 427 articles an hour one at a time and about 890 at four or eight at once.\n- That is about 58 days of machine time for the 1,236,122 candidates, with no credits. Prompt reading dominates: about 1,180 prompt tokens an article against 75 generated.\n- So it's a fallback for whatever part of the pass the credits can't cover, not the whole pass before the site's date.\n- Whether the nvfp4 weights read as Tinker's do is step 9's to measure on dev.\n\n**5. Not started, as you asked:** the 3,000-article teacher run and the skip-rule measure. Both wait on the owner's balance.\n\nOne slip to know about: one commit (11c26da) went out before its lint and secret scan ran, because my command chain skipped them. I scanned the pushed commit afterwards and it's clean. The only lint failure was formatting, fixed in 7505a00."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":235,"cache_read_input_tokens":882319,"output_tokens":1186,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":235,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1186,"cache_read_input_tokens":882319,"cache_creation_input_tokens":235,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":235},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"faad345a-11ec-447f-9c67-746578274afd","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgatuaqaT1dRw9k2dy3DF","requestRef":"dc34e215-a52c-4947-a0bf-1cafa19832fb","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"f35872ec-abbf-44d5-a07f-1ba86378dd87","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:50:22.568Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
