{"parentUuid":"a759f500-0fe2-4cc0-b5f2-9e7dc37c0cc1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgavB7CjCy2kbeZjs6FtZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UznU7rdWCEMMu9FsktzyFL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && sed -n 119,160p Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md","description":"Read the plan's 2C steps 4 to the gate"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":309,"cache_read_input_tokens":944689,"output_tokens":234,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":54},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":309,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":234,"cache_read_input_tokens":944689,"cache_creation_input_tokens":309,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":309},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01UznU7rdWCEMMu9FsktzyFL":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && sed -n 119,160p Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md","description":"Read the plan's 2C steps 4 to the gate"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"e2667fda-b430-48d4-81fe-24792bf62175","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgavB69iz7DzgCDNLLR4j","requestRef":"5a0f2f04-d318-4279-9270-210fbf5294c8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2b1814ed-8639-4fe2-833e-3021f3026ec3","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:06:53.510Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"2b1814ed-8639-4fe2-833e-3021f3026ec3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d2602119-bcf8-4f02-a39d-de2ec6b1e251","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UznU7rdWCEMMu9FsktzyFL","type":"tool_result","content":"3. Label gold and dev before seeing any model output, with a blind second pass on gold to measure agreement. Then freeze them: `HASH` gains the labels' sha256.\n   - Done in decision 38. `labels.jsonl` and `dev_labels.jsonl` hold one label per article, the ruling where the passes disagreed. The second pass is in `second_pass.jsonl`, and each dispute's two labels and ruling are in `adjudication.jsonl`. Evals read only the two label files, and `check_leakage.py` checks their hashes.\n4. Teacher labels for the training pool, with the leakage check passing.\n   - The training draw comes from `split.json`'s pool, at most one printing per story, and `check_leakage.py` is extended to check that draw.\n   - Each drawn item is checked again against gold and dev by a stricter text rule: at least 4 shared runs, and 0.05 of the shorter's (the EM's call). The split's rule, 0.10 and 5 runs, sits just under the lowest one-story pair (0.105, 6 runs), and a false flag on a training draw costs nothing.\n5. Baselines: a keyword rule, and base 4B both zero-shot and few-shot.\n6. LoRA training on Tinker, iterating on the dev split until improvements stop. Each iteration is recorded.\n7. Eval B, ablations B1 to B10, and edge-case slices E1 to E14.\n   - Eval B also has the reader screen the random reservoirs, for a recall bound that doesn't rest on flag words (decision 30). The Tinker credit check sets how many it reads.\n   - That screen gives lexicon v2's independent recall. Decision 31's 84% is in-sample.\n   - **A pooled recall screen** (the EM's call, decision 37's review). At the judged rates, six in ten of the population's expected reports sit in the low-rate strata. Those are the bulk, about 16,000, and the five rules without a headline term, about 11,000. Gold expects about 4.5 reports there.\n     - A seeded draw from those strata is screened by the tuned reader and by the teacher. Every article either calls a report is read by hand under `POLICY.md`.\n     - The credit check sizes it to find about 50 reports.\n     - Recall is reported per stratum and weighted. It's an upper bound, since reports both models miss go uncounted.\n8. The failure log, and `eval/MODEL_CARD.md`.\n9. The local export and the offline proof.\n10. The full pass over all triaged candidates.\n   - Lexicon v2 makes the reader's job 1,236,122 candidates, 17.7% more than v1's (decision 31). The Tinker credit check weighs that before the pass starts.\n   - **Every triaged candidate is read** (the EM's call, decision 36). A member that reads differently from its story's first printing becomes a report of its own, shown as printed inside its story. It counts as different if it's a report where the first printing isn't one, or if it gives another place, date or person.\n   - If the credit check finds that every candidate doesn't fit, stop. Bring the EM the shortfall, and the skip rule's loss, measured on a seeded draw of skipped members read beside their first printings.\n\n**Gate**\n- The gold hash hasn't changed since the freeze, and the leakage check passes.\n- The eval JSON and charts include confidence intervals.\n- At least one failure is written up with its fix.\n- The offline proof passes, and the full-pass counts are recorded.\n- The EM audits 30 random reader outputs against their clippings.\n\n### 2D: load, cluster and harvest\n**Persona:** data engineer.\n- Geocode, cluster, embed, and load Atlas.\n  - Cluster with decision 36's stories at its tuned 0.25. Before loading, measure these changes on a fresh draw, never on decision 36's frozen set:\n    - the body's links added to the blocking. Its probe found 76 of 80 such pairs to be one story, outside eval A's links.\n    - a floor on the share of the longer printing. Three large clusters still join two texts that each hold a short first printing.\n    - digits in the shingles. `eval-0508`, freight columns a year apart, passes the threshold because the tokens drop their figures.\n    - short texts' weak links. A 50-word advert keeps about five of its seven-word runs, so a few OCR errors leave it unlinked. Decision 37's whole-text check found 1,196 such reprints of gold and dev articles outside their groups, mostly adverts, timetables and columns.\n  - Count the members whose reading differs from their first printing's. Each is shown as a report of its own, and is a false-merge candidate.\n  - Before choosing int8 embeddings over float32, measure their neighbours against float32's on real embeddings. Decision 33's check used synthetic vectors.\n  - The places autocomplete index, `places_search`, needs a free Search slot (decision 33). `make db-init` creates it once there is one.\n  - Fetch the loc.gov title records only for the LCCNs among stored printings, as decision 29 does for pages, cached (`paperghosts/geo/loc.py`). A paper's place is checked against its record (decision 34), and without one it stands unchecked.\n  - Story places follow 2C's rule: a county or state the text gives, or the dateline, and never the paper's state.\n  - A crop is fetched through `crops_for`, which checks a page by its size and its OCR before its crop is shown, wherever its member and batch path don't agree (decision 35).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b63d4c7e-f730-4b33-a5ba-e7407e8ae721","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:06:54.464Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"3. Label gold and dev before seeing any model output, with a blind second pass on gold to measure agreement. Then freeze them: `HASH` gains the labels' sha256.\n   - Done in decision 38. `labels.jsonl` and `dev_labels.jsonl` hold one label per article, the ruling where the passes disagreed. The second pass is in `second_pass.jsonl`, and each dispute's two labels and ruling are in `adjudication.jsonl`. Evals read only the two label files, and `check_leakage.py` checks their hashes.\n4. Teacher labels for the training pool, with the leakage check passing.\n   - The training draw comes from `split.json`'s pool, at most one printing per story, and `check_leakage.py` is extended to check that draw.\n   - Each drawn item is checked again against gold and dev by a stricter text rule: at least 4 shared runs, and 0.05 of the shorter's (the EM's call). The split's rule, 0.10 and 5 runs, sits just under the lowest one-story pair (0.105, 6 runs), and a false flag on a training draw costs nothing.\n5. Baselines: a keyword rule, and base 4B both zero-shot and few-shot.\n6. LoRA training on Tinker, iterating on the dev split until improvements stop. Each iteration is recorded.\n7. Eval B, ablations B1 to B10, and edge-case slices E1 to E14.\n   - Eval B also has the reader screen the random reservoirs, for a recall bound that doesn't rest on flag words (decision 30). The Tinker credit check sets how many it reads.\n   - That screen gives lexicon v2's independent recall. Decision 31's 84% is in-sample.\n   - **A pooled recall screen** (the EM's call, decision 37's review). At the judged rates, six in ten of the population's expected reports sit in the low-rate strata. Those are the bulk, about 16,000, and the five rules without a headline term, about 11,000. Gold expects about 4.5 reports there.\n     - A seeded draw from those strata is screened by the tuned reader and by the teacher. Every article either calls a report is read by hand under `POLICY.md`.\n     - The credit check sizes it to find about 50 reports.\n     - Recall is reported per stratum and weighted. It's an upper bound, since reports both models miss go uncounted.\n8. The failure log, and `eval/MODEL_CARD.md`.\n9. The local export and the offline proof.\n10. The full pass over all triaged candidates.\n   - Lexicon v2 makes the reader's job 1,236,122 candidates, 17.7% more than v1's (decision 31). The Tinker credit check weighs that before the pass starts.\n   - **Every triaged candidate is read** (the EM's call, decision 36). A member that reads differently from its story's first printing becomes a report of its own, shown as printed inside its story. It counts as different if it's a report where the first printing isn't one, or if it gives another place, date or person.\n   - If the credit check finds that every candidate doesn't fit, stop. Bring the EM the shortfall, and the skip rule's loss, measured on a seeded draw of skipped members read beside their first printings.\n\n**Gate**\n- The gold hash hasn't changed since the freeze, and the leakage check passes.\n- The eval JSON and charts include confidence intervals.\n- At least one failure is written up with its fix.\n- The offline proof passes, and the full-pass counts are recorded.\n- The EM audits 30 random reader outputs against their clippings.\n\n### 2D: load, cluster and harvest\n**Persona:** data engineer.\n- Geocode, cluster, embed, and load Atlas.\n  - Cluster with decision 36's stories at its tuned 0.25. Before loading, measure these changes on a fresh draw, never on decision 36's frozen set:\n    - the body's links added to the blocking. Its probe found 76 of 80 such pairs to be one story, outside eval A's links.\n    - a floor on the share of the longer printing. Three large clusters still join two texts that each hold a short first printing.\n    - digits in the shingles. `eval-0508`, freight columns a year apart, passes the threshold because the tokens drop their figures.\n    - short texts' weak links. A 50-word advert keeps about five of its seven-word runs, so a few OCR errors leave it unlinked. Decision 37's whole-text check found 1,196 such reprints of gold and dev articles outside their groups, mostly adverts, timetables and columns.\n  - Count the members whose reading differs from their first printing's. Each is shown as a report of its own, and is a false-merge candidate.\n  - Before choosing int8 embeddings over float32, measure their neighbours against float32's on real embeddings. Decision 33's check used synthetic vectors.\n  - The places autocomplete index, `places_search`, needs a free Search slot (decision 33). `make db-init` creates it once there is one.\n  - Fetch the loc.gov title records only for the LCCNs among stored printings, as decision 29 does for pages, cached (`paperghosts/geo/loc.py`). A paper's place is checked against its record (decision 34), and without one it stands unchecked.\n  - Story places follow 2C's rule: a county or state the text gives, or the dateline, and never the paper's state.\n  - A crop is fetched through `crops_for`, which checks a page by its size and its OCR before its crop is shown, wherever its member and batch path don't agree (decision 35).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e2667fda-b430-48d4-81fe-24792bf62175","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2c-reader","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":4,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2b1814ed-8639-4fe2-833e-3021f3026ec3","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Do