{"parentUuid":"4f31913a-c9a1-4e1d-a5b1-fde6ea6f28fc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"961e3d1a-ef11-4fb3-9157-154d4dc357e8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, Bash, Edit, Monitor, Read, SendMessage, Skill, TaskStop, ToolSearch, WebSearch, Write, mcp__Claude_Browser__browser_batch, mcp__Claude_Browser__computer, mcp__Claude_Browser__find, mcp__Claude_Browser__get_page_text, mcp__Claude_Browser__javascript_tool, mcp__Claude_Browser__navigate, mcp__Claude_Browser__tabs_close, mcp__ccd_pr__get_status, mcp__ccd_session__mark_chapter, mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan, mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\n**Setup.**\n- This is a child session of the EM session `local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e`, on Paper Ghosts: repo `/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts`, branch `phase-2c-reader`.\n- Hand-over notes go to `/Users/hotragn/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e/`. `step-2C.2.md` and `step-2C.3.md` have been written.\n- Every turn ends with `mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up`, then a closing message. Use `mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan` for the task list.\n- Report formats the EM gave, in order:\n  - \"2C.2: GATE PASSED\" (done)\n  - \"2C.3: GATE PASSED / BLOCKED — reason\"\n  - \"2C.3 interim: ...\" and \"2C.3 interim 2: ...\"\n  - \"2C.3: SPEND STOPPED — <today's Tinker total>\" (sent)\n  - Now: \"Your report's first line is `2C.3: GATE PASSED` or `2C.3: BLOCKED — <reason>`.\"\n  - \"Before the long teacher run starts, send me an interim report with the teacher comparison. I'll approve the teacher choice before hours of compute go in.\"\n\n**Standing and security rules (verbatim where possible):**\n- \"never print, log or echo secrets from `.env`, and check keys by shape only\"\n- \"No global installs and no Homebrew\"\n- \"Stop and ask before anything public (repo visibility, deploys, DNS, posting) or any spending beyond free tiers and existing credits\"\n- \"Make small commits on phase branches and open pull requests into `main`; I merge them\" (no PR until 2C closes)\n- \"Record numbered decisions in `Docs/DECISIONS.md`, and end each milestone with a STATUS block in `Docs/RESUME.md`\"\n- \"Entire capture is enabled through `.claude/settings.json`; don't touch it\"\n- Scope pgrep/ps to my uid; never print the hostname; filter push output with `grep -v -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\"`.\n- Library of Congress requests: one at a time, cached, 3.5 s apart.\n- \"Never touch sample_mflix or any other database\"\n- \"check claims like 'pushed' with `ls-remote`\"\n- Commits end with `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`.\n- \"No model output of any kind may touch gold or dev until the labels are frozen\" (now frozen). Gold stays untouched until eval B.\n- **The gate chain:** \"chain the gate as `make lint && make test && <secret scan> && git push`, never with `;`\". The scan is:\n  - `git diff --cached > $S/staged-X.diff`\n  - `uv run python $S/scan_staged.py .env $S/staged-X.diff`\n  - `grep -c -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\"` on the diff, which must be 0\n- **Owner decision:** \"no Tinker spend at all, and step 2C runs locally.\" \"Make no further Tinker calls of any kind.\" Reading billing is fine since it's free.\n- \"No model download may take free disk below 15 GB. Delete nothing to make room without the owner's yes. The installed gemma4 models are the owner's.\" Free disk is now 15 GB, at the floor.\n- \"Training labels must come from the local open-weight teacher, never from Claude or from the reading agents. Gold and dev are for evaluation only.\"\n- \"Don't start the 3,000-article teacher run or the skip-rule measure until I send the owner's answer\" / until the teacher choice is approved.\n\n**The EM's current re-plan of 2C.3, all local:**\n1. **Local teacher candidates:** gemma4:26b-a4b-it-qat (installed). A Qwen MoE or dense 27B doesn't fit: the 35B-A3B models are 22 GB, the 27Bs 17.5 GB, and disk is at the floor.\n   - Run each on dev with round 3's prompt, thinking on and off.\n   - Score kind, report-or-not, report recall on dev's 32 and each field, with Wilson intervals, after the verifier.\n   - Report the time per article and the projected hours for the draw.\n2. **The quality comparison:** `eval/results/phase2c/teacher_local.json` and a BUDGET.md table, the best local teacher against Tinker's 397B round 3 (kind 112/150, recall 23/32) and the 397B thinking run's partial results (none). Say which differences are inside the intervals.\n3. **mlx-lm LoRA on Qwen3.5-4B:** time per epoch on 3,000 examples, peak memory, and a check that the adapter loads in the full-pass reader.\n4. **The full pass locally** with the short prompt: throughput, projected days, resumable from checkpoints, logged.\n5. **Free levers, measured on dev:** majority vote over local samples, routing uncertain or report-ish articles to a thinking pass, and the draw's size.\n6. Training labels come only from the local teacher.\n7. Update BUDGET.md and the plan's 2C steps, and record decision 39 (the owner's call).\n8. **Runtime diagnosis (EM message):** \"688 tokens in 4.11 s is about 170 tokens a second... find the cause\":\n   - (1) In Ollama: reloads, num_ctx, parallel slots, load_duration against prompt_eval_duration.\n   - (2) In mlx-lm directly: prefill tok/s on the same 50 with the short prompt, batched generation, and a prompt cache.\n   - (3) Project from the fastest path that gives the same answers, with agreement between the runtimes on the 50 (kind and JSON). Record each figure with its settings.\n   - \"Same for gemma4 as the teacher.\"\n9. **The latest EM message:** \"before anyone concludes from outcome at 5/24, read its 19 misses... Report how many misses are format and how many are judgment, and score it again with the format normalised to the schema, keeping both numbers. Do the same check for the 397B's place state at 13/23. Then carry on with thinking on.\"\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n- **Tinker:**\n  - Sampling and billing: `AdminClient`/`RestClient.get_billing_usage` takes hour-aligned bounds and windows of at most 14 days. Buckets carry `cached` for prefill and lag about 3 hours.\n  - Rates per million tokens:\n    - Qwen3.5-397B: prompt $3.00 uncached, $0.60 cached; generated $7.50.\n    - Qwen3.5-4B: prompt $0.33 uncached, $0.066 cached; generated $1.005; training $0.737.\n  - The balance was $0, and the account is now blocked with HTTP 402.\n- **Qwen ChatML:**\n  - Rendered by hand with an empty `<think>\\n\\n</think>` block for thinking off.\n  - jinja2 was added for each model's own chat template: Qwen `enable_thinking=True`; gpt-oss `reasoning_effort`.\n  - Kimi's tokenizer needs remote code plus tiktoken, so it was refused.\n- **The quote verifier:** normalized exact match scores 1. Otherwise the best word-aligned window is compared with SequenceMatcher. The threshold, calibrated on dev, is 0.70, at which 0% of cross-article negatives pass.\n- **Agreement metrics:** in `second_pass.agreed` and `same()`: Wilson intervals, Cohen's kappa with a bootstrap interval, and field agreement by quote overlap.\n- **Ollama 0.40.2:**\n  - `qwen3.5:4b` runs on the MLX runner with nvfp4 weights, loaded at 12 GB with an 8,192 context.\n  - `gemma4:26b-a4b-it-qat` runs on the llamacpp runner, 15 GB, 16,384 context.\n  - The `think` option is used for gemma.\n- **mlx-lm 0.32.2:** in uv group `local` (macOS only). It supports `qwen3_5`. `batch_generate`, `stream_generate`, `make_prompt_cache`, and the `GenerationResponse` fields `prompt_tps`, `generation_tps` and `peak_memory`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n**Labels and the blind re-ruling (2C.2 fix, all committed):**\n- `eval/gold/labels.jsonl` and `dev_labels.jsonl` hold final labels, one per article.\n- The HASH sha256s are:\n  - labels.jsonl: d51a3737…364\n  - dev_labels.jsonl: 99ee43…931\n- `eval/gold/second_pass.jsonl` holds the 330 second-pass labels. `eval/gold/adjudication.jsonl` holds each dispute: first, second, ruling, own_ruling, blind ruling, and how it was settled.\n- `scripts/blind_rulings.py` (modes `packets`, `check`, `compare`, `settle`; functions `masked`, `cases`, `stated`, `compared`, `settled`, `problems`), with `tests/test_blind_rulings.py`.\n- `eval/results/phase2c/blind_rulings.json`.\n- Decision 38 is amended.\n\n**`scripts/second_pass.py`:**\n- Paths: SECOND_PASS and ADJUDICATION.\n- Modes: `packets`, `check`, `save`, `agreement`, `disputes`, `rule`, `frozen`.\n- `paired(split, out, second_pass, adjudication)`.\n\n**`scripts/label_gold.py`:** `save(path, record, replace=False)` and `shown()`.\n\n**`scripts/check_leakage.py`:** `hashes_hold()` checks file by file; `flagged`/`between` take `leak`/`fewest`.\n\n**`scripts/gold_measures.py`:** results in `eval/results/phase2c/gold_measures.json`:\n- gold reports 46 against 35.3 expected\n- weighted rate 0.97%\n- the story-place rule 29/32, paper state 2/9\n\n**`scripts/credit_check.py`:**\n- Modes `pool`, which writes `data/gold/pool.json.zst` (1,539,818 articles, 1,229,780 candidates), and `measure`.\n- `billed(model, since)` splits cached from uncached.\n- `eval/results/phase2c/credit_check.json`.\n\n**`scripts/teacher.py`:**\n- INSTRUCTIONS includes round 3's five POLICY-restating lines, followed by POLICY.md in full.\n- Functions: `system_prompt`, `prompt_sha256`, `rendered`, `article_text`, `parsed` (drops malformed fields), `normal`, `score`, `verified`, `final`, `read`, `voted`, `quotes`, `calibrated`, `recall`, `dev_round`, `confusion`.\n- `read(..., thinking, samples, temperature)` is guarded:\n  ```python\n  if os.environ.get(\"TINKER_SPEND_ALLOWED\") != \"1\":\n      raise RuntimeError(\"Tinker sampling is off (decision 39): set TINKER_SPEND_ALLOWED=1 only with the owner's yes\")\n  ```\n- `dev_round(round_name, model=TEACHER, thinking=False, samples=1, temperature=0.0, max_tokens=700)` rescores from `data/teacher/dev_ROUND.jsonl` if it exists, with no Tinker call.\n- The CLI is `dev ROUND [--model --thinking --samples --temperature --max-tokens]` and `confusion R...`.\n- Results: `teacher_dev_r1.json`, `_r2.json`, `_r3.json` and `teacher_confusion.json`.\n\n**`scripts/training_draw.py`:**\n- Gold's ALLOCATION scaled, one printing per story, systematic draw.\n- `check` uses STRICT `{\"leak\": 0.05, \"fewest\": 4}`. It passed on a provisional 3,000, which wasn't committed.\n- `tests/test_training_draw.py`.\n\n**`scripts/local_throughput.py`:**\n- Modes `long`, `short` and `prefix`, using Ollama `qwen3.5:4b` with `raw: True`.\n- SHORT = \"Label this newspaper article for the ghost-report archive. Answer with the label's JSON.\"\n- Results in `eval/results/phase2c/local_throughput.json`:\n  - long prompt: 427/h at 1, 895/h at 4, 873/h at 8 (57.6 days)\n  - short prompt, clean: 812/h at 4 (63.5 days)\n  - prefix: long prompt 1,450 tokens evaluated in 5.45 s, short 688 in 4.11 s, so no prefix reuse\n\n**`scripts/local_teacher.py`:**\n- `one(row, model, system, think)` calls Ollama `/api/chat` with `\"think\": think`, num_ctx 16384 and num_predict 4096.\n- Modes `throughput MODEL` and `dev MODEL ROUND [think]`. The dev mode runs one at a time, saves the raw file, then calls `dev_round` (no Tinker), and writes timing to `eval/results/phase2c/local_teacher.json`.\n\n**`scripts/local_lora_timing.py`:**\n- Runs `python -m mlx_lm lora --model Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B --train --data DIR --iters N --batch-size B --num-layers 16 --max-seq-length 2048` and parses It/sec, Tokens/sec and Peak mem.\n- Projects an epoch of 3,000 examples into `eval/results/phase2c/local_lora_timing.json`.\n- Not yet committed? It was committed in 9ecc117.\n\n**`scripts/runtime_check.py`:** new and uncommitted. Modes `ollama` (num_ctx 2048 vs 8192, load and prompt durations), `mlx` (one at a time, batched 4 and 8, the long prompt's prefix cached vs uncached) and `agree`. Results go to `eval/results/phase2c/runtime_check.json`.\n\n**Tests:** `tests/test_teacher.py` has 7 tests, including the guard test. `make test` passes 392.\n\n**Docs:**\n- `Docs/SRS.md`: RDR-9 now calibrates on dev.\n- `Docs/BUDGET.md`: the Tinker credit section, the caching evidence (88% cached historically), the free-path section, and the spend-stopped section with today's table.\n- `Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md`: 2C steps 4, 6, 7, 9 and 10 moved to the local path.\n- `Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`: the reader row moved to local (decision 39).\n- `pyproject.toml` and `uv.lock`: jinja2 added, and the `local` group with `mlx-lm; sys_platform == 'darwin'`.\n\n**Scratch** (`S=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad`):\n- `$S/chain.sh` and `$S/chain.log` (the chain)\n- `$S/lora/train.jsonl` (400) and `valid.jsonl` (20): seeded pool articles with a placeholder answer\n- `$S/local_section.py`\n- logs: g26.log, g26t.log, lora.log, short2.log\n\n**Commits:** 35e8a53, 537e605, e2d9200, 4777043, 11c26da, 7505a00, e4fda3a and 9ecc117, the latest pushed and confirmed with ls-remote.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n- **Billing usage:** it needs hour-aligned bounds and windows of at most 14 days; fixed.\n- **jinja2 was missing:** I first rendered ChatML by hand, then added jinja2 for the thinking templates.\n- **The teacher wrote flat strings,** so the parse dropped its fields in round 1. Round 2 added a worked JSON example, and `parsed` now drops malformed fields.\n- **TypeError in `quotes()` on string fields:** fixed by the `shaped()` normalisation.\n- **ruff:** BLE001 (narrowed to TinkerError, TimeoutError and ConnectionError), RUF046, RUF034, I001, and format failures.\n- **Commit 11c26da** was pushed without lint or the scan because the chain used `;`. I scanned it after the push (clean) and fixed the formatting in 7505a00. The EM said: chain with `&&`, never `;`.\n- **The 397B thinking round** hit HTTP 402 (billing block) and was killed. It saved nothing.\n- **Spend:** I assumed credits existed. The balance was $0, so today's $3.19–14.45 was billed to the owner's card. Reported honestly.\n- **Kimi tokenizer:** it needs remote code and tiktoken, so I refused it and used gpt-oss instead, which was never run.\n- **ProcessPool spawn from stdin failed:** moved to a script file.\n- **The first short-prompt run (378/h)** overlapped with other load; re-run clean at 812/h.\n- **du showed 9.7 MB for the HF download:** it was Xet links; `du -L` shows 8.7 GB.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n\n**Blind re-ruling:**\n- Kind matched the first labeller in 28/34. People matched in 4/19, with the blind judges siding with the second pass.\n- The blind ruling was taken in 28 cases and mine kept in 2.\n- Rule 10's bullet: 15 of 17 would be `other` even without it.\n\n**Teacher on dev:**\n- 397B round 3: kind 112/150, report-or-not 139, recall 23/32 (55–84%). Fields: place 14/23, place_state 13/23, seen 10, outcome 16, specific_place 16, place_type 18, precision 16, people 7.\n- gemma4 with thinking off (g26): kind 100/150 (59–74%), report-or-not 134 (83–93%), recall 24/32 (58–87%), 2 unparsed. Fields: place 14/24, place_state 22/24, seen 11, outcome 5, specific_place 11, place_type 14, precision 13, people 5.\n- gemma4 speed: 244 articles an hour, 9,862 prompt tokens an article, 9.1 s of prompt each (about 1,080 tok/s, so no overhead problem), and 12.3 h for a 3,000 draw.\n\n**Local 4B runtime:** Ollama MLX shows a fixed overhead, not prefill compute; under diagnosis with `runtime_check.py`.\n\n**Disk:** free disk is 15 GB, at the floor, so no further downloads are possible.\n\n6. All user messages (all from the EM session):\n- **2C.2 accepted, with the blind re-ruling fix and the 2C.3 brief:**\n  - the credit check\n  - a teacher tuned on dev only\n  - the verifier calibrated on dev\n  - a pool draw with the stricter leakage check\n  - provenance on teacher labels\n  - a hand-check of 40\n- **The re-ruling accepted.** \"Until then, work only on items that spend under $10 in all.\" Asks:\n  - the RDR-9 amendment (approved)\n  - round 3 with confusion matrices: \"write each prompt change as a general rule from POLICY, never an article-specific hint\", stop when the gain is under the interval width\n  - the caching check\n  - a free local path\n  - \"Don't start the 3,000-article teacher run or the skip-rule measure until I send the owner's answer.\"\n- **Interim reviewed;** spend cap $30. Thinking on; majority of 3 at temp 0.6; one other large model; the student's short prompt; local timing and prefix reuse; caching; \"On the slip: chain the gate as `make lint && make test && <secret scan> && git push`, never with `;`.\"\n- **\"STOP all Tinker requests now.** The owner's console shows a remaining credit balance of $0.00, with $0.80 of unpaid usage due this month... My $30 cap is withdrawn.\" It asked:\n  - cancel and kill the running jobs\n  - report what ran, with tokens and costs\n  - make \"no further Tinker calls of any kind\"\n  - local work only: mlx-lm LoRA timing and peak memory; the largest local teacher\n  - first line \"2C.3: SPEND STOPPED — <today's Tinker total>\"\n- **The owner has decided:** \"no Tinker spend at all, and step 2C runs locally... Finish the spend-stopped report first.\" Machine constraints: M4, 24 GB, 30 GB free (now 15). Items 1–7 as in section 1. \"Before the long teacher run starts, send me an interim report with the teacher comparison.\"\n- **About the prefix test:** \"don't interrupt\" the chain. Find the cause in Ollama (reload, num_ctx, slots, load_duration) and in mlx-lm directly (prefill, batched, prompt cache). Project from the fastest path with the same answers, with agreement on the 50. Same for gemma4.\n- **Latest:** \"About gemma4 with thinking off: before anyone concludes from outcome at 5/24, read its 19 misses... format... or the verifier dropping a quote. Report how many misses are format and how many are judgment, and score it again with the format normalised to the schema, keeping both numbers. Do the same check for the 397B's place state at 13/23. Then carry on with thinking on.\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n- Analyse gemma4 g26's 19 outcome misses: format against judgment, and a normalised re-score keeping both numbers. Do the same for the 397B's place_state at 13/23.\n- Let the chain finish: gemma4 with thinking on (g26t), then the Ollama unload, then the LoRA timing. Don't interrupt it.\n- Run `scripts/runtime_check.py` (ollama, mlx, agree) after the chain, then project the full pass from the fastest equivalent path, and do the same overhead check for gemma4.\n- Check that the mlx adapter loads in the full-pass reader (Ollama).\n- Write `teacher_local.json` and the BUDGET.md comparison table, saying what's inside the intervals.\n- Measure the free levers on dev: majority vote, routing to a thinking pass, the draw's size.\n- Write decision 39 and update RESUME.\n- Send the interim teacher comparison before any long teacher run, and wait for approval.\n- Then the 2C.3 gate: local teacher labels for the draw with sha256 and provenance, the leakage check, a hand-check of 40, gate chain, and ls-remote.\n\n8. Current Work:\n- The local chain (`$S/chain.sh`, background ID bh1gvki0j) is running. `chain.log` shows:\n  - \"16:16:11 prefix done\"\n  - \"16:20:04 short rerun exit 0\"\n  - \"16:57:18 gemma think off exit 0\"\n- It is now running gemma4 with thinking on (`local_teacher.py dev gemma4:26b-a4b-it-qat g26t think`). Then it unloads Ollama's models and runs `local_lora_timing.py $S/lora 40 4`.\n- A monitor (bffcy1yv3) tails `chain.log`.\n- I had just reported gemma4 with thinking off against the 397B round 3 when the EM asked for the format-vs-judgment check on outcome and place_state.\n- `scripts/runtime_check.py` is written, linted and uncommitted, waiting for the chain to finish.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\nPer the EM's latest message: \"read its 19 misses. ... Report how many misses are format and how many are judgment, and score it again with the format normalised to the schema, keeping both numbers. Do the same check for the 397B's place state at 13/23. Then carry on with thinking on.\"\n- Next, without touching the GPU chain, read `data/teacher/dev_g26.jsonl` against `eval/gold/dev_labels.jsonl` for outcome on the reports both call reports.\n- Classify each miss: a value outside the schema or in the wrong case, a null against \"unknown\", the verifier dropping a quote, or a judgment difference.\n- Re-score with the format normalised, keeping both numbers.\n- Do the same for `data/teacher/dev_r3.jsonl`'s place_state.\n- Then continue waiting for the chain (gemma4 thinking on, then the LoRA timing) before running `runtime_check.py`.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/hotragn/.claude/projects/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"41541527-d0ad-459f-804f-82aff9fb68af","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:59:14.788Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":0,"turnIndex":68},"turnOrigin":"peer","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"41541527-d0ad-459f-804f-82aff9fb68af","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/scripts/runtime_check.py","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/scripts/runtime_check.py","content":"\"\"\"Why local prefill is slow, and which runtime the full pass should use (2C.3).\n\nOn the credit check's seeded 50 with the student's short prompt:\n  ollama    one request at a time at num_ctx 2048 and 8192, with Ollama's own load_duration and\n            prompt_eval_duration, so reloads and context allocation show apart from compute\n  mlx       mlx-lm directly on the downloaded Qwen3.5-4B weights: prefill and generation tokens\n            a second one article at a time, batched generation, and a prompt cache reused for\n            the instruction prefix the articles share\n  agree     the kind and the JSON the two runtimes give each article, greedy, compared\nWrites eval/results/phase2c/runtime_check.json, one key per mode, each with its settings.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport sys\nimport time\n\nimport httpx\nfrom credit_check import RESULT as CREDIT\nfrom credit_check import rows_of\nfrom label_gold import ROOT\nfrom local_throughput import SHORT\nfrom teacher import article_text, parsed, rendered\n\nRESULT = ROOT / \"eval\" / \"results\" / \"phase2c\" / \"runtime_check.json\"\nOLLAMA = \"http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/generate\"\nMODEL = \"Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B\"\nMAX_TOKENS = 700\n\n\ndef sample_rows() -> list:\n    picked = json.loads(CREDIT.read_text())[\"sample\"]\n    rows = rows_of(set(picked))\n    return [rows[aid] for aid in picked]\n\n\ndef ollama(rows: list) -> dict:\n    found = {}\n    for ctx in (2048, 8192):\n        out = []\n        for row in rows:\n            body = {\n                \"model\": \"qwen3.5:4b\",\n                \"prompt\": rendered(SHORT, article_text(row)),\n                \"raw\": True,\n                \"stream\": False,\n                \"keep_alive\": \"30m\",\n                \"options\": {\n                    \"temperature\": 0,\n                    \"num_predict\": MAX_TOKENS,\n                    \"num_ctx\": ctx,\n                    \"stop\": [\"<|im_end|>\"],\n                },\n            }\n            a = httpx.post(OLLAMA, json=body, timeout=600).json()\n            out.append(a)\n        n = len(out)\n        found[f\"num_ctx {ctx}\"] = {\n            \"settings\": {\n                \"num_ctx\": ctx,\n                \"concurrent\": 1,\n                \"keep_alive\": \"30m\",\n                \"prompt\": \"short\",\n            },\n            \"load_seconds\": sum(a.get(\"load_duration\", 0) for a in out) / n / 1e9,\n            \"prompt_seconds\": sum(a.get(\"prompt_eval_duration\", 0) for a in out)\n            / n\n            / 1e9,\n            \"prompt_tokens\": sum(a.get(\"prompt_eval_count\", 0) for a in out) / n,\n            \"generation_seconds\": sum(a.get(\"eval_duration\", 0) for a in out) / n / 1e9,\n            \"output_tokens\": sum(a.get(\"eval_count\", 0) for a in out) / n,\n            \"total_seconds\": sum(a.get(\"total_duration\", 0) for a in out) / n / 1e9,\n            \"answers\": [a.get(\"response\", \"\") for a in out],\n        }\n        f = found[f\"num_ctx {ctx}\"]\n        f[\"prefill_tokens_per_second\"] = f[\"prompt_tokens\"] / max(\n            f[\"prompt_seconds\"], 1e-9\n        )\n    return found\n\n\ndef mlx(rows: list) -> dict:\n    from mlx_lm import batch_generate, load, stream_generate\n    from mlx_lm.models.cache import make_prompt_cache\n    from mlx_lm.sample_utils import make_sampler\n\n    model, tokenizer = load(MODEL)\n    greedy = make_sampler(temp=0.0)\n    prompts = [\n        tokenizer.encode(rendered(SHORT, article_text(r)), add_special_tokens=False)\n        for r in rows\n    ]\n    found = {}\n\n    started, answers, stats = time.time(), [], []\n    for ids in prompts:\n        text, last = \"\", None\n        for last in stream_generate(\n            model, tokenizer, ids, max_tokens=MAX_TOKENS, sampler=greedy\n        ):\n            text += last.text\n            if \"<|im_end|>\" in text:\n                break\n        answers.append(text.split(\"<|im_end|>\")[0])\n        stats.append(last)\n    wall = time.time() - started\n    found[\"one at a time\"] = {\n        \"settings\": {\n            \"concurrent\": 1,\n            \"prompt\": \"short\",\n            \"sampler\": \"greedy\",\n            \"weights\": \"bf16\",\n        },\n        \"articles_per_hour\": round(len(rows) / wall * 3600),\n        \"prefill_tokens_per_second\": sum(s.prompt_tps for s in stats) / len(stats),\n        \"generation_tokens_per_second\": sum(s.generation_tps for s in stats)\n        / len(stats),\n        \"peak_memory_gb\": max(s.peak_memory for s in stats),\n        \"answers\": answers,\n    }\n\n    for size in (4, 8):\n        started = time.time()\n        done = []\n        for i in range(0, len(prompts), size):\n            done += batch_generate(\n                model,\n                tokenizer,\n                prompts[i : i + size],\n                max_tokens=MAX_TOKENS,\n                sampler=greedy,\n            ).texts\n        wall = time.time() - started\n        found[f\"batched {size}\"] = {\n            \"settings\": {\n                \"batch\": size,\n                \"prompt\": \"short\",\n                \"sampler\": \"greedy\",\n                \"weights\": \"bf16\",\n            },\n            \"articles_per_hour\": round(len(rows) / wall * 3600),\n        }\n\n    # the long prompt's shared prefix, its 779 instruction tokens, read once and reused: what a\n    # prompt cache buys, on ten articles, against reading the whole prompt each time\n    import copy\n\n    from teacher import INSTRUCTIONS\n\n    head = rendered(INSTRUCTIONS, \"\")\n    prefix = tokenizer.encode(\n        head[: head.index(\"<|im_start|>user\")], add_special_tokens=False\n    )\n    longs = [\n        tokenizer.encode(\n            rendered(INSTRUCTIONS, article_text(r)), add_special_tokens=False\n        )\n        for r in rows[:10]\n    ]\n    timings = {}\n    for cached in (False, True):\n        base = None\n        if cached:\n            base = make_prompt_cache(model)\n            for _ in stream_generate(\n                model,\n                tokenizer,\n                prefix,\n                max_tokens=1,\n                sampler=greedy,\n                prompt_cache=base,\n            ):\n                pass\n        started = time.time()\n        for ids in longs:\n            cache = copy.deepcopy(base) if cached else None\n            rest = ids[len(prefix) :] if cached else ids\n            for _ in stream_generate(\n                model, tokenizer, rest, max_tokens=1, sampler=greedy, prompt_cache=cache\n            ):\n                pass\n        timings[\"cached\" if cached else \"uncached\"] = (time.time() - started) / len(\n            longs\n        )\n    found[\"long prompt prefix\"] = {\n        \"settings\": {\n            \"prefix_tokens\": len(prefix),\n            \"articles\": len(longs),\n            \"max_tokens\": 1,\n        },\n        \"prefill_seconds_per_article\": timings,\n    }\n    return found\n\n\ndef agree(found: dict) -> dict:\n    ollama_answers = found[\"ollama\"][\"num_ctx 8192\"][\"answers\"]\n    mlx_answers = found[\"mlx\"][\"one at a time\"][\"answers\"]\n    kinds = [\n        ((parsed(a) or {}).get(\"kind\"), (parsed(b) or {}).get(\"kind\"))\n        for a, b in zip(ollama_answers, mlx_answers, strict=True)\n    ]\n    return {\n        \"articles\": len(kinds),\n        \"same_kind\": sum(a == b for a, b in kinds),\n        \"both_parse\": sum(a is not None and b is not None for a, b in kinds),\n        \"same_json\": sum(\n            (parsed(a) or {}) == (parsed(b) or {})\n            for a, b in zip(ollama_answers, mlx_answers, strict=True)\n        ),\n    }\n\n\ndef main(runs: list) -> None:\n    rows = sample_rows()\n    found = json.loads(RESULT.read_text()) if RESULT.exists() else {}\n    if \"ollama\" in runs:\n        found[\"ollama\"] = ollama(rows)\n    if \"mlx\" in runs:\n        found[\"mlx\"] = mlx(rows)\n    if \"agree\" in runs:\n        found[\"agree\"] = agree(found)\n    RESULT.write_text(json.dumps(found, indent=1) + \"\\n\")\n    print(\n        json.dumps(\n            {\n                k: {\n                    m: {x: y for x, y in v.items() if x != \"answers\"}\n                    for m, v in part.items()\n                }\n                if k != \"agree\"\n                else part\n                for k, part in found.items()\n            },\n            indent=1,\n            default=str,\n        )\n    )\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main(sys.argv[1:] or [\"ollama\", \"mlx\", \"agree\"])\n","numLines":242,"startLine":1,"totalLines":242}},"displayPath":"scripts/runtime_check.py"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"23768aa5-a3d1-4726-9d6d-3248857c2d2d","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:59:15.023Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/scripts/runtime_check.py\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t\"\"\"Why local prefill is slow, and which runtime the full pass should use (2C.3).\n2\t\n3\tOn the credit check's seeded 50 with the student's short prompt:\n4\t  ollama    one request at a time at num_ctx 2048 and 8192, with Ollama's own load_duration and\n5\t            prompt_eval_duration, so reloads and context allocation show apart from compute\n6\t  mlx       mlx-lm directly on the downloaded Qwen3.5-4B weights: prefill and generation tokens\n7\t            a second one article at a time, batched generation, and a prompt cache reused for\n8\t            the instruction prefix the articles share\n9\t  agree     the kind and the JSON the two runtimes give each article, greedy, compared\n10\tWrites eval/results/phase2c/runtime_check.json, one key per mode, each with its settings.\n11\t\"\"\"\n12\t\n13\timport json\n14\timport sys\n15\timport time\n16\t\n17\timport httpx\n18\tfrom credit_check import RESULT as CREDIT\n19\tfrom credit_check import rows_of\n20\tfrom label_gold import ROOT\n21\tfrom local_throughput import SHORT\n22\tfrom teacher import article_text, parsed, rendered\n23\t\n24\tRESULT = ROOT / \"eval\" / \"results\" / \"phase2c\" / \"runtime_check.json\"\n25\tOLLAMA = \"http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/generate\"\n26\tMODEL = \"Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B\"\n27\tMAX_TOKENS = 700\n28\t\n29\t\n30\tdef sample_rows() -> list:\n31\t    picked = json.loads(CREDIT.read_text())[\"sample\"]\n32\t    rows = rows_of(set(picked))\n33\t    return [rows[aid] for aid in picked]\n34\t\n35\t\n36\tdef ollama(rows: list) -> dict:\n37\t    found = {}\n38\t    for ctx in (2048, 8192):\n39\t        out = []\n40\t        for row in rows:\n41\t            body = {\n42\t                \"model\": \"qwen3.5:4b\",\n43\t                \"prompt\": rendered(SHORT, article_text(row)),\n44\t                \"raw\": True,\n45\t                \"stream\": False,\n46\t                \"keep_alive\": \"30m\",\n47\t                \"options\": {\n48\t                    \"temperature\": 0,\n49\t                    \"num_predict\": MAX_TOKENS,\n50\t                    \"num_ctx\": ctx,\n51\t                    \"stop\": [\"<|im_end|>\"],\n52\t                },\n53\t            }\n54\t            a = httpx.post(OLLAMA, json=body, timeout=600).json()\n55\t            out.append(a)\n56\t        n = len(out)\n57\t        found[f\"num_ctx {ctx}\"] = {\n58\t            \"settings\": {\n59\t                \"num_ctx\": ctx,\n60\t                \"concurrent\": 1,\n61\t                \"keep_alive\": \"30m\",\n62\t                \"prompt\": \"short\",\n63\t            },\n64\t            \"load_seconds\": sum(a.get(\"load_duration\", 0) for a in out) / n / 1e9,\n65\t            \"prompt_seconds\": sum(a.get(\"prompt_eval_duration\", 0) for a in out)\n66\t            / n\n67\t            / 1e9,\n68\t            \"prompt_tokens\": sum(a.get(\"prompt_eval_count\", 0) for a in out) / n,\n69\t            \"generation_seconds\": sum(a.get(\"eval_duration\", 0) for a in out) / n / 1e9,\n70\t            \"output_tokens\": sum(a.get(\"eval_count\", 0) for a in out) / n,\n71\t            \"total_seconds\": sum(a.get(\"total_duration\", 0) for a in out) / n / 1e9,\n72\t            \"answers\": [a.get(\"response\", \"\") for a in out],\n73\t        }\n74\t        f = found[f\"num_ctx {ctx}\"]\n75\t        f[\"prefill_tokens_per_second\"] = f[\"prompt_tokens\"] / max(\n76\t            f[\"prompt_seconds\"], 1e-9\n77\t        )\n78\t    return found\n79\t\n80\t\n81\tdef mlx(rows: list) -> dict:\n82\t    from mlx_lm import batch_generate, load, stream_generate\n83\t    from mlx_lm.models.cache import make_prompt_cache\n84\t    from mlx_lm.sample_utils import make_sampler\n85\t\n86\t    model, tokenizer = load(MODEL)\n87\t    greedy = make_sampler(temp=0.0)\n88\t    prompts = [\n89\t        tokenizer.encode(rendered(SHORT, article_text(r)), add_special_tokens=False)\n90\t        for r in rows\n91\t    ]\n92\t    found = {}\n93\t\n94\t    started, answers, stats = time.time(), [], []\n95\t    for ids in prompts:\n96\t        text, last = \"\", None\n97\t        for last in stream_generate(\n98\t            model, tokenizer, ids, max_tokens=MAX_TOKENS, sampler=greedy\n99\t        ):\n100\t            text += last.text\n101\t            if \"<|im_end|>\" in text:\n102\t                break\n103\t        answers.append(text.split(\"<|im_end|>\")[0])\n104\t        stats.append(last)\n105\t    wall = time.time() - started\n106\t    found[\"one at a time\"] = {\n107\t        \"settings\": {\n108\t            \"concurrent\": 1,\n109\t            \"prompt\": \"short\",\n110\t            \"sampler\": \"greedy\",\n111\t            \"weights\": \"bf16\",\n112\t        },\n113\t        \"articles_per_hour\": round(len(rows) / wall * 3600),\n114\t        \"prefill_tokens_per_second\": sum(s.prompt_tps for s in stats) / len(stats),\n115\t        \"generation_tokens_per_second\": sum(s.generation_tps for s in stats)\n116\t        / len(stats),\n117\t        \"peak_memory_gb\": max(s.peak_memory for s in stats),\n118\t        \"answers\": answers,\n119\t    }\n120\t\n121\t    for size in (4, 8):\n122\t        started = time.time()\n123\t        done = []\n124\t        for i in range(0, len(prompts), size):\n125\t            done += batch_generate(\n126\t                model,\n127\t                tokenizer,\n128\t                prompts[i : i + size],\n129\t                max_tokens=MAX_TOKENS,\n130\t                sampler=greedy,\n131\t            ).texts\n132\t        wall = time.time() - started\n133\t        found[f\"batched {size}\"] = {\n134\t            \"settings\": {\n135\t                \"batch\": size,\n136\t                \"prompt\": \"short\",\n137\t                \"sampler\": \"greedy\",\n138\t                \"weights\": \"bf16\",\n139\t            },\n140\t            \"articles_per_hour\": round(len(rows) / wall * 3600),\n141\t        }\n142\t\n143\t    # the long prompt's shared prefix, its 779 instruction tokens, read once and reused: what a\n144\t    # prompt cache buys, on ten articles, against reading the whole prompt each time\n145\t    import copy\n146\t\n147\t    from teacher import INSTRUCTIONS\n148\t\n149\t    head = rendered(INSTRUCTIONS, \"\")\n150\t    prefix = tokenizer.encode(\n151\t        head[: head.index(\"<|im_start|>user\")], add_special_tokens=False\n152\t    )\n153\t    longs = [\n154\t        tokenizer.encode(\n155\t            rendered(INSTRUCTIONS, article_text(r)), add_special_tokens=False\n156\t        )\n157\t        for r in rows[:10]\n158\t    ]\n159\t    timings = {}\n160\t    for cached in (False, True):\n161\t        base = None\n162\t        if cached:\n163\t            base = make_prompt_cache(model)\n164\t            for _ in stream_generate(\n165\t                model,\n166\t                tokenizer,\n167\t                prefix,\n168\t                max_tokens=1,\n169\t                sampler=greedy,\n170\t                prompt_cache=base,\n171\t            ):\n172\t                pass\n173\t        started = time.time()\n174\t        for ids in longs:\n175\t            cache = copy.deepcopy(base) if cached else None\n176\t            rest = ids[len(prefix) :] if cached else ids\n177\t            for _ in stream_generate(\n178\t                model, tokenizer, rest, max_tokens=1, sampler=greedy, prompt_cache=cache\n179\t            ):\n180\t                pass\n181\t        timings[\"cached\" if cached else \"uncached\"] = (time.time() - started) / len(\n182\t            longs\n183\t        )\n184\t    found[\"long prompt prefix\"] = {\n185\t        \"settings\": {\n186\t            \"prefix_tokens\": len(prefix),\n187\t            \"articles\": len(longs),\n188\t            \"max_tokens\": 1,\n189\t        },\n190\t        \"prefill_seconds_per_article\": timings,\n191\t    }\n192\t    return found\n193\t\n194\t\n195\tdef agree(found: dict) -> dict:\n196\t    ollama_answers = found[\"ollama\"][\"num_ctx 8192\"][\"answers\"]\n197\t    mlx_answers = found[\"mlx\"][\"one at a time\"][\"answers\"]\n198\t    kinds = [\n199\t        ((parsed(a) or {}).get(\"kind\"), (parsed(b) or {}).get(\"kind\"))\n200\t        for a, b in zip(ollama_answers, mlx_answers, strict=True)\n201\t    ]\n202\t    return {\n203\t        \"articles\": len(kinds),\n204\t        \"same_kind\": sum(a == b for a, b in kinds),\n205\t        \"both_parse\": sum(a is not None and b is not None for a, b in kinds),\n206\t        \"same_json\": sum(\n207\t            (parsed(a) or {}) == (parsed(b) or {})\n208\t            for a, b in zip(ollama_answers, mlx_answers, strict=True)\n209\t        ),\n210\t    }\n211\t\n212\t\n213\tdef main(runs: list) -> None:\n214\t    rows = sample_rows()\n215\t    found = json.loads(RESULT.read_text()) if RESULT.exists() else {}\n216\t    if \"ollama\" in runs:\n217\t        found[\"ollama\"] = ollama(rows)\n218\t    if \"mlx\" in runs:\n219\t        found[\"mlx\"] = mlx(rows)\n220\t    if \"agree\" in runs:\n221\t        found[\"agree\"] = agree(found)\n222\t    RESULT.write_text(json.dumps(found, indent=1) + \"\\n\")\n223\t    print(\n224\t        json.dumps(\n225\t            {\n226\t                k: {\n227\t                    m: {x: y for x, y in v.items() if x != \"answers\"}\n228\t                    for m, v in part.items()\n229\t                }\n230\t                if k != \"agree\"\n231\t                else part\n232\t                for k, part in found.items()\n233\t            },\n234\t            indent=1,\n235\t            default=str,\n236\t        )\n237\t    )\n238\t\n239\t\n240\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n241\t    main(sys.argv[1:] or [\"ollama\", \"mlx\", \"agree\"])\n242\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"23768aa5-a3d1-4726-9d6d-3248857c2d2d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"compact_file_reference","filename":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md","displayPath":"Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"be936fff-98aa-4478-8c26-4a61e2ef1c0a","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:59:15.023Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"be936fff-98aa-4478-8c26-4a61e2ef1c0a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/scripts/local_teacher.py","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/scripts/local_teacher.py","content":"\"\"\"A local teacher on this Mac (2C.3), at no cost: the largest model that runs at a usable speed,\nread through the local Ollama server with the teacher's full prompt (round 3's instructions\nand POLICY.md).\n\n  throughput MODEL     the credit check's seeded 50 at 1 and 2 requests at once, into\n                       eval/results/phase2c/local_teacher.json\n  dev MODEL ROUND [think]   all 150 dev articles, one at a time so the server can reuse the\n                       policy prefix, saved as data/teacher/dev_ROUND.jsonl in the dev round's\n                       own format, then scored by teacher.dev_round from that file, so no Tinker\n                       call is made\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nfrom datetime import UTC, datetime\n\nimport httpx\nfrom credit_check import RESULT as CREDIT\nfrom credit_check import rows_of\nfrom label_gold import ROOT\nfrom teacher import article_text, final, prompt_sha256, system_prompt\n\nURL = \"http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat\"\nRESULT = ROOT / \"eval\" / \"results\" / \"phase2c\" / \"local_teacher.json\"\nCANDIDATES = 1_236_122\n\n\ndef one(row: dict, model: str, system: str, think: bool = False) -> dict:\n    body = {\n        \"model\": model,\n        \"messages\": [\n            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": system},\n            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": article_text(row)},\n        ],\n        \"stream\": False,\n        \"think\": think,\n        \"options\": {\"temperature\": 0, \"num_predict\": 4096, \"num_ctx\": 16384},\n    }\n    answer = httpx.post(URL, json=body, timeout=1800).json()\n    return {\n        \"article_id\": row[\"article_id\"],\n        \"answer\": final(answer.get(\"message\", {}).get(\"content\", \"\")),\n        \"prompt_tokens\": answer.get(\"prompt_eval_count\", 0),\n        \"output_tokens\": answer.get(\"eval_count\", 0),\n        \"hit_limit\": int(answer.get(\"eval_count\", 0) >= 4096),\n        \"model\": model,\n        \"thinking\": think,\n        \"thinking_chars\": len(answer.get(\"message\", {}).get(\"thinking\") or \"\"),\n        \"seconds\": answer.get(\"total_duration\", 0) / 1e9,\n        \"prompt_seconds\": answer.get(\"prompt_eval_duration\", 0) / 1e9,\n        \"prompt_sha256\": prompt_sha256(system),\n        \"at\": datetime.now(UTC).isoformat(timespec=\"seconds\"),\n    }\n\n\ndef timed(\n    rows: list, model: str, system: str, workers: int, think: bool = False\n) -> tuple[dict, list]:\n    started = time.time()\n    with ThreadPoolExecutor(workers) as pool:\n        out = list(pool.map(lambda r: one(r, model, system, think), rows))\n    wall = time.time() - started\n    per_hour = len(rows) / wall * 3600\n    return {\n        \"concurrent\": workers,\n        \"wall_seconds\": round(wall, 1),\n        \"articles_per_hour\": round(per_hour),\n        \"prompt_tokens\": sum(o[\"prompt_tokens\"] for o in out),\n        \"output_tokens\": sum(o[\"output_tokens\"] for o in out),\n        \"draw_of_3000_hours\": round(3000 / per_hour, 1),\n        \"prompt_seconds_per_article\": round(\n            sum(o[\"prompt_seconds\"] for o in out) / len(out), 2\n        ),\n    }, out\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    run, model, *rest = sys.argv[1:]\n    system = system_prompt()\n    if run == \"throughput\":\n        picked = json.loads(CREDIT.read_text())[\"sample\"]\n        rows = rows_of(set(picked))\n        rows = [rows[aid] for aid in picked]\n        one(rows[0], model, system)  # load the model before timing\n        found = json.loads(RESULT.read_text()) if RESULT.exists() else {}\n        found[model] = [timed(rows, model, system, workers)[0] for workers in (1, 2)]\n        RESULT.write_text(json.dumps(found, indent=1) + \"\\n\")\n        print(json.dumps(found[model], indent=1))\n    elif run == \"dev\":\n        from label_gold import articles\n        from teacher import dev_round\n\n        round_name, think = rest[0], \"think\" in rest[1:]\n        rows = {aid: r for aid, r in articles().items() if r[\"split\"] == \"dev\"}\n        timing, out = timed([rows[a] for a in sorted(rows)], model, system, 1, think)\n        found = json.loads(RESULT.read_text()) if RESULT.exists() else {}\n        found[round_name] = timing | {\n            \"model\": model,\n            \"thinking\": think,\n            \"articles\": len(out),\n        }\n        RESULT.write_text(json.dumps(found, indent=1) + \"\\n\")\n        raw = ROOT / \"data\" / \"teacher\" / f\"dev_{round_name}.jsonl\"\n        raw.write_text(\"\".join(json.dumps(o) + \"\\n\" for o in out))\n        found = dev_round(\n            round_name, model=model\n        )  # scored from the saved file: no Tinker call\n        print(\n            json.dumps(\n                {\n                    k: found[k]\n                    for k in (\"model\", \"report_recall\", \"unparsed\", \"hit_limit\")\n                },\n                indent=1,\n                default=str,\n            )\n        )\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n","numLines":124,"startLine":1,"totalLines":124}},"displayPath":"scripts/local_teacher.py"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b0ddcb47-eff8-44ce-8447-8edeb85a1221","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:59:15.023Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/scripts/local_teacher.py\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t\"\"\"A local teacher on this Mac (2C.3), at no cost: the largest model that runs at a usable speed,\n2\tread through the local Ollama server with the teacher's full prompt (round 3's instructions\n3\tand POLICY.md).\n4\t\n5\t  throughput MODEL     the credit check's seeded 50 at 1 and 2 requests at once, into\n6\t                       eval/results/phase2c/local_teacher.json\n7\t  dev MODEL ROUND [think]   all 150 dev articles, one at a time so the server can reuse the\n8\t                       policy prefix, saved as data/teacher/dev_ROUND.jsonl in the dev round's\n9\t                       own format, then scored by teacher.dev_round from that file, so no Tinker\n10\t                       call is made\n11\t\"\"\"\n12\t\n13\timport json\n14\timport sys\n15\timport time\n16\tfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\n17\tfrom datetime import UTC, datetime\n18\t\n19\timport httpx\n20\tfrom credit_check import RESULT as CREDIT\n21\tfrom credit_check import rows_of\n22\tfrom label_gold import ROOT\n23\tfrom teacher import article_text, final, prompt_sha256, system_prompt\n24\t\n25\tURL = \"http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat\"\n26\tRESULT = ROOT / \"eval\" / \"results\" / \"phase2c\" / \"local_teacher.json\"\n27\tCANDIDATES = 1_236_122\n28\t\n29\t\n30\tdef one(row: dict, model: str, system: str, think: bool = False) -> dict:\n31\t    body = {\n32\t        \"model\": model,\n33\t        \"messages\": [\n34\t            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": system},\n35\t            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": article_text(row)},\n36\t        ],\n37\t        \"stream\": False,\n38\t        \"think\": think,\n39\t        \"options\": {\"temperature\": 0, \"num_predict\": 4096, \"num_ctx\": 16384},\n40\t    }\n41\t    answer = httpx.post(URL, json=body, timeout=1800).json()\n42\t    return {\n43\t        \"article_id\": row[\"article_id\"],\n44\t        \"answer\": final(answer.get(\"message\", {}).get(\"content\", \"\")),\n45\t        \"prompt_tokens\": answer.get(\"prompt_eval_count\", 0),\n46\t        \"output_tokens\": answer.get(\"eval_count\", 0),\n47\t        \"hit_limit\": int(answer.get(\"eval_count\", 0) >= 4096),\n48\t        \"model\": model,\n49\t        \"thinking\": think,\n50\t        \"thinking_chars\": len(answer.get(\"message\", {}).get(\"thinking\") or \"\"),\n51\t        \"seconds\": answer.get(\"total_duration\", 0) / 1e9,\n52\t        \"prompt_seconds\": answer.get(\"prompt_eval_duration\", 0) / 1e9,\n53\t        \"prompt_sha256\": prompt_sha256(system),\n54\t        \"at\": datetime.now(UTC).isoformat(timespec=\"seconds\"),\n55\t    }\n56\t\n57\t\n58\tdef timed(\n59\t    rows: list, model: str, system: str, workers: int, think: bool = False\n60\t) -> tuple[dict, list]:\n61\t    started = time.time()\n62\t    with ThreadPoolExecutor(workers) as pool:\n63\t        out = list(pool.map(lambda r: one(r, model, system, think), rows))\n64\t    wall = time.time() - started\n65\t    per_hour = len(rows) / wall * 3600\n66\t    return {\n67\t        \"concurrent\": workers,\n68\t        \"wall_seconds\": round(wall, 1),\n69\t        \"articles_per_hour\": round(per_hour),\n70\t        \"prompt_tokens\": sum(o[\"prompt_tokens\"] for o in out),\n71\t        \"output_tokens\": sum(o[\"output_tokens\"] for o in out),\n72\t        \"draw_of_3000_hours\": round(3000 / per_hour, 1),\n73\t        \"prompt_seconds_per_article\": round(\n74\t            sum(o[\"prompt_seconds\"] for o in out) / len(out), 2\n75\t        ),\n76\t    }, out\n77\t\n78\t\n79\tdef main() -> None:\n80\t    run, model, *rest = sys.argv[1:]\n81\t    system = system_prompt()\n82\t    if run == \"throughput\":\n83\t        picked = json.loads(CREDIT.read_text())[\"sample\"]\n84\t        rows = rows_of(set(picked))\n85\t        rows = [rows[aid] for aid in picked]\n86\t        one(rows[0], model, system)  # load the model before timing\n87\t        found = json.loads(RESULT.read_text()) if RESULT.exists() else {}\n88\t        found[model] = [timed(rows, model, system, workers)[0] for workers in (1, 2)]\n89\t        RESULT.write_text(json.dumps(found, indent=1) + \"\\n\")\n90\t        print(json.dumps(found[model], indent=1))\n91\t    elif run == \"dev\":\n92\t        from label_gold import articles\n93\t        from teacher import dev_round\n94\t\n95\t        round_name, think = rest[0], \"think\" in rest[1:]\n96\t        rows = {aid: r for aid, r in articles().items() if r[\"split\"] == \"dev\"}\n97\t        timing, out = timed([rows[a] for a in sorted(rows)], model, system, 1, think)\n98\t        found = json.loads(RESULT.read_text()) if RESULT.exists() else {}\n99\t        found[round_name] = timing | {\n100\t            \"model\": model,\n101\t            \"thinking\": think,\n102\t            \"articles\": len(out),\n103\t        }\n104\t        RESULT.write_text(json.dumps(found, indent=1) + \"\\n\")\n105\t        raw = ROOT / \"data\" / \"teacher\" / f\"dev_{round_name}.jsonl\"\n106\t        raw.write_text(\"\".join(json.dumps(o) + \"\\n\" for o in out))\n107\t        found = dev_round(\n108\t            round_name, model=model\n109\t        )  # scored from the saved file: no Tinker call\n110\t        print(\n111\t            json.dumps(\n112\t                {\n113\t                    k: found[k]\n114\t                    for k in (\"model\", \"report_recall\", \"unparsed\", \"hit_limit\")\n115\t                },\n116\t                indent=1,\n117\t                default=str,\n118\t            )\n119\t        )\n120\t\n121\t\n122\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n123\t    main()\n124\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"b0ddcb47-eff8-44ce-8447-8edeb85a1221","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/scripts/local_lora_timing.py","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/scripts/local_lora_timing.py","content":"\"\"\"Local LoRA training of Qwen3.5-4B with mlx-lm on this Mac (2C.3): time per epoch and peak memory.\n\nmlx-lm's own trainer runs a short LoRA on a timing set of seeded pool articles, each with the\nshort instruction and a placeholder answer of a teacher label's length; only lengths matter, so\nno teacher label and no dev or gold article is needed. Its log gives seconds per iteration,\ntokens per second and peak memory, and an epoch of 3,000 examples is projected from them. The\nadapter is thrown away. Writes eval/results/phase2c/local_lora_timing.json.\n\n  uv run --group local python scripts/local_lora_timing.py DATA_DIR [ITERS] [BATCH]\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport time\n\nfrom label_gold import ROOT\n\nMODEL = \"Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B\"\nRESULT = ROOT / \"eval\" / \"results\" / \"phase2c\" / \"local_lora_timing.json\"\nEXAMPLES = 3000\nLINE = re.compile(\n    r\"Iter (\\d+): Train loss [\\d.]+.*?It/sec ([\\d.]+).*?Tokens/sec ([\\d.]+).*?Peak mem ([\\d.]+) GB\"\n)\n\n\ndef main(data: str, iters: int = 40, batch: int = 4) -> None:\n    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as adapters:\n        started = time.time()\n        log = subprocess.run(\n            [\n                sys.executable,\n                \"-m\",\n                \"mlx_lm\",\n                \"lora\",\n                \"--model\",\n                MODEL,\n                \"--train\",\n                \"--data\",\n                data,\n                \"--iters\",\n                str(iters),\n                \"--batch-size\",\n                str(batch),\n                \"--num-layers\",\n                \"16\",\n                \"--max-seq-length\",\n                \"2048\",\n                \"--steps-per-report\",\n                \"10\",\n                \"--steps-per-eval\",\n                \"100000\",\n                \"--adapter-path\",\n                adapters,\n            ],\n            capture_output=True,\n            text=True,\n            check=False,\n        )\n        wall = time.time() - started\n    reports = [\n        tuple(map(float, m.groups())) for m in LINE.finditer(log.stdout + log.stderr)\n    ]\n    if not reports:\n        sys.exit(\n            \"no training report in mlx-lm's log:\\n\" + (log.stdout + log.stderr)[-2000:]\n        )\n    steady = reports[1:] or reports  # the first report includes the warm-up\n    it_per_sec = sum(r[1] for r in steady) / len(steady)\n    epoch = EXAMPLES / batch / it_per_sec\n    found = {\n        \"model\": MODEL,\n        \"iterations\": iters,\n        \"batch\": batch,\n        \"lora_layers\": 16,\n        \"wall_seconds\": round(wall, 1),\n        \"iterations_per_second\": round(it_per_sec, 3),\n        \"tokens_per_second\": round(sum(r[2] for r in steady) / len(steady)),\n        \"peak_memory_gb\": max(r[3] for r in reports),\n        \"epoch_of_3000_hours\": round(epoch / 3600, 2),\n        \"reports\": reports,\n    }\n    RESULT.write_text(json.dumps(found, indent=1) + \"\\n\")\n    print(json.dumps({k: v for k, v in found.items() if k != \"reports\"}, indent=1))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main(sys.argv[1], *map(int, sys.argv[2:]))\n","numLines":91,"startLine":1,"totalLines":91}},"displayPath":"scripts/local_lora_timing.py"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ae3d40b9-b991-4f75-940c-9735b0c76dcc","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:59:15.024Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/scripts/local_lora_timing.py\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t\"\"\"Local LoRA training of Qwen3.5-4B with mlx-lm on this Mac (2C.3): time per epoch and peak memory.\n2\t\n3\tmlx-lm's own trainer runs a short LoRA on a timing set of seeded pool articles, each with the\n4\tshort instruction and a placeholder answer of a teacher label's length; only lengths matter, so\n5\tno teacher label and no dev or gold article is needed. Its log gives seconds per iteration,\n6\ttokens per second and peak memory, and an epoch of 3,000 examples is projected from them. The\n7\tadapter is thrown away. Writes eval/results/phase2c/local_lora_timing.json.\n8\t\n9\t  uv run --group local python scripts/local_lora_timing.py DATA_DIR [ITERS] [BATCH]\n10\t\"\"\"\n11\t\n12\timport json\n13\timport re\n14\timport subprocess\n15\timport sys\n16\timport tempfile\n17\timport time\n18\t\n19\tfrom label_gold import ROOT\n20\t\n21\tMODEL = \"Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B\"\n22\tRESULT = ROOT / \"eval\" / \"results\" / \"phase2c\" / \"local_lora_timing.json\"\n23\tEXAMPLES = 3000\n24\tLINE = re.compile(\n25\t    r\"Iter (\\d+): Train loss [\\d.]+.*?It/sec ([\\d.]+).*?Tokens/sec ([\\d.]+).*?Peak mem ([\\d.]+) GB\"\n26\t)\n27\t\n28\t\n29\tdef main(data: str, iters: int = 40, batch: int = 4) -> None:\n30\t    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as adapters:\n31\t        started = time.time()\n32\t        log = subprocess.run(\n33\t            [\n34\t                sys.executable,\n35\t                \"-m\",\n36\t                \"mlx_lm\",\n37\t                \"lora\",\n38\t                \"--model\",\n39\t                MODEL,\n40\t                \"--train\",\n41\t                \"--data\",\n42\t                data,\n43\t                \"--iters\",\n44\t                str(iters),\n45\t                \"--batch-size\",\n46\t                str(batch),\n47\t                \"--num-layers\",\n48\t                \"16\",\n49\t                \"--max-seq-length\",\n50\t                \"2048\",\n51\t                \"--steps-per-report\",\n52\t                \"10\",\n53\t                \"--steps-per-eval\",\n54\t                \"100000\",\n55\t                \"--adapter-path\",\n56\t                adapters,\n57\t            ],\n58\t            capture_output=True,\n59\t            text=True,\n60\t            check=False,\n61\t        )\n62\t        wall = time.time() - started\n63\t    reports = [\n64\t        tuple(map(float, m.groups())) for m in LINE.finditer(log.stdout + log.stderr)\n65\t    ]\n66\t    if not reports:\n67\t        sys.exit(\n68\t            \"no training report in mlx-lm's log:\\n\" + (log.stdout + log.stderr)[-2000:]\n69\t        )\n70\t    steady = reports[1:] or reports  # the first report includes the warm-up\n71\t    it_per_sec = sum(r[1] for r in steady) / len(steady)\n72\t    epoch = EXAMPLES / batch / it_per_sec\n73\t    found = {\n74\t        \"model\": MODEL,\n75\t        \"iterations\": iters,\n76\t        \"batch\": batch,\n77\t        \"lora_layers\": 16,\n78\t        \"wall_seconds\": round(wall, 1),\n79\t        \"iterations_per_second\": round(it_per_sec, 3),\n80\t        \"tokens_per_second\": round(sum(r[2] for r in steady) / len(steady)),\n81\t        \"peak_memory_gb\": max(r[3] for r in reports),\n82\t        \"epoch_of_3000_hours\": round(epoch / 3600, 2),\n83\t        \"reports\": reports,\n84\t    }\n85\t    RESULT.write_text(json.dumps(found, indent=1) + \"\\n\")\n86\t    print(json.dumps({k: v for k, v in found.items() if k != \"reports\"}, indent=1))\n87\t\n88\t\n89\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n90\t    main(sys.argv[1], *map(int, sys.argv[2:]))\n91\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
