{"parentUuid":"ea49bc23-d126-4555-9c2c-fef608cf9c39","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"961e3d1a-ef11-4fb3-9157-154d4dc357e8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BHECtvhWHohiLHXVmWikGT","type":"tool_result","content":"            temperature=temperature,\n        )\n        raw.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        raw.write_text(\"\".join(json.dumps(o) + \"\\n\" for o in out))\n    answers, unparsed = {}, []\n    for o in out:\n        label = (\n            (voted(o[\"answers\"]) if samples > 1 else parsed(o.get(\"answer\") or \"\"))\n            if o and \"error\" not in o\n            else None\n        )\n        if label is None:\n            unparsed.append(o[\"article_id\"] if o else None)\n            label = {\n                \"kind\": \"other\",\n                \"kind_quote\": \"\",\n            }  # no answer: scored as a miss, never kept\n        answers[o[\"article_id\"]] = {\n            \"article_id\": o[\"article_id\"],\n            \"people\": [],\n            **label,\n        }\n    calibration = calibrated(answers, labels, texts)\n    kept = {\n        aid: {**verified(a, texts[aid], calibration[\"threshold\"])[0], \"article_id\": aid}\n        for aid, a in answers.items()\n    }\n    pairs = [(labels[aid], kept[aid]) for aid in sorted(kept)]\n    raw_pairs = [(labels[aid], answers[aid]) for aid in sorted(answers)]\n    found = {\n        \"round\": round_name,\n        \"model\": model,\n        \"thinking\": thinking,\n        \"samples\": samples,\n        \"temperature\": temperature,\n        \"max_tokens\": max_tokens,\n        \"hit_limit\": sum(o.get(\"hit_limit\", 0) for o in out if o),\n        \"errors\": sum(1 for o in out if not o or \"error\" in o),\n        \"report_recall\": recall(labels, kept),\n        \"prompt_sha256\": prompt_sha256(system),\n        \"articles\": len(out),\n        \"unparsed\": unparsed,\n        \"prompt_tokens\": sum(o.get(\"prompt_tokens\", 0) for o in out if o),\n        \"output_tokens\": sum(o.get(\"output_tokens\", 0) for o in out if o),\n        \"accuracy_verified\": agreed(pairs, texts),\n        \"accuracy_unverified\": agreed(raw_pairs, texts),\n        \"verifier\": calibration,\n    }\n    (RESULTS / f\"teacher_dev_{round_name}.json\").write_text(\n        json.dumps(found, indent=1) + \"\\n\"\n    )\n    return found\n\n\ndef confusion(round_name: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"The dev label's kind against the teacher's, from a round's saved answers.\"\"\"\n    from label_gold import OUT, saved\n\n    labels = {r[\"article_id\"]: r[\"kind\"] for r in saved(OUT[\"dev\"])}\n    found = {}\n    for line in (\n        (ROOT / \"data\" / \"teacher\" / f\"dev_{round_name}.jsonl\").read_text().splitlines()\n    ):\n        answer = json.loads(line)\n        label = parsed(answer.get(\"answer\") or \"\")\n        row = found.setdefault(labels[answer[\"article_id\"]], {})\n        kind = label[\"kind\"] if label else \"unparsed\"\n        row[kind] = row.get(kind, 0) + 1\n    return found\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    run, *rest = sys.argv[1:]\n    if run == \"confusion\":\n        found = {r: confusion(r) for r in rest}\n        (RESULTS / \"teacher_confusion.json\").write_text(\n            json.dumps(found, indent=1) + \"\\n\"\n        )\n        for r, m in found.items():\n            print(r, \"rows: dev label; columns: teacher\")\n            for label, row in sorted(m.items()):\n## Fields, for reports only\n\n- **Every value carries a quote:** the shortest exact span of the OCR text that states it, copied as it is, OCR errors and all.\n- **A value the text doesn't state is left empty,** which means \"not stated\". It is never inferred.\n\n| Field | What it holds |\n|---|---|\n| `place` | Where the experience happened, as the text names it: \"the old Hale farmhouse at Milford\". |\n| `place_state` | The state of that place, from the text or from its dateline. Gold uses it to measure the story-place rule, and the reader isn't asked for it. |\n| `people` | Each person who saw, heard, felt or claimed it, by name if the text names them, or as the text describes them (\"the family\", \"two boys\"). At a séance, the medium and the sitters the text names are people. |\n| `seen` | What was seen, heard or felt, as the text says it: \"knockings upon the walls\". |\n| `outcome` | One of four values, set out below. |\n| `specific_place` | For walks: the building, house, road or spot, if the text names one. |\n| `place_type` | For walks: `house`, `church`, `cemetery`, `inn_or_hotel`, `road_or_bridge`, `public_building`, `ship` or `other`, the schema's values. |\n| `precision` | For walks: `town` if only a town is given, `street` for a street or road, `building` for a particular building or spot. |\n\n**The four outcomes:**\n- `explained`: the text gives a natural cause, such as a trapped man, rats, a reflection or a delusion.\n- `hoax`: the text says someone deliberately deceived, such as fraud exposed or a prankster caught.\n- `unexplained`: the text says no cause was found, or that it remains a mystery after a search.\n- `unknown`: the text tells the claim and no more. Its quote is the sentence the account ends on.\n\n**The story-place rule:**\n- A town alone takes its state from the text: a county or state the text gives, or the dateline.\n- Otherwise `place_state` stays empty.\n- It is never taken from the paper's place or state. That guess put 2 of decision 34's 9 town-only places wrong.\n\n## The label record\n\nLabels are saved one JSON object per article, in `eval/gold/labels.jsonl` and `eval/gold/dev_labels.jsonl`, with these keys:\n- `article_id`, `kind`, and `kind_quote` (the span that shows the kind)\n139:def same(name: str, a: dict, b: dict, text: str) -> bool:\n140-    \"\"\"Whether the two passes agree on one field of a report; the module's docstring says how.\"\"\"\n141-    if name == \"people\":\n142-        first, second = a.get(\"people\") or [], b.get(\"people\") or []\n143-        return all(any(overlap(p, q, text) for q in second) for p in first) and all(\n144-            any(overlap(q, p, text) for p in first) for q in second\n145-        )\n146-    x, y = a.get(name), b.get(name)\n147-    if not x or not y:\n148-        return not x and not y\n149-    return x[\"value\"] == y[\"value\"] if name in VALUES else overlap(x, y, text)\n150-\n151-\n152-def rate(agree: int, n: int) -> dict:\n153-    return {\"agree\": agree, \"n\": n, \"rate\": agree / n, \"interval\": wilson(agree, n)}\n154-\n155-\n156:def agreed(pairs: list, texts: dict) -> dict:\n157-    \"\"\"Kind, report-or-not and each field, on the pairs both passes call reports.\"\"\"\n158-    kinds = [(a[\"kind\"], b[\"kind\"]) for a, b in pairs]\n159-    reports = [(a[\"kind\"] == \"report\", b[\"kind\"] == \"report\") for a, b in pairs]\n160-    both = [(a, b) for a, b in pairs if a[\"kind\"] == b[\"kind\"] == \"report\"]\n161-    found = {\"n\": len(pairs)}\n162-    for name, values in ((\"kind\", kinds), (\"report\", reports)):\n163-        first, second = [x for x, _ in values], [y for _, y in values]\n164-        found[name] = rate(sum(x == y for x, y in values), len(values)) | {\n165-            \"kappa\": kappa(first, second),\n166-            \"kappa_interval\": interval(first, second),\n167-        }\n168-    found[\"fields\"] = {\n169-        name: rate(\n170-            sum(same(name, a, b, texts[a[\"article_id\"]]) for a, b in both), len(both)\n171-        )\n172-        for name in (*FIELDS, \"people\")\n173-        if both\n174-    }\n175-    return found\n176-\n177-\n178-def disputes(pairs: list, texts: dict) -> list:\n179-    \"\"\"Each article the passes disagree on: its kinds, and the fields of a report both call one.\"\"\"\n180-    found = []\n181-    for a, b in pairs:\n182-        fields = (\n183-            [\n184-                name\n185-                for name in (*FIELDS, \"people\")\n186-                if not same(name, a, b, texts[a[\"article_id\"]])","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4bf5b6e5-aa1c-4a00-ad15-810d982c54d3","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:59:39.763Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"            temperature=temperature,\n        )\n        raw.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        raw.write_text(\"\".join(json.dumps(o) + \"\\n\" for o in out))\n    answers, unparsed = {}, []\n    for o in out:\n        label = (\n            (voted(o[\"answers\"]) if samples > 1 else parsed(o.get(\"answer\") or \"\"))\n            if o and \"error\" not in o\n            else None\n        )\n        if label is None:\n            unparsed.append(o[\"article_id\"] if o else None)\n            label = {\n                \"kind\": \"other\",\n                \"kind_quote\": \"\",\n            }  # no answer: scored as a miss, never kept\n        answers[o[\"article_id\"]] = {\n            \"article_id\": o[\"article_id\"],\n            \"people\": [],\n            **label,\n        }\n    calibration = calibrated(answers, labels, texts)\n    kept = {\n        aid: {**verified(a, texts[aid], calibration[\"threshold\"])[0], \"article_id\": aid}\n        for aid, a in answers.items()\n    }\n    pairs = [(labels[aid], kept[aid]) for aid in sorted(kept)]\n    raw_pairs = [(labels[aid], answers[aid]) for aid in sorted(answers)]\n    found = {\n        \"round\": round_name,\n        \"model\": model,\n        \"thinking\": thinking,\n        \"samples\": samples,\n        \"temperature\": temperature,\n        \"max_tokens\": max_tokens,\n        \"hit_limit\": sum(o.get(\"hit_limit\", 0) for o in out if o),\n        \"errors\": sum(1 for o in out if not o or \"error\" in o),\n        \"report_recall\": recall(labels, kept),\n        \"prompt_sha256\": prompt_sha256(system),\n        \"articles\": len(out),\n        \"unparsed\": unparsed,\n        \"prompt_tokens\": sum(o.get(\"prompt_tokens\", 0) for o in out if o),\n        \"output_tokens\": sum(o.get(\"output_tokens\", 0) for o in out if o),\n        