{"parentUuid":"78e73b93-c573-43e1-9eea-4a6c1543f294","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgazgKxxL5Y239cZW4Pko","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MzWaWQYTwXiyBkzmdMDVaP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"N=\"/Users/hotragn/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e/step-2C.3.md\" && cat >> \"$N\" <<'EOF'\n\n## Format against judgment (commit 1547b7d, eval/results/phase2c/format_check.json, scripts/format_check.py)\n- gemma4 thinking off, outcome: strict 5/24 (9–40%), normalised 20/24 (64–93%). 18 of 19 misses are format: a bare string with no quote, which the parse drops. 15 of those 18 are right once read as values; 3 say `explained` where dev has `unknown`. 1 is a judgment miss (`unknown` against `unexplained`). The verifier dropped no outcome quote.\n- The same bare-string habit shows up in place_type (5 format, now 15/24) and precision (5 format, now 15/24). Bare values carry no quote, so they can't pass the verifier as training labels. The fix is a schema-constrained output, which is free to measure.\n- 397B r3, place_state: strict 13/23, normalised 16/23. 7 judgment misses fill a state where dev and the story-place rule leave it empty: 2 come from a source paper's name (Albany Times, Baltimore American), and 5 come from a town with no state given (Georgetown→Delaware, Gainesville→Florida, NEW YORK dateline with no story place, \"New York letter\", Hilo→Hawaiian Islands). 3 format misses give a value that isn't a state (Philadelphia twice, China). The normalised score empties those, so they agree with dev's null, but each was the same town-name inference underneath.\nEOF","description":"Append the format check findings to the hand-over note"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":412,"cache_read_input_