{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","id":"e83d27ec-21d0-4397-84db-637316bb79c9","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:06:04.698Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"7b35af0d1ba22d1b1b7d4c91038d50b583ea5d544dd1607adac5368903cb8a35","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"2cfb3fd0-d7f7-41b6-adce-ced822df247f","keep":38,"tail":["9d93ff4ae97ee0ae5439fc869f99f7b6abcd3530278c8f28b53fa2139afe8e02","db0b46dcee52fad9064dbb482bc15d2086358f7023d372c8cb5c3e3b8aa5fb4f"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",39,"content",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"ef12d7123d16f3cae7e76ba7dca1f6af082a14d91a10f59d1aa4069ac88aa063"}
{"parentUuid":"a17d7205-0d28-4939-bebb-4c9eb6bbfc8c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgazhJQj7FXbpTHycyDDF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"2C.3 interim 3: gemma4's low outcome score is mostly a format problem, not a judgment one. The 397B's low place_state score is mostly judgment. Both scores are kept, and the check is committed and pushed (1547b7d, confirmed with ls-remote; 395 tests pass, secret scan clean).\n\nThe script is `scripts/format_check.py` and the results are in `eval/results/phase2c/format_check.json`. Both read the saved answers only; no model was asked anything.\n\n**gemma4, thinking off, outcome**\n- **As scored:** 5/24 (9–40%).\n- **With the format normalised:** 20/24 (64–93%).\n- **Format, 18 of the 19 misses:** it wrote the outcome as a bare string like `\"outcome\": \"unknown\"` with no quote, and the parse drops anything that isn't `{\"value\", \"quote\"}`. Read as values, 15 of those 18 are right. The other 3 say `explained` where dev has `unknown`, so they're also judgment errors.\n- **Judgment, 1 miss:** it wrote `unknown` with a quote where dev has `unexplained`.\n- **The verifier dropped no outcome quote.**\n- **The same habit in two other fields:** place type (5 format misses; 14/24 rises to 15/24) and precision (5 format misses; 13/24 rises to 15/24).\n\nThe normalised values have no quotes, so they still can't pass the verifier as training labels. The fix would be to make gemma4 answer in a fixed JSON schema. That costs nothing, and I'll measure it with the other free levers.\n\n**397B round 3, place state**\n- **As scored:** 13/23. **With the format normalised:** 16/23.\n- **No quote was dropped by the verifier.**\n- **Judgment, 7 misses:** each one fills in a state where dev leaves it empty, which the story-place rule requires.\n  - 2 took the state from a source paper's name (the Albany Times, the Baltimore American).\n  - 5 guessed it from a town with no state given: Georgetown→Delaware, Gainesville→Florida, a NEW YORK dateline on a story with no place, \"New York letter\", and Hilo→Hawaiian Islands.\n- **Format, 3 misses:** the value isn't a state (Philadelphia twice, China). Normalising empties them, so they match dev, but underneath each is the same guess from a town name.\n\nBy contrast, gemma4 scores 22/24 on place state.\n\nThe gemma4 thinking-on run on dev started at 16:57 and saves only at the end. The off run took 37 minutes, so I expect one to three hours. The mlx-lm LoRA timing runs after it, then `runtime_check.py`. The teacher comparison follows, and no long teacher run starts before you approve it.\n\nI didn't hand-check the 3 `explained`-vs-`unknown` cases against the articles; the judgment calls there are dev's labels as they stand."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1231,"cache_read_input_tokens":139175,"output_tokens":976,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1231,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":976,"cache_read_input_tokens":139175,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1231,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1231},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e3811256-541b-454c-af40-2f3a95c2d262","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgazhHe6cqATNQ7WCHmfs","requestRef":"e83d27ec-21d0-4397-84db-637316bb79c9","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"aed0809e-e041-4d91-b69c-98f8ccaaaede","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:06:14.657Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
