{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","id":"d00599c4-a75e-4a77-a1fe-0db18b3207ee","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:08:33.919Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"7b35af0d1ba22d1b1b7d4c91038d50b583ea5d544dd1607adac5368903cb8a35","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"09e1354f-1e44-4043-9320-62f82f93c94c","keep":54,"tail":["49f819cbd7d043bbe67e82730274585551b01caf9b4a4e888fe7ed4c04130c63","e6b540e780affd915b3c782024891cd383ac5df1fd0f6cca2d1aa81316f119cb"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",55,"content",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"761b8955550a50d0a340be3286ce3a2c0a2ebfc837a02b3dc67c04efdc785eac"}
{"parentUuid":"63d098af-2aab-47a5-82fd-a08f83355ef0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaztJVk5dCUE2j9wUfdN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"2C.3 interim 4: the quote rule is in the teacher prompt, pushed as c243058 and confirmed with ls-remote (395 tests pass, secret scan clean). The gemma4 rerun with it is queued and hasn't started yet.\n\n**The prompt.** Round 2's worked example and \"never a bare string\" were already in the prompt, and gemma4 broke them anyway for the three choice fields. So the rule went on the line that lists the choices, which read like a list of bare values. It now says outcome, place type and precision are value-plus-quote objects like every other field, and gives the shape once. It's a general rule, not tied to any article.\n\n**Training labels.** They still go through `teacher.verified`, which drops any value without a verified quote. The format check's normalisation is for scoring only, and its docstring now says so.\n\n**Queued, in order:**\n1. The gemma4 thinking-on run on dev, still going (old prompt; started 16:57).\n2. Unload Ollama, then the mlx-lm LoRA timing.\n3. gemma4 with the new prompt, thinking off, saved as round `g26q`. Its scores after the verifier, with quotes, are the ones I'll report for choosing the teacher.\n4. The runtime check: Ollama first, then mlx-lm on its own once the Ollama models are unloaded, with the agreement on the 50.\n\nThe teacher comparison and the timings come when those finish.\n\nI picked thinking off for the rerun because that's where the format failure showed up and it takes 37 minutes. If thinking on comes out clearly better, it would need its own rerun with the new prompt, which is likely a few hours."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":388,"cache_read_input_tokens":150622,"output_tokens":536,"output_tokens_details