{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","id":"f08e8116-e8e7-4d1e-b3bf-d7661dad2bdb","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:34:40.519Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"7b35af0d1ba22d1b1b7d4c91038d50b583ea5d544dd1607adac5368903cb8a35","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"27ac4fd1-67aa-4471-8955-3c18ff511c06","keep":83,"tail":["dd4312ebcdaabbe9c0a746c52aa6de3f707c1523c51f4af0d7886bca2b3c1d38","21ae882bc61b7b3c536468f85b3d3f25bb3ac7b6d1f658d189e4dff2da673a61"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",84,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"a183841eaacc21de8edff114ae2dd41ba58feb338cc517d0a5fe6414c7dcc22d"}
{"parentUuid":"5f885c98-a72f-4a68-8d17-44d712404c7e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb2smdqgnssuoQmt2RxJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"gemma4's thinking-on run on dev didn't finish, and it saved nothing.\n\n- **What happened:** at 17:30 macOS killed Ollama's runner while it was on the 7th article. This machine has no swap, so when memory fills up macOS kills a process instead. I can't say for sure what tipped it over. The likeliest causes are gemma4's long thinking context, or the test suite I ran for a commit at about that time. From now on I won't run anything heavy alongside the local runs.\n- **Thinking on is too slow for a full run.** From Ollama's own log, the 6 finished articles took 2.4 to 8.1 minutes each. That's about 13 hours for dev and about 11 days for a 3,000-article draw, against 15 seconds an article with thinking off. Thinking on only makes sense for a few routed articles. Re-running it on all of dev would take about 13 hours, so I'm not doing that without the go-ahead.\n- **The fix:** `scripts/local_teacher.py` now saves each dev answer as soon as it arrives. A rerun picks up where the last one stopped, and a dropped connection is retried up to 3 times, a minute apart. The queued gemma4 run with the quote rule (thinking off) will use it, starting when the LoRA timing finishes. `tests/test_local_teacher.py` covers the retry.\n- **Not yet committed:** I'll run the lint, tests and secret scan, then commit, once the LoRA timing ends and memory frees up."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":889,"cache_read_input_tokens":170491,"output_tokens":492,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":889,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"infere