{"parentUuid":"36321000-2c7f-44b5-bd36-bca632c4789b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb3X7Lo6PsNKfKihJmfW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"2C.3: BLOCKED — Ollama's server is down and every local run has failed since 17:31.\n\nI've pushed the fixes (11c054f, confirmed with ls-remote; 397 tests pass, lint and secret scan clean). Before I restart anything, I need to know whether the owner quit these processes on purpose.\n\n**What failed:**\n- **gemma4 with thinking on:** at 17:31 macOS killed Ollama's model process on the 7th article, and the run saved nothing. The 6 finished articles took 2.4–8.1 minutes each, which is about 11 days for a 3,000 draw.\n- **The LoRA timing:** mlx-lm ran out of GPU memory in its first validation pass, before any training step.\n- **The quote-rule rerun and the Ollama runtime check:** both failed because the Ollama server refused connections from about 17:38.\n- **The mlx-lm runtime check:** it got SIGTERM at 17:42. The Ollama server and its leftover model process are now gone too.\n\n**What's fixed:**\n- Local dev runs now save each answer as soon as it arrives, so a rerun picks up where the last one stopped. A dropped connection is retried up to 3 times, a minute apart.\n- The LoRA timing now uses gradient checkpointing and a single validation batch.\n\nNothing is running now. A follow-up script that would rerun the LoRA timing is written, but I haven't started it.\n\n**The question, also sent to the kickoff session:** did the owner quit Ollama and the mlx-lm run? If not, may I restart Ollama with `ollama serve` in the background, on 127.0.0.1 with its previous defaults? After that I'd rerun, one at a time: the quote-rule run, the runtime check, then the LoRA timing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":333,"cache_read_input_tokens":186768,"output_tokens":587,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":333,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":587,"cache_read_input_tokens":186768,"cache_creation_input_tokens":333,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":333},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"feacc1d9-541b-4605-8b3f-01f22b22b9e8","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgb3X6nJiLi6zAsGZvm3m","requestRef":"09c041ef-7f35-4717-8927-03582396b205","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"1bde3b01-3104-464b-9f8c-ae30579aee0b","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:43:13.231Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
