{"parentUuid":"d1c82144-be25-4169-bd96-f94d873b4be6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb3cNp6mfWoha4uLpv1T","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xdf4fQSdiizhs31PbYmq5v","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"N=\"/Users/hotragn/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e/step-2C.3.md\" && cat >> \"$N\" <<'EOF'\n\n## PAUSED (about 17:45): all local model work stopped, because the owner's Mac was freezing\n- Another session stopped Ollama and killed runtime_check. I've started nothing since, and no chain of mine is running or queued (chain3 deleted).\n- Lost so far:\n  - gemma4 thinking on: runner killed at 17:31 after 6 articles in 32 min, 2.4–8.1 min each.\n  - The LoRA timing: GPU memory ran out in the first validation pass, likely with the orphaned runner still holding memory.\n  - g26q (the quote rule) and the runtime check: no server.\n- Ready for the resume (pushed in 11c054f and 4c24f36):\n  - dev runs save each answer as it lands, resume, and retry a dropped request\n  - thinking off asks for a 12,288-token context and at most 1,024 answer tokens (was 16,384 and 4,096)\n  - the LoRA uses gradient checkpointing and one validation batch\n- Resume order once the owner says so, one model at a time with nothing else heavy alongside:\n  1. g26q, gemma4 thinking off with the quote rule\n  2. unload, then the runtime check's Ollama mode\n  3. unload, then its mlx mode and the agreement\n  4. the LoRA timing at batch 4, then at batch 2 if that fails\n- Thinking on isn't planned: at about 5 min an article, dev alone would take about 13 h.\nEOF","description":"Record the pause and the resume plan in the hand-over note"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":889,"cache_read_input_tokens":190758,"output_tokens":797,"ou