{"parentUuid":"d4a19365-4bed-4885-a1fe-ba62f092786d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb3d5nwYJUnRf2CGAnSa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"2C.3: PAUSED. All local model work has stopped: nothing of mine is running or queued, and I won't start Ollama, mlx-lm or any GPU job until the owner says to resume.\n\n- **Checked:** none of my jobs are running. The follow-up script that would have rerun the LoRA timing is deleted, so it can't start by accident.\n- **Less memory for the resume** (commit 4c24f36, pushed and confirmed with ls-remote; 397 tests pass, secret scan clean):\n  - gemma4 with thinking off now asks Ollama for a 12,288-token context and at most 1,024 answer tokens, down from 16,384 and 4,096. Dev's longest prompt is 11,294 tokens and its longest answer 334, so both still fit.\n  - From 11c054f: each dev answer is saved as it arrives, a rerun picks up where the last one stopped, and a dropped request is retried. The LoRA timing uses gradient checkpointing and a single validation batch.\n- **The resume order,** one model at a time, with nothing else heavy alongside:\n  1. gemma4 with the quote rule, thinking off.\n  2. Unload, then the runtime check's Ollama part.\n  3. Unload, then its mlx-lm part and the agreement between the two.\n  4. The LoRA timing at batch 4, or batch 2 if that runs out of memory.\n- **Thinking on isn't planned:** at about 5 minutes an article, dev alone would take about 13 hours.\n\nThe pause and the plan are in the hand-over note. The teacher comparison waits until the gemma4 quote-rule run can finish."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":929,"cache_read_input_tokens":191647,"output_tokens":539,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephe