{"parentUuid":"35d17a10-a7ed-494d-a4c9-446cb17d06b5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"<cross-session-message from=\"local_cbd6aed2-f42a-4724-8982-8a86e51899ae\" from-name=\"btw: My mac is stucking, can I stop ollama\">\nPIVOT, from the owner: Week 4 is submitted TONIGHT. The deadline is 11:59 PM PDT, which is 02:59 EDT; it is now about 17:45 EDT. Park 2C.3 where it is, committed. The new goal is a working demo and a numbers sheet by 01:00 EDT. I'm writing the article myself. The Mac froze earlier, so there's one rule: no Ollama or mlx runs except step 3, run once, alone, with num_ctx 4096 and 1 request at a time. Lowest priority (nice) for anything heavier than a script.\n\nBuild this on a new branch `submission`, cut from phase-2c-reader. Commit in small steps and push.\n\n1. **The Morgue, a static demo (top priority, done by 22:30).**\n   - `scripts/export_demo.py` writes `web/public/reports.json` from the frozen gold and dev labels whose kind is `report`, about 78.\n   - Each entry: article id, paper, date, the place and its state, seen, outcome, people, each with its verified quote, the headline, the full OCR text, and the loc.gov page and crop URL from `crops_for`'s cache. Don't fetch anything new.\n   - `web/` renders it as a static Vite build, with no API and no DB:\n     - search by town, state or word, and filter by decade and outcome\n     - each report as a card: the clipping image beside its transcription, quotes highlighted in the text, and \"not stated\" where a field has no quote\n     - a footer on how it was made: hand-labelled under POLICY.md with a blind second pass, and the reader is still being trained\n   - Accessible, works at phone width, with a newspaper-morgue look per UI-IDEAS.md. Take it as far as time allows.\n   - `pnpm --dir web build` must pass, and `make lint` and the tests too.\n   - Add a launch.json-ready `pnpm --dir web preview` command. Nothing deploys: going public waits for the owner's yes.\n2. **The numbers sheet: `scripts/numbers.py`** prints every number the article may use, each with its source file, and writes `eval/results/numbers.json`:\n   - the corpus and candidates (1,236,122), lexicon v1 against v2, eval A's results\n   - stories and reprints (decision 36's figures), the reservoir\n   - gold and dev (300/150, 17 strata, 46 gold reports, the weighted rate with its interval), agreement (271/300, κ 0.88), and the blind re-ruling (28 of 30)\n   - the teachers on dev: 397B round 3 against gemma4, before and after the format fix\n   - the Tinker spend, local throughput, and the test count\n   \n   One command reproduces it all. I will quote only from this file.\n3. **The live reading demo (after 1 is done, about 22:30).** `scripts/read_one.py <article_id>`: gemma4:26b, local, the round-3 prompt plus the value-and-quote example. It prints each field, its quote, and VERIFIED or NOT STATED from the verifier.\n   - Run it on 3 dev reports, using dev only.\n   - Save the outputs to `docs/demo/` as text, and take terminal screenshots if you can.\n   - Then `ollama stop` the model.\n4. **The README** for judges: what it is, how to run the demo (`pnpm --dir web preview`), how to reproduce the numbers, the data source and licence (AmericanStories and loc.gov), and the open-weight models used.\n5. **Release hygiene:**\n   - Run the secret scan over the whole history and the recorded Entire sessions, as the 5A item says.\n   - Redact the other local account's process list from step 1.7's Entire logs.\n   - Report anything that blocks making the repo public. Don't make it public: that's the owner's call.\n\nSend me a short report when 1 and 2 are pushed, with the first line `SUBMISSION: DEMO READY at <sha>`, then another after 3–5.\n</cross-session-message>","source_uuid":"3a0a951d-dbf2-4c48-b7f4-80b4363b0e8d","delivery_id":"5fd19a88-bc3b-40bc-b26c-85c3003abc07","commandMode":"prompt","origin":{"kind":"peer","from":"local_cbd6aed2-f42a-4724-8982-8a86e51899ae",