{"parentUuid":"c991442b-39e8-489f-bce9-a08644d04c61","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb3mQptcBX7mFBZcz9Px","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Branch `submission` is cut at 1ad0348 and pushed. The numbers sheet touches none of the demo's files, so a subagent builds it while I do the demo:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1906,"cache_read_input_tokens":206726,"output_tokens":2766,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":713},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1906,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2766,"cache_read_input_tokens":206726,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1906,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1906},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a8ff0810-105b-4cbf-a561-a22a3de8c78f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgb3mQPcFZbVsv9YdmWwQ","requestRef":"85e96009-e83e-460f-a06a-576606ad0852","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"fbc76743-63d6-4cd9-9bba-c33eedc2ee79","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:46:29.114Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"fbc76743-63d6-4cd9-9bba-c33eedc2ee79","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb3mQptcBX7mFBZcz9Px","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LM4LsFAHdNSduZaKhEwXCd","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Build the numbers sheet script","prompt":"You're building `scripts/numbers.py` for the Paper Ghosts repo at /Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts (git branch `submission`, already checked out; do NOT switch branches, commit, push, or run any git command that changes state). The project owner is writing a hackathon article tonight and will quote ONLY numbers from this file, so every number must be exactly what a committed results file or doc says, with its source.\n\n## Goal\n`uv run python scripts/numbers.py` prints every number below, one per line with its source, and writes `eval/results/numbers.json`: a list or dict of entries, each with a name, the value(s), and a `source` giving the file path and the JSON key path (or doc file and line) it was read from. The script READS the sources at run time. Don't hard-code a value except where the only source is a doc's prose; then read the doc and parse it, or, if you truly can't parse it, hard-code it with the exact file and line in `source` and a `# shortcut:` comment.\n\n## Numbers wanted (find each source; most live in eval/results/ and Docs/)\n- The corpus and the candidates. `scripts/local_teacher.py` has CANDIDATES = 1_236_122. `eval/results/phase2c/credit_check.json` has a pool of 1,539,818 articles and 1,229,780 candidates. Find where 1,236,122 comes from (likely an ingest or eval-A results file, or Docs/DECISIONS.md). Report both figures with sources and add a one-line note on what each counts. Do NOT reconcile them by guessing.\n- Lexicon v1 against v2, and eval A's results (search eval/results/ and Docs/DECISIONS.md, BUILD-PLAN.md, RESUME.md).\n- Stories and reprints: decision 36's figures in Docs/DECISIONS.md, and the reservoir.\n- Gold and dev: 300 and 150 articles, 17 strata, 46 gold reports, the weighted report rate with its interval. `eval/results/phase2c/gold_measures.json` has the weighted rate (about 0.97%) and the story-place rule figures. eval/gold/labels.jsonl and dev_labels.jsonl are the frozen labels; counting kinds from them is fine.\n- First-pass against second-pass agreement: 271/300 and κ 0.88 (find the results file; scripts/second_pass.py has an `agreement` mode). Also the blind re-ruling, 28 of 30 (`eval/results/phase2c/blind_rulings.json`).\n- The teachers on dev:\n  - Qwen3.5-397B round 3: `eval/results/phase2c/teacher_dev_r3.json`, with kind, report-or-not, report recall, and each field with its Wilson interval, after the verifier.\n  - gemma4:26b with thinking off: `teacher_dev_g26.json`.\n  - `eval/results/phase2c/format_check.json`: strict against normalised for outcome, place_state, place_type and precision, for rounds g26 and r3. Label \"normalised\" as scoring only.\n- The Tinker spend: Docs/BUDGET.md's spend-stopped section and `credit_check.json`'s billing fields, if present.\n- Local throughput:\n  - `eval/results/phase2c/local_throughput.json`: articles an hour per concurrency, the long prompt against the short one, and the prefix figures.\n  - `eval/results/phase2c/local_teacher.json`: gemma4's articles an hour and its hours for a 3,000 draw.\n  - gemma4 with thinking on: there is NO results file. Its only record is 6 articles taking 2.4–8.1 minutes each, from Ollama's server log. Put it in with source \"Ollama server log, 2026-10-31 17:00–17:30 (not committed)\" as a hard-coded shortcut.\n- The test count: `uv run pytest --collect-only -q | tail -1`, run by the script through subprocess.\n\n## Rules\n- No network calls, no model calls, no Ollama or mlx, nothing heavy. This Mac froze earlier, so only read files and run pytest's collection.\n- Never read, print or echo `.env` or anything secret.\n- Write only: scripts/numbers.py, tests/test_numbers.py (one small test, e.g. that every entry has a non-empty source and the file loads), and eval/results/numbers.json.\n- Match the repo's style. Scripts import siblings by bare name (`from label_gold import ROOT`) because tests and scripts put scripts/ on the path; look at scripts/format_check.py for a recent, compact example. There's a one-paragraph docstring at the top and few comments.\n- When done: `uv run ruff format scripts/numbers.py tests/test_numbers.py && uv run ruff check scripts/numbers.py tests/test_numbers.py && uv run pytest -q tests/test_numbers.py && uv run python scripts/numbers.py` must all pass.\n\n## Report back\nThe full printed output of `uv run python scripts/numbers.py`, plus a short list of every number you couldn't find or that conflicts between sources, each with the files involved.","subagent_type":"general-purpose"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1906,"cache_read_input_tokens":206726,"output_tokens":2766,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":713},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1906,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2766,"cache_read_input_tokens":206726,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1906,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1906},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LM4LsFAHdNSduZaKhEwXCd":{"description":"Build the numbers sheet script","prompt":"You're building `scripts/numbers.py` for the Paper Ghosts repo at /Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts (git branch `submission`, already checked out; do NOT switch branches, commit, push, or run any git command that changes state). The project owner is writing a hackathon article tonight and will quote ONLY numbers from this file, so every number must be exactly what a committed results file or doc says, with its source.\n\n## Goal\n`uv run python scripts/numbers.py` prints every number below, one per line with its source, and writes `eval/results/numbers.json`: a list or dict of entries, each with a name, the value(s), and a `source` giving the file path and the JSON key path (or doc file and line) it was read from. The script READS the sources at run time. Don't hard-code a value except where the only source is a doc's prose; then read the doc and parse it, or, if you truly can't parse it, hard-code it with the exact file and line in `source` and a `# shortcut:` comment.\n\n## Numbers wanted (find each source; most live in eval/results/ and Docs/)\n- The corpus and the candidates. `scripts/local_teacher.py` has CANDIDATES = 1_236_122. `eval/results/phase2c/credit_check.json` has a pool of 1,539,818 articles and 1,229,780 candidates. Find where 1,236,122 comes from (likely an ingest or eval-A results file, or Docs/DECISIONS.md). Report both figures with sources and add a one-line note on what each counts. Do NOT reconcile them by guessing.\n- Lexicon v1 against v2, and eval A's results (search eval/results/ and Docs/DECISIONS.md, BUILD-PLAN.md, RESUME.md).\n- Stories and reprints: decision 36's figures in Docs/DECISIONS.md, and the reservoir.\n- Gold and dev: 300 and 150 articles, 17 strata, 46 gold reports, the weighted report rate with its interval. `eval/results/phase2c/gold_measures.json` has the weighted rate (about 0.97%) and the story-place rule figures. eval/gold/labels.jsonl and dev_labels.jsonl are the frozen labels; counting kinds from them is fine.\n- First-pass against second-pass agreement: 271/300 and κ 0.88 (find the results file; scripts/second_pass.py has an `agreement` mode). Also the blind re-ruling, 28 of 30 (`eval/results/phase2c/blind_rulings.json`).\n- The teachers on dev:\n  - Qwen3.5-397B round 3: `eval/results/phase2c/teacher_dev_r3.json`, with kind, report-or-not, report recall, and each field with its Wilson interval, after the verifier.\n  - gemma4:26b with thinking off: `teacher_dev_g26.json`.\n  - `eval/results/phase2c/format_check.json`: strict against normalised for outcome, place_state, place_type and precision, for rounds g26 and r3. Label \"normalised\" as scoring only.\n- The Tinker spend: Docs/BUDGET.md's spend-stopped section and `credit_check.json`'s billing fields, if present.\n- Local throughput:\n  - `eval/results/phase2c/local_throughput.json`: articles an hour per concurrency, the long prompt against the short one, and the prefix figures.\n  - `eval/results/phase2c/local_teacher.json`: gemma4's articles an hour and its hours for a 3,000 draw.\n  - gemma4 with thinking on: there is NO results file. Its only record is 6 articles taking 2.4–8.1 minutes each, from Ollama's server log. Put it in with source \"Ollama server log, 2026-10-31 17:00–17:30 (not committed)\" as a hard-coded shortcut.\n- The test count: `uv run pytest --collect-only -q | tail -1`, run by the script through subprocess.\n\n## Rules\n- No network calls, no model calls, no Ollama or mlx, nothing heavy. This Mac froze earlier, so only read files and run pytest's collection.\n- Never read, print or echo `.env` or anything secret.\n- Write only: scripts/numbers.py, tests/test_numbers.py (one small test, e.g. that every entry has a non-empty source and the file loads), and eval/results/numbers.json.\n- Match the repo's style. Scripts import siblings by bare name (`from label_gold import ROOT`) because tests and scripts put scripts/ on the path; look at scripts/format_check.py for a recent, compact example. There's a one-paragraph docstring at the top and few comments.\n- When done: `uv run ruff format scripts/numbers.py tests/test_numbers.py && uv run ruff check scripts/numbers.py tests/test_numbers.py && uv run pytest -q tests/test_numbers.py && uv run python scripts/numbers.py` must all pass.\n\n## Report back\nThe full printed output of `uv run python scripts/numbers.py`, plus a short list of every number you couldn't find or that conflicts between sources, each with the files involved.","subagent_type":"general-purpose"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a8ff0810-105b-4cbf-a561-a22a3de8c78f","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgb3mQPcFZbVsv9YdmWwQ","requestRef":"85e96009-e83e-460f-a06a-576606ad0852","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"65a12f65-f930-4d93-8158-e83d11483ef7","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:46:45.959Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
