uniq -c | tr '\\n' ' ')\"; done; jq -r '.settled // .how // empty' eval/gold/adjudication.jsonl 2>/dev/null | sort | uniq -c | head; grep -n -i \"labeller\\|blind\\|second pass\" Docs/DECISIONS.md | head -12; ls web/node_modules/@fontsource/bodoni-moda/ | head -30 | tr '\\n' ' '; echo; ls web/node_modules/@fontsource/newsreader/ | tr '\\n' ' '","description":"Check who labelled each pass, and the font files"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"be7c6fbc-93b2-4dd4-924a-345f65ba7fac","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgb3v4ZzK5L9ftnxkWft7","requestRef":"4fa3b020-6409-4aca-a172-aed471c2b325","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3b9c654a-f58e-4f91-84fb-db07e21bd6e9","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:48:43.804Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"3b9c654a-f58e-4f91-84fb-db07e21bd6e9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1d7af7f1-1a6e-437a-aa3b-3271a087cd0a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L6mnMbGn327LzmYfoGEmYi","type":"tool_result","content":"eval/gold/labels.jsonl:  239 Claude   61 ruling \neval/gold/dev_labels.jsonl:  142 Claude    8 ruling \neval/gold/second_pass.jsonl:  330 second pass \n  28 blind ruling taken\n   1 own ruling kept: this is the second printing of the backwoods-preacher sketch, whose other printing the blind judge ruled fiction; both printings take one kind\n   1 own ruling kept: two other gold obituaries with 'spirit land' are other in both passes and undisputed; one rule for all three\n  39 the blind ruling agrees\n297:  - **Blind check:** I re-judged a seeded 10% of their negatives (17, seed \"eval A v2 added check\") from the same text, without their notes, and agreed on all 17 (81.6–100%).\n299:  - **Beyond decision 30's protocol:** I also read in full the 8 negatives outside the blind check that the agents' notes called near. The ninth was in the blind check.\n300:  - **Outcome:** all 10 of the agents' reports stand. 3 of the close calls are reports and 18 are not, and 1 of the near negatives is a report. In `added.json`, `rejudged` is \"sample\" for the blind check and \"full\" for an article I read in full.\n729:  - **My blind re-check:** a seeded 10% of each stratum's commoner label (\"same\" in every stratum), judged before seeing the agents' labels. I agreed on all 61 (94.1–100%).\n886:  - Each labeller keeps one label per article, so the owner's re-check sits beside mine without replacing it.\n891:**38. Gold and dev are labelled by hand under `POLICY.md`, all 450 through the page's `checked()`. A blind second pass relabels all of gold and a seeded fifth of dev. On gold it agrees with the first pass on 271 of 300 kinds (κ 0.88, 0.84–0.92) and on 296 of 300 report-or-not calls (κ 0.95). Every one of the 69 disagreements is ruled on under `POLICY.md`, and then ruled again blind by fresh judges, since the first rulings were the first labeller's. Every difference is settled with a written reason, all the labels and rulings are kept, and the labels are frozen by sha256 before any model output. Gold holds 46 reports, against the 35.3 expected.**\n896:- **Calls `POLICY.md` left to the labeller,** made the same way in gold and dev:\n903:- **The blind second pass** (`scripts/second_pass.py`) covers 330 articles: all of gold, and the 30 of dev drawn with the seed \"2C.2 second pass dev sample\".\n906:  - A usage limit stopped seven of them partway, and each was resumed in its own blind context.\n931:- **The first rulings** (`eval/gold/adjudication.jsonl`), the first labeller's: 69 articles disagreed, 61 of them in gold. 34 were on kind, and 35 on fields alone.\n935:  - **The second pass's call was taken six times:**\n944:- **The blind re-ruling** (the EM's review: gold can't rest on a judge ruling its own case). Four fresh judges ruled all 69 disputes again, one pair at a time (`scripts/blind_rulings.py`).\n400-italic.css 400.css 500-italic.css 500.css 600-italic.css 600.css 700-italic.css 700.css 800-italic.css 800.css 900-italic.css 900.css CHANGELOG.md LICENSE README.md files index.css index.d.css.ts latin-400-italic.css latin-400.css latin-500-italic.css latin-500.css latin-600-italic.css latin-600.css latin-700-italic.css latin-700.css latin-800-italic.css latin-800.css latin-900-italic.css latin-900.css \n200-italic.css 200.css 300-italic.css 300.css 400-italic.css 400.css 500-italic.css 500.css 600-italic.css 600.css 700-italic.css 700.css 800-italic.css 800.css CHANGELOG.md LICENSE README.md files index.css index.d.css.ts latin-200-italic.css latin-200.css latin-300-italic.css latin-300.css latin-400-italic.css latin-400.css latin-500-italic.css latin-500.css latin-600-italic.css latin-600.css latin-700-italic.css latin-700.css latin-800-italic.css latin-800.css latin-ext-200-italic.css latin-ext-200.css latin-ext-300-italic.css latin-ext-300.css latin-ext-400-italic.css latin-ext-400.css latin-ext-500-italic.css latin-ext-500.css latin-ext-600-italic.css latin-ext-600.css latin-ext-700-italic.css latin-ext-700.css latin-ext-800-italic.css latin-ext-800.css latin-ext-italic.css latin-ext.css latin-italic.css latin.css metadata.json package.json scss unicode.json vietnamese-200-italic.css vietnamese-200.css vietnamese-300-italic.css vietnamese-300.css vietnamese-400-italic.css vietnamese-400.css vietnamese-500-italic.css vietnamese-500.css vietnamese-600-italic.css vietnamese-600.css vietnamese-700-italic.css vietnamese-700.css vietnamese-800-italic.css vietnamese-800.css vietnamese-italic.css vietnamese.css","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"582da044-ce1a-48f3-9f01-8994859fe890","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:48:44.507Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"eval/gold/labels.jsonl:  239 Claude   61 ruling \neval/gold/dev_labels.jsonl:  142 Claude    8 ruling \neval/gold/second_pass.jsonl:  330 second pass \n  28 blind ruling taken\n   1 own ruling kept: this is the second printing of the backwoods-preacher sketch, whose other printing the blind judge ruled fiction; both printings take one kind\n   1 own ruling kept: two other gold obituaries with 'spirit land' are other in both passes and undisputed; one rule for all three\n  39 the blind ruling agrees\n297:  - **Blind check:** I re-judged a seeded 10% of their negatives (17, seed \"eval A v2 added check\") from the same text, without their notes, and agreed on all 17 (81.6–100%).\n299:  - **Beyond decision 30's protocol:** I also read in full the 8 negatives outside the blind check that the agents' notes called near. The ninth was in the blind check.\n300:  - **Outcome:** all 10 of the agents' reports stand. 3 of the close calls are reports and 18 are not, and 1 of the near negatives is a report. In `added.json`, `rejudged` is \"sample\" for the blind check and \"full\" for an article I read in full.\n729:  - **My blind re-check:** a seeded 10% of each stratum's commoner label (\"same\" in every stratum), judged before seeing the agents' labels. I agreed on all 61 (94.1–100%).\n886:  - Each labeller keeps one label per article, so the owner's re-check sits beside mine without replacing it.\n891:**38. Gold and dev are labelled by hand under `POLICY.md`, all 450 through the page's `checked()`. A blind second pass relabels all of gold and a seeded fifth of dev. On gold it agrees with the first pass on 271 of 300 kinds (κ 0.88, 0.84–0.92) and on 296 of 300 report-or-not calls (κ 0.95). Every one of the 69 disagreements is ruled on under `POLICY.md`, and then ruled again blind by fresh judges, since the first rulings were the first labeller's. Every difference is settled with a written reason, all the labels and rulings are kept, and the labels are frozen by sha256 before any model output. Gold holds 46 reports, against the 35.3 expected.**\n896:- **Calls `POLICY.md` left to the labeller,** made the same way in gold and dev:\n903:- **The blind second pass** (`scripts/second_pass.py`) covers 330 articles: all of gold, and the 30 of dev drawn with the seed \"2C.2 second pass dev sample\".\n906:  - A usage limit stopped seven of them partway, and each was resumed in its own blind context.\n931:- **The first rulings** (`eval/gold/adjudication.jsonl`), the first labeller's: 69 articles disagreed, 61 of them in gold. 34 were on kind, and 35 on fields alone.\n935:  - **The second pass's call was taken six times:**\n944:- **The blind re-ruling** (the EM's review: gold can't rest on a judge ruling its own case). Four fresh judges ruled all 69 disputes again, one pair at a time (`scripts/blind_rulings.py`).\n400-italic.css 400.css 500-italic.css 500.css 600-italic.css 600.css 700-italic.css 700.css 800-italic.css 800.css 900-italic.css 900.css CHANGELOG.md LICENSE README.md files index.css index.d.css.ts latin-400-italic.css latin-400.css latin-500-italic.css latin-500.css latin-600-italic.css latin-600.css latin-700-italic.css latin-700.css latin-800-italic.css latin-800.css latin-900-italic.css latin-900.css \n200-italic.css 200.css 300-italic.css 300.css 400-italic.css 400.css 500-italic.css 500.css 600-italic.css 600.css 700-italic.css 700.css 800-italic.css 800.css CHANGELOG.md LICENSE README.md files index.css index.d.css.ts latin-200-italic.css latin-200.css latin-300-italic.css latin-300.css latin-400-italic.css latin-400.css latin-500-italic.css latin-500.css latin-600-italic.css latin-600.css latin-700-italic.css latin-700.css latin-800-italic.css latin-800.css latin-ext-200-italic.css latin-ext-200.css latin-ext-300-italic.css latin-ext-300.css latin-ext-400-italic.css latin-ext-400.css latin-ext-500-italic.css latin-ext-500.css latin-ext-600-italic.css latin-ext-600.css latin-ext-700-italic.css latin-ext-700.css latin-ext-800-italic.css latin-ext-800.css latin-ext-italic.css latin-ext.css latin-italic.css latin.css metadata.json package.json scss unicode.json vietnamese-200-italic.css vietnamese-200.css vietnamese-300-italic.css vietnamese-300.css vietnamese-400-italic.css vietnamese-400.css vietnamese-500-italic.css vietnamese-500.css vietnamese-600-italic.css vietnamese-600.css vietnamese-700-italic.css vietnamese-700.css vietnamese-800-italic.css vietnamese-800.css vietnamese-italic.css vietnamese.css","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"be7c6fbc-93b2-4dd4-924a-345f65ba7fac","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"submission","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"o