{"parentUuid":"4894faf0-63de-44e9-87c4-ff219da4a1ca","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1d7af7f1-1a6e-437a-aa3b-3271a087cd0a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01THVZBtvE2XnQ21r3MuibV7","type":"tool_result","content":"Docs\nLICENSE\nMakefile\nREADME.md\napi\ndata\neval\npaperghosts\npyproject.toml\nscripts\ntests\nuv.lock\nweb\n# Paper Ghosts\n\nType a US town and read the ghost reports its newspapers printed between 1774 and 1963. The reports come from the AmericanStories dataset and the Library of Congress page scans. The site never writes a ghost story: every claim links to the clipping it came from.\n\nThis is a work in progress. The plan is in [`Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md`](Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md), and where the build stands is in [`Docs/RESUME.md`](Docs/RESUME.md).\n\n## Run it\n\nYou need `uv`, Node with `pnpm`, the Temporal CLI and Ollama. Keys go in `.env`, which git ignores.\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `make setup` | Installs the Python 3.12 environment and the web shell's packages |\n| `make lint` | ruff, oxlint and the TypeScript check |\n| `make test` | pytest, offline; the Temporal test starts its own throwaway server |\n| `make keys` | Checks every key by shape and with one cheap call, and never prints a value |\n| `make temporal` | The Temporal dev server, with its state in `data/temporal/` and its UI at http://localhost:8233 |\n| `make worker` | The Temporal worker |\n| `make smoke` | One workflow whose activity heartbeats, fails once on purpose and recovers through its retry policy; needs `make temporal` and `make worker` running |\n| `make ingest YEARS=\"1850 1910\"` | Streams those year files through the prefilter, four at a time, and writes each year's candidates, counts, samples and manifest under `data/`; with no `YEARS`, every year in the dataset. A year is skipped while its manifest matches the pinned dataset revision and the current code, and every output on disk matches its recorded sha256. Needs `make temporal` and `make worker` running |\n| `make api` | The read-only API at http://localhost:8000 |\n| `make web` | The web shell at http://localhost:5173 |\n| `make app` | `make api` and `make web` together |\n\n`make eval`, `make db-init`, `make db-verify` and `make numbers` print the phase that builds them and exit with an error.\n\nThe walking skeleton takes one 1850 article from the archive, through Atlas and the API, to a page that shows its clipping beside its text:\n\n```bash\nuv run python scripts/phase1_env.py     # environment facts; saves the 1850 Stratford articles\nuv run python scripts/load_skeleton.py  # loads the Lewistown gazette's knockings into Atlas\nmake app\n```\n\n## What it can't do\n\nFilled in as limits are found.\n\n## Failure log\n\nFilled in as failures are found.\n\n## Credits\n\n- Article text: AmericanStories, from Harvard's Dell Research (CC-BY-4.0)\n- Page scans: Library of Congress, Chronicling America (public domain)\n\nThe code is MIT licensed; see [LICENSE](LICENSE).\nDocs/BRIEF.md:60:**AmericanStories** (Hugging Face `dell-research-harvard/AmericanStories`, CC-BY-4.0, from Harvard's Dell Research): article-level text extracted from the Library of Congress's Chronicling America scans.\nDocs/BRIEF.md:62:  - Download: `https://huggingface.co/datasets/dell-research-harvard/AmericanStories/resolve/main/faro_{year}.tar.gz`\nDocs/BRIEF.md:84:**Places:** take the publication place from the `lccn` title, plus places named in the article. Geocode offline with GeoNames (`cities1000`, CC-BY), recording the source and retrieval date in a manifest.\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:19:    HF[\"AmericanStories<br/>180 year files, 340 GB\"]\nDocs/SRS.md:6:- **Article:** one article region from AmericanStories, with its text, headline, bounding boxes and page.\nDocs/SRS.md:47:| GEO-1 | The publication place is parsed from the LCCN title and geocoded offline against GeoNames `cities1000`. A manifest records the source, retrieval date and licence. | Parser tests on at least 200 distinct titles, plus the manifest |\nDocs/SRS.md:118:| NFR-LIC-1 | AmericanStories (CC-BY-4.0), GeoNames (CC-BY), the LoC scans, the OpenStreetMap and OpenFreeMap attribution, the font licences and the React Bits licence are all credited on the method page and in the README. | Review |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e2caeb8f-3ecf-4472-87b6-97f7a2f48696","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:53:45.314Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Docs\nLICENSE\nMakefile\nREADME.md\napi\ndata\neval\npaperghosts\npyproject.toml\nscripts\ntests\nuv.lock\nweb\n# Paper Ghosts\n\nType a US town and read the ghost reports its newspapers printed between 1774 and 1963. The reports come from the AmericanStories dataset and the Library of Congress page scans. The site never writes a ghost story: every claim links to the clipping it came from.\n\nThis is a work in progress. The plan is in [`Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md`](Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md), and where the build stands is in [`Docs/RESUME.md`](Docs/RESUME.md).\n\n## Run it\n\nYou need `uv`, Node with `pnpm`, the Temporal CLI and Ollama. Keys go in `.env`, which git ignores.\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `make setup` | Installs the Python 3.12 environment and the web shell's packages |\n| `make lint` | ruff, oxlint and the TypeScript check |\n| `make test` | pytest, offline; the Temporal test starts its own throwaway server |\n| `make keys` | Checks every key by shape and with one cheap call, and never prints a value |\n| `make temporal` | The Temporal dev server, with its state in `data/temporal/` and its UI at http://localhost:8233 |\n| `make worker` | The Temporal worker |\n| `make smoke` | One workflow whose activity heartbeats, fails once on purpose and recovers through its retry policy; needs `make temporal` and `make worker` running |\n| `make ingest YEARS=\"1850 1910\"` | Streams those year files through the prefilter, four at a time, and writes each year's candidates, counts, samples and manifest under `data/`; with no `YEARS`, every year in the dataset. A year is skipped while its manifest matches the pinned dataset revision and the current code, and every output on disk matches its recorded sha256. Needs `make temporal` and `make worker` running |\n| `make api` | The read-only API at http://localhost:8000 |\n| `make web` | The web shell at http://localhost:5173 |\n| `make app` | `make api` and `make web` together |\n\n`make eval`, `make db-init`, `make db-verify` and `make numbers` print the phase that builds them and exit with an error.\n\nThe walking skeleton takes one 1850 article from the archive, through Atlas and the API, to a page that shows its clipping beside its text:\n\n```bash\nuv run python scripts/phase1_env.py     # environment facts; saves the 1850 Stratford articles\nuv run python scripts/load_skeleton.py  # loads the Lewistown gazette's knockings into Atlas\nmake app\n```\n\n## What it can't do\n\nFilled in as limits are found.\n\n## Failure log\n\nFilled in as failures are found.\n\n## Credits\n\n- Article text: AmericanStories, from Harvard's Dell Research (CC-BY-4.0)\n- Page scans: Library of Congress, Chronicling America (public domain)\n\nThe code is MIT licensed; see [LICENSE](LICENSE).\nDocs/BRIEF.md:60:**AmericanStories** (Hugging Face `dell-research-harvard/AmericanStories`, CC-BY-4.0, from Harvard's Dell Research): article-level text extracted from the Library of Congress's Chronicling America scans.\nDocs/BRIEF.md:62:  - Download: `https://huggingface.co/datasets/dell-research-harvard/AmericanStories/resolve/main/faro_{year}.tar.gz`\nDocs/BRIEF.md:84:**Places:** take the publication place from the `lccn` title, plus places named in the article. Geocode offline with GeoNames (`cities1000`, CC-BY), recording the source and retrieval date in a manifest.\nDocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:19:    HF[\"AmericanStories<br/>180 year files, 340 GB\"]\nDocs/SRS.md:6:- **Article:** one article region from AmericanStories, with its text, headline, bounding boxes and page.\nDocs/SRS.md:47:| GEO-1 | The publication place is parsed from the LCCN title and geocoded offline against GeoNames `cities1000`. A manifest records the source, retrieval date and licence. | Parser tests on at least 200 distinct titles, plus the manifest |\nDocs/SRS.md:118:| NFR-LIC-1 | AmericanStories (CC-BY-4.0), GeoNames (CC-BY), the LoC scans, the OpenStreetMap and OpenFreeMap attribution, the font licences and the React Bits licence are all credited on the method page and in the README. | Review |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"fc245e4c-809a-4e87-ab92-d7f32ae6b461","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"submission","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4894faf0-63de-44e9-87c4-ff219da4a1ca","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","hash":"385e16ac0b037f1d2834c976703daa229456d8b0d309c2ead5efc09d5a3c83b0","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Step 3 is blocked: the round-3 prompt with POLICY.md is 9,500 to 11,300 tokens, which won't fit the 4,096-token context and would be silently truncated by Ollama. I'm asking about it now and doing steps 4 and 5 in the meantime, since they don't need the model.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HwYFAPEaLoAPSbPHs7Ut7d","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"local_cbd6aed2-f42a-4724-8982-8a86e51899ae","summary":"Ask how to fit read_one in num_ctx 4096","message":"Step 3 question: the round-3 prompt is too big for num_ctx 4096. With POLICY.md in full it runs 9,500–11,300 tokens per dev article, and Ollama would silently cut it. Which do you want?\n(a) num_ctx 12288 for this single run, one request, nothing else running. gemma4 at 12K was the setup the Mac handled earlier; the freeze came from gemma4 and mlx-lm running side by side.\n(b) Keep 4096 and send only the instructions with the quote rule (about 1,000 tokens) and no POLICY.md. The demo would then say it's a shortened prompt.\nI'm doing the README and the release hygiene meanwhile. Ollama stays off until you answer."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01THVZBtvE2XnQ21r3MuibV7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && ls; cat README.md 2>/dev/null | head -60; grep -rn -i \"licen\\|cc-by\\|AmericanStories\" Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md Docs/BRIEF.md Docs/SRS.md | head -12","description":"Read the current README and licence notes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
