{"parentUuid":"5e30c5de-35e8-4f9d-846a-5a17226a01e0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb4LAKSFCJLkYG4sAYDT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"While that's queued, the README for judges goes on top of the existing developer table. I'm keeping the existing table and its credits:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2929,"cache_read_input_tokens":272592,"output_tokens":2149,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":337},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2929,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2149,"cache_read_input_tokens":272592,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2929,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2929},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"7f224156-c27f-4186-b116-c4094fb4516c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgb4L9vNbfKXeABN4b8is","requestRef":"ee94588e-7a09-45e7-992d-30cc21517284","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_session_mgmt","attributionMcpTool":"send_message","type":"assistant","uuid":"d841b839-c89f-4eae-bb84-c567f464aee3","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:53:50.203Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"d841b839-c89f-4eae-bb84-c567f464aee3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb4LAKSFCJLkYG4sAYDT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011NTYeX9dFaJCFRsBa5cdkQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"README.md\"); s = p.read_text()\nhead, rest = s.split(\"## Run it\", 1)\nrest = rest.split(\"## What it can't do\", 1)[0]\nnew = \"\"\"# Paper Ghosts\n\nA morgue of ghost reports from American newspapers, 1774–1963. Paper Ghosts reads the AmericanStories OCR of the Library of Congress's page scans, picks out the articles that report a ghost, and files each one with the exact words of the scan that state its place, what was seen and how it ended. The site never writes a ghost story: every value on it is a quote, and every report links to its clipping.\n\n## The demo: the Morgue\n\nThe 78 ghost reports among the 450 frozen evaluation articles, each with its clipping beside its transcription, the quotes marked in the text, and a typed index card that says \"Not stated\" wherever the paper didn't say. There's no server and no database behind it, and it works offline.\n\n```bash\nmake setup                     # once: the Python environment and the web packages\npnpm --dir web build\npnpm --dir web preview         # http://localhost:4173\n```\n\n`uv run python scripts/export_demo.py` rebuilds its data, `web/public/reports.json` and the clippings in `web/public/crops/`, from the frozen labels and the local crop cache, and fetches nothing.\n\n## The numbers\n\n```bash\nuv run python scripts/article_numbers.py\n```\n\nThis prints every figure the write-up uses, each beside the committed results file or doc line it was read from, and writes them to `eval/results/numbers.json`. Among them:\n- the archive: 370 million articles on 16.9 million pages\n- the 1,236,122 articles the lexicon flags, which group into 974,399 distinct stories\n- the gold set, and how far its two labelling passes agree\n- the teachers compared on dev\n\n## How it was made, and where it stands\n\n- **Ingest and evaluation A** stream all 180 year files through a ghost-word prefilter, then measure what it keeps and misses on samples judged by hand (`Docs/DECISIONS.md`).\n- **Stories** group reprints of one story across papers, so each story is read once.\n- **Gold and dev,** 300 and 150 articles drawn across 17 strata, are labelled one article at a time under `eval/gold/POLICY.md` by an AI labeller (Claude), in a labelling page that shows the crop beside the text.\n  - A blind second pass relabelled all of gold and a seeded fifth of dev.\n  - Fresh judges ruled every disagreement again, blind.\n  - The labels are frozen by sha256 before any model output touched them.\n- **The reader is not trained yet.** Its training labels will come from an open-weight teacher run locally on this Mac; labels never come from Claude, and gold and dev are kept for evaluation only. Two teachers were compared on dev (`eval/results/phase2c/`):\n  - Qwen3.5-397B-A17B, through Tinker, until the spend stopped\n  - gemma4:26b-a4b-it-qat, through Ollama\n- **The student** is Qwen3.5-4B, to be fine-tuned with LoRA through mlx-lm.\n\n## What it can't do yet\n\n- The archive-wide pass hasn't run, so the demo shows only the 78 evaluation reports, not every ghost the papers printed.\n- The OCR is shown as printed. Some clippings are hard to read, and a quote is only as good as the scan's text.\n- A place is the paper's own words. Nothing is geocoded or mapped yet.\n\n## Data and licences\n\n- Article text: AmericanStories, from Harvard's Dell Research (`dell-research-harvard/AmericanStories`, CC-BY-4.0)\n- Page scans and clippings: Library of Congress, Chronicling America (no known copyright restrictions)\n- Fonts, self-hosted through Fontsource under the SIL Open Font License: UnifrakturMaguntia, Bodoni Moda, Newsreader and Courier Prime\n- Open-weight models: Qwen3.5-397B-A17B and Qwen3.5-4B (Qwen), and gemma4:26b-a4b-it-qat (Google)\n- The code is MIT licensed; see [LICENSE](LICENSE).\n\n## Development\n\nThe plan is in [`Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md`](Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md), and where the build stands is in [`Docs/RESUME.md`](Docs/RESUME.md).\n\"\"\"\np.write_text(new + rest.replace(\"\\n\\n\", \"\\n\\n\", 1).rstrip() + \"\\n\")\nPY\nsed -n '/## Development/,$p' README.md | head -12; jq -r '.[] | select(.name|test(\"archive|distinct, v2\")) | .name + \" \" + (.value|tostring)' eval/results/numbers.json 2>/dev/null | head; jq 'type' eval/results/numbers.json","description":"Write the judges' README and check its figures"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2929,"cache_read_input_tokens":272592,"output_tokens":2149,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":337},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2929,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2149,"cache_read_input_tokens":272592,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2929,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2929},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011NTYeX9dFaJCFRsBa5cdkQ":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"README.md\"); s = p.read_text()\nhead, rest = s.split(\"## Run it\", 1)\nrest = rest.split(\"## What it can't do\", 1)[0]\nnew = \"\"\"# Paper Ghosts\n\nA morgue of ghost reports from American newspapers, 1774–1963. Paper Ghosts reads the AmericanStories OCR of the Library of Congress's page scans, picks out the articles that report a ghost, and files each one with the exact words of the scan that state its place, what was seen and how it ended. The site never writes a ghost story: every value on it is a quote, and every report links to its clipping.\n\n## The demo: the Morgue\n\nThe 78 ghost reports among the 450 frozen evaluation articles, each with its clipping beside its transcription, the quotes marked in the text, and a typed index card that says \"Not stated\" wherever the paper didn't say. There's no server and no database behind it, and it works offline.\n\n```bash\nmake setup                     # once: the Python environment and the web packages\npnpm --dir web build\npnpm --dir web preview         # http://localhost:4173\n```\n\n`uv run python scripts/export_demo.py` rebuilds its data, `web/public/reports.json` and the clippings in `web/public/crops/`, from the frozen labels and the local crop cache, and fetches nothing.\n\n## The numbers\n\n```bash\nuv run python scripts/article_numbers.py\n```\n\nThis prints every figure the write-up uses, each beside the committed results file or doc line it was read from, and writes them to `eval/results/numbers.json`. Among them:\n- the archive: 370 million articles on 16.9 million pages\n- the 1,236,122 articles the lexicon flags, which group into 974,399 distinct stories\n- the gold set, and how far its two labelling passes agree\n- the teachers compared on dev\n\n## How it was made, and where it stands\n\n- **Ingest and evaluation A** stream all 180 year files through a ghost-word prefilter, then measure what it keeps and misses on samples judged by hand (`Docs/DECISIONS.md`).\n- **Stories** group reprints of one story across papers, so each story is read once.\n- **Gold and dev,** 300 and 150 articles drawn across 17 strata, are labelled one article at a time under `eval/gold/POLICY.md` by an AI labeller (Claude), in a labelling page that shows the crop beside the text.\n  - A blind second pass relabelled all of gold and a seeded fifth of dev.\n  - Fresh judges ruled every disagreement again, blind.\n  - The labels are frozen by sha256 before any model output touched them.\n- **The reader is not trained yet.** Its training labels will come from an open-weight teacher run locally on this Mac; labels never come from Claude, and gold and dev are kept for evaluation only. Two teachers were compared on dev (`eval/results/phase2c/`):\n  - Qwen3.5-397B-A17B, through Tinker, until the spend stopped\n  - gemma4:26b-a4b-it-qat, through Ollama\n- **The student** is Qwen3.5-4B, to be fine-tuned with LoRA through mlx-lm.\n\n## What it can't do yet\n\n- The archive-wide pass hasn't run, so the demo shows only the 78 evaluation reports, not every ghost the papers printed.\n- The OCR is shown as printed. Some clippings are hard to read, and a quote is only as good as the scan's text.\n- A place is the paper's own words. Nothing is geocoded or mapped yet.\n\n## Data and licences\n\n- Article text: AmericanStories, from Harvard's Dell Research (`dell-research-harvard/AmericanStories`, CC-BY-4.0)\n- Page scans and clippings: Library of Congress, Chronicling America (no known copyright restrictions)\n- Fonts, self-hosted through Fontsource under the SIL Open Font License: UnifrakturMaguntia, Bodoni Moda, Newsreader and Courier Prime\n- Open-weight models: Qwen3.5-397B-A17B and Qwen3.5-4B (Qwen), and gemma4:26b-a4b-it-qat (Google)\n- The code is MIT licensed; see [LICENSE](LICENSE).\n\n## Development\n\nThe plan is in [`Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md`](Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md), and where the build stands is in [`Docs/RESUME.md`](Docs/RESUME.md).\n\"\"\"\np.write_text(new + rest.replace(\"\\n\\n\", \"\\n\\n\", 1).rstrip() + \"\\n\")\nPY\nsed -n '/## Development/,$p' README.md | head -12; jq -r '.[] | select(.name|test(\"archive|distinct, v2\")) | .name + \" \" + (.value|tostring)' eval/results/numbers.json 2>/dev/null | head; jq 'type' eval/results/numbers.json","description":"Write the judges' README and check its figures"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7f224156-c27f-4186-b116-c4094fb4516c","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgb4L9vNbfKXeABN4b8is","requestRef":"ee94588e-7a09-45e7-992d-30cc21517284","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_session_mgmt","attributionMcpTool":"send_message","type":"assistant","uuid":"c1befb8d-8acd-4878-ade6-0b73c7f997a0","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:54:05.087Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"c1befb8d-8acd-4878-ade6-0b73c7f997a0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1d7af7f1-1a6e-437a-aa3b-3271a087cd0a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011NTYeX9dFaJCFRsBa5cdkQ","type":"tool_result","content":"## Development\n\nThe plan is in [`Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md`](Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md), and where the build stands is in [`Docs/RESUME.md`](Docs/RESUME.md).\n\n\nYou need `uv`, Node with `pnpm`, the Temporal CLI and Ollama. Keys go in `.env`, which git ignores.\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `make setup` | Installs the Python 3.12 environment and the web shell's packages |\n| `make lint` | ruff, oxlint and the TypeScript check |\n| `make test` | pytest, offline; the Temporal test starts its own throwaway server |\narchive: pages and articles {\"pages\":16887460,\"articles\":370313913}\nstories: distinct, v2 {\"distinct_stories\":974399,\"with_more_than_one_printing\":96105,\"printings_in_them\":357828,\"cross_paper\":82854}\n\"array\"","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"123ba4c8-00c6-458e-8ea0-1094945bbe09","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:54:06.968Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Development\n\nThe plan is in [`Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md`](Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md), and where the build stands is in [`Docs/RESUME.md`](Docs/RESUME.md).\n\n\nYou need `uv`, Node with `pnpm`, the Temporal CLI and Ollama. Keys go in `.env`, which git ignores.\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `make setup` | Installs the Python 3.12 environment and the web shell's packages |\n| `make lint` | ruff, oxlint and the TypeScript check |\n| `make test` | pytest, offline; the Temporal test starts its own throwaway server |\narchive: pages and articles {\"pages\":16887460,\"articles\":370313913}\nstories: distinct, v2 {\"distinct_stories\":974399,\"with_more_than_one_printing\":96105,\"printings_in_them\":357828,\"cross_paper\":82854}\n\"array\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":10,"newStart":1,"newLines":62,"lines":[" # Paper Ghosts"," ","-Type a US town and read the ghost reports its newspapers printed between 1774 and 1963. The reports come from the AmericanStories dataset and the Library of Congress page scans. The site never writes a ghost story: every claim links to the clipping it came from.","+A morgue of ghost reports from American newspapers, 1774–1963. Paper Ghosts reads the AmericanStories OCR of the Library of Congress's page scans, picks out the articles that report a ghost, and files each one with the exact words of the scan that state its place, what was seen and how it ended. The site never writes a ghost story: every value on it is a quote, and every report links to its clipping."," ","-This is a work in progress. The plan is in [`Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md`](Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md), and where the build stands is in [`Docs/RESUME.md`](Docs/RESUME.md).","+## The demo: the Morgue","+","+The 78 ghost reports among the 450 frozen evaluation articles, each with its clipping beside its transcription, the quotes marked in the text, and a typed index card that says \"Not stated\" wherever the paper didn't say. There's no server and no database behind it, and it works offline.","+","+```bash","+make setup                     # once: the Python environment and the web packages","+pnpm --dir web build","+pnpm --dir web preview         # http://localhost:4173","+```","+","+`uv run python scripts/export_demo.py` rebuilds its data, `web/public/reports.json` and the clippings in `web/public/crops/`, from the frozen labels and the local crop cache, and fetches nothing.","+","+## The numbers","+","+```bash","+uv run python scripts/article_numbers.py","+```","+","+This prints every figure the write-up uses, each beside the committed results file or doc line it was read from, and writes them to `eval/results/numbers.json`. Among them:","+- the archive: 370 million articles on 16.9 million pages","+- the 1,236,122 articles the lexicon flags, which group into 974,399 distinct stories","+- the gold set, and how far its two labelling passes agree","+- the teachers compared on dev","+","+## How it was made, and where it stands","+","+- **Ingest and evaluation A** stream all 180 year files through a ghost-word prefilter, then measure what it keeps and misses on samples judged by hand (`Docs/DECISIONS.md`).","+- **Stories** group reprints of one story across papers, so each story is read once.","+- **Gold and dev,** 300 and 150 articles drawn across 17 strata, are labelled one article at a time under `eval/gold/POLICY.md` by an AI labeller (Claude), in a labelling page that shows the crop beside the text.","+  - A blind second pass relabelled all of gold and a seeded fifth of dev.","+  - Fresh judges ruled every disagreement again, blind.","+  - The labels are frozen by sha256 before any model output touched them.","+- **The reader is not trained yet.** Its training labels will come from an open-weight teacher run locally on this Mac; labels never come from Claude, and gold and dev are kept for evaluation only. Two teachers were compared on dev (`eval/results/phase2c/`):","+  - Qwen3.5-397B-A17B, through Tinker, until the spend stopped","+  - gemma4:26b-a4b-it-qat, through Ollama","+- **The student** is Qwen3.5-4B, to be fine-tuned with LoRA through mlx-lm.","+","+## What it can't do yet","+","+- The archive-wide pass hasn't run, so the demo shows only the 78 evaluation reports, not every ghost the papers printed.","+- The OCR is shown as printed. Some clippings are hard to read, and a quote is only as good as the scan's text.","+- A place is the paper's own words. Nothing is geocoded or mapped yet.","+","+## Data and licences","+","+- Article text: AmericanStories, from Harvard's Dell Research (`dell-research-harvard/AmericanStories`, CC-BY-4.0)","+- Page scans and clippings: Library of Congress, Chronicling America (no known copyright restrictions)","+- Fonts, self-hosted through Fontsource under the SIL Open Font License: UnifrakturMaguntia, Bodoni Moda, Newsreader and Courier Prime","+- Open-weight models: Qwen3.5-397B-A17B and Qwen3.5-4B (Qwen), and gemma4:26b-a4b-it-qat (Google)","+- The code is MIT licensed; see [LICENSE](LICENSE).","+","+## Development","+","+The plan is in [`Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md`](Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md), and where the build stands is in [`Docs/RESUME.md`](Docs/RESUME.md)."," ","-## Run it"," "," You need `uv`, Node with `pnpm`, the Temporal CLI and Ollama. Keys go in `.env`, which git ignores."," "]},{"oldStart":31,"oldLines":18,"newStart":83,"newLines":3,"lines":[" uv run python scripts/load_skeleton.py  # loads the Lewistown gazette's knockings into Atlas"," make app"," ```","-","-## What it can't do","-","-Filled in as limits are found.","-","-## Failure log","-","-Filled in as failures are found.","-","-## Credits","-","-- Article text: AmericanStories, from Harvard's Dell Research (CC-BY-4.0)","-- Page scans: Library of Congress, Chronicling America (public domain)","-","-The code is MIT licensed; see [LICENSE](LICENSE)."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/README.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"7f224156-c27f-4186-b116-c4094fb4516c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"submission","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c1befb8d-8acd-4878-ade6-0b73c7f997a0","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
