{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","id":"642dfea0-0121-45e1-b6b2-de47145257e6","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:03:03.164Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"7b35af0d1ba22d1b1b7d4c91038d50b583ea5d544dd1607adac5368903cb8a35","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"a8a2e30c-bdc4-4b20-a2dd-9cde1597bfe6","keep":248,"tail":["21af7321f38de2bcb00d48e2b177b9b44e6c889dfd34d3499f1987d8aa3b5879","4515e35153bd5c0bf6287ddede0dff2973aad6c3f3e22c00a8a7506733027e01"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",249,"content",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"afeae2eb76cd781c1c4a08d54523cc2d22d433703764d12b6c4fbe686ec5f2d7"}
{"parentUuid":"1d30b16b-5098-4dbe-bca6-6ce556e46d33","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb53HC5Risfh3oJofK6W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"SUBMISSION: DEMO READY at 8995499. The demo, the numbers sheet and the judges' README are all on `submission` (now at a1a3cb5, pushed and confirmed with ls-remote; 400 tests, lint, build and secret scan pass). The live reading demo is written but not run, and making the repo public is blocked on one redaction.\n\n- **The Morgue:** run `pnpm --dir web build && pnpm --dir web preview`, then open http://localhost:4173; `.claude/launch.json` also has it as \"morgue\".\n  - It shows the 78 reports (46 gold, 32 dev) with 205 clippings copied from the local crop cache (10 MB). Nothing was downloaded.\n  - Every clipping's Library of Congress link was rebuilt without any network call, and each one matches its cached image file.\n  - You can search by town, state or word, and filter by decade and outcome.\n  - Each report opens to its clipping beside the transcription, with the quoted words marked. An index card lists the fields, with \"Not stated\" where the paper didn't say.\n  - It has lights on and off, works at phone width, and all text has contrast of at least 4.5:1.\n- **The numbers:** run `uv run python scripts/article_numbers.py`. It writes `eval/results/numbers.json`, with the source file or doc line beside every number.\n  - It's not called `numbers.py`, because that name would hide Python's own `numbers` module and crash anything that loads numpy.\n- **The README for judges:** what the project is, how to run the demo and the numbers, where the work stands, what it can't do yet, and the licences for the data, fonts and models.\n- **Wording to check before the article quotes it:**\n  - **\"Hand-labelled\":** the gold and dev labels were made one article at a time by Claude (`labeller: \"Claude\"`). The blind second pass and the blind rulings were done by separate judges. The demo's footer says exactly that.\n  - **\"28 of 30\":** this is the settling step in DECISIONS.md. The blind re-ruling file's own figure is 28 of 34 kind rulings matching the first ones.\n  - **Decision 39:** the docs cite it, but it was never written into DECISIONS.md.\n- **The secret scan, over all history including Entire's saved sessions:**\n  - No secrets found, and the hostname appears nowhere.\n  - The four MongoDB addresses are test fixtures.\n  - Two `.env` values do appear, but they're plain names the docs already print: the Sentry project name and a model name.\n\nTwo decisions are with the owner's session:\n\n1. **Context size for `read_one`:** the full prompt runs 9,500 to 11,300 tokens, which doesn't fit in the 4,096 you set. Either use 12,288 for this single run with nothing else running, or keep 4,096 and drop POLICY.md from the prompt. Ollama stays off until you choose.\n2. **The other account's process list** from step 1.7 is inside Entire's saved sessions on GitHub, and it blocks going public. Either I rewrite those saved sessions and force-push them, which is hard to undo and may break Entire's own checks, or the public copy leaves Entire's sessions out. I won't touch them until you say."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1252,"cache_read_input_tokens":296508,"output_tokens":1066,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1252,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1066,"cache_read_input_tokens":296508,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1252,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1252},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostic