{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","hash":"33d027e21c8c5c76c2f676d0f8843c8228d4141c3ae9a18af18abba500e4bc0e","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Two sessions conflict: the owner's wants `read_one` at num_ctx 12288, while the kickoff one wants it dropped with Ollama off. I'll keep Ollama off as the safer choice, ask once for a decision, and start the shared work with Atlas.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019eittTZDmbguLc3A4hvKV9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"date \"+%H:%M %Z\"; cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && git status --short | head; ls paperghosts/store/; grep -n \"^def \\|MONGODB\\|DB_NAME\\|database\" paperghosts/store/*.py | head -30; grep -n \"^[A-Z_]*=\" .env | cut -d= -f1 | tr '\\n' ' '","description":"Check the time, tree state, and existing Atlas code"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015tdrSvPFk5a8ZaoTvh9w22","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"local_cbd6aed2-f42a-4724-8982-8a86e51899ae","summary":"Flag the read_one conflict between sessions","message":"Conflict on step 3: you said run read_one at num_ctx 12288, but the kickoff session (local_98906164) says the owner now forbids any Ollama or mlx-lm run and wants gemma4's recorded dev outputs used as the proof instead. Which stands? Until one of you confirms with the owner, Ollama stays off. Meanwhile I'm doing what both lists share:\n- Atlas: load and query scripts, upsert only, keys from the environment\n- render.yaml, never deployed by me\n- decision 39 in DECISIONS.md\n- clean headlines first in the list, and the paper's own printed-in place\n- the Tinker and Entire figures in the numbers sheet\nThe kickoff list also asks for Atlas Search and Vector Search, a brand sheet, a logo, and more pages. I'll take those in order as time allows and report what's left."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
