{"parentUuid":"7fc9dd41-91bd-4961-93b0-136c3a5d22e1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6c483b0a-cf7c-4711-85d5-56f30a3e6823","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FMwP3roMdNPp8iEfs31zRX","type":"tool_result","content":"**38. Gold and dev are labelled by hand under `POLICY.md`, all 450 through the page's `checked()`. A blind second pass relabels all of gold and a seeded fifth of dev. On gold it agrees with the first pass on 271 of 300 kinds (κ 0.88, 0.84–0.92) and on 296 of 300 report-or-not calls (κ 0.95). Eve\n\n- **The first pass:** I labelled all 300 gold and 150 dev articles in batches of 20. They came in the page's seeded order, with no stratum or weight in view, and each batch was committed as it was done.\n  - Every label passes `checked()`: its kind is `POLICY.md`'s, its fields are a report's only, every value has its quote in the text, and every choice is the schema's.\n  - **Crops:** 443 of the 450 articles have them, cached one article at a time at loc.gov's pace. The other 7 fail the page check, or have too few words to check. I read the crop wherever the OCR was unclear. Eight dev labels were made before their crops arrived, so I read those crops afterwards and\n- **Calls `POLICY.md` left to the labeller,** made the same way in gold and dev:\n  - An apparition of the living is a report when a figure is seen, as with Buller's sight of Wolseley.\n  - An essay or sermon that tells several particular claims takes its fields from the first one told in particulars. Examples: Scott's sight of the dead Byron in the Westminster Review's essay on hallucinations, and Slade's slate-writing in the Boston Pilot's round-up of exposures.\n  - A column of short items under one heading is one article. Rule 16 and E11 are kept for segmentation errors: an item's tail, or an advert, joined to another.\n  - E1 marks the Holy Ghost in religious matter. A joke's catechism or a pioneer tale's blazes are not E1.\n## Spend stopped (2026-10-31): no Tinker spend, and 2C runs locally (decision 39)\n\n- **The balance was $0.00.** The owner's console showed a remaining credit balance of $0.00, with $0.80 of unpaid usage due this month. I had taken the account's past usage for evidence of credits left. It wasn't, so today's runs were billed to the owner's card without a yes.\n- **Today's Tinker use,** from each run's recorded tokens (billing hadn't caught up when the spend stopped):\n\n  | Job | Prompt tokens | Generated tokens | Cost, all cached to none |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | credit check, teacher, 50 articles | 456,246 | 3,630 | $0.30–1.40 |\n  | credit check, 4B, 50 articles | 47,396 | 3,330 | $0.01–0.02 |\n  | teacher on dev, round 1, 150 | 1,373,823 | 15,087 | $0.94–4.23 |\n  | teacher on dev, round 2, 150 | 1,408,773 | 15,820 | $0.96–4.34 |\n  | teacher on dev, round 3, 150 | 1,449,123 | 14,930 | $0.98–4.46 |\n  | probes | 56 | 12 | under $0.01 |\n  | **all** | **4,735,417** | **52,809** | **$3.19–14.45** |\n\n  - **The thinking round** was refused by Tinker's billing block (HTTP 402) and stopped, and it saved no answer. Any requests served before the block aren't recorded: at most 150 prompts of about 9,400 tokens, or $4.2 more at the uncached rate.\n  - Loading the gpt-oss and Kimi tokenizers cost nothing.\n- **From now on Tinker sampling is off in code:** `teacher.read` refuses unless `TINKER_SPEND_ALLOWED=1` is set, which needs the owner's yes. Reading billing stays free.\n- **Disk:** today's two downloads, Ollama's `qwen3.5:4b` (6.6 GB) and the Qwen3.5-4B weights for mlx-lm (8.7 GB), took free disk from 30 GB to 15 GB. That is the floor, so no further model fits. Deleting either is the owner's call.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"bf7afd96-2904-4a7e-b36f-3568158c2c36","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:07:12.629Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"**38. Gold and dev are labelled by hand under `POLICY.md`, all 450 through the page's `checked()`. A blind second pass relabels all of gold and a seeded fifth of dev. On gold it agrees with the first pass on 271 of 300 kinds (κ 0.88, 0.84–0.92) and on 296 of 300 report-or-not calls (κ 0.95). Eve\n\n- **The first pass:** I labelled all 300 gold and 150 dev articles in batches of 20. They came in the page's seeded order, with no stratum or weight in view, and each batch was committed as it was done.\n  - Every label passes `checked()`: its kind is `POLICY.md`'s, its fields are a report's only, every value has its quote in the text, and every choice is the schema's.\n  - **Crops:** 443 of the 450 articles have them, cached one article at a time at loc.gov's pace. The other 7 fail the page check, or have too few words to check. I read the crop wherever the OCR was unclear. Eight dev labels were made before their crops arrived, so I read those crops afterwards and\n- **Calls `POLICY.md` left to the labeller,** made the same way in gold and dev:\n  - An apparition of the living is a report when a figure is seen, as with Buller's sight of Wolseley.\n  - An essay or sermon that tells several particular claims takes its fields from the first one told in particulars. Examples: Scott's sight of the dead Byron in the Westminster Review's essay on hallucinations, and Slade's slate-writing in the Boston Pilot's round-up of exposures.\n  - A column of short items under one heading is one article. Rule 16 and E11 are kept for segmentation errors: an item's tail, or an advert, joined to another.\n  - E1 marks the Holy Ghost in religious matter. A joke's catechism or a pioneer tale's blazes are not E1.\n## Spend stopped (2026-10-31): no Tinker spend, and 2C runs locally (decision 39)\n\n- **The balance was $0.00.** The owner's console showed a remaining credit balance of $0.00, with $0.80 of unpaid usage due this month. I had taken the account's past usage for evidence of credits left. It wasn't, so today's runs were billed to the owner's card without a yes.\n- **Today's Tinker use,** from each run's recorded tokens (billing hadn't caught up when the spend stopped):\n\n  | Job | Prompt tokens | Generated tokens | Cost, all cached to none |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | credit check, teacher, 50 articles | 456,246 | 3,630 | $0.30–1.40 |\n  | credit check, 4B, 50 articles | 47,396 | 3,330 | $0.01–0.02 |\n  | teacher on dev, round 1, 150 | 1,373,823 | 15,087 | $0.94–4.23 |\n  | teacher on dev, round 2, 150 | 1,408,773 | 15,820 | $0.96–4.34 |\n  | teacher on dev, round 3, 150 | 1,449,123 | 14,930 | $0.98–4.46 |\n  | probes | 56 | 12 | under $0.01 |\n  | **all** | **4,735,417** | **52,809** | **$3.19–14.45** |\n\n  - **The thinking round** was refused by Tinker's billing block (HTTP 402) and stopped, and it saved no answer. Any requests served before the block aren't recorded: at most 150 prompts of about 9,400 tokens, or $4.2 more at the uncached rate.\n  - Loading the gpt-oss and Kimi tokenizers cost nothing.\n- **From now on Tinker sampling is off in code:** `teacher.read` refuses unless `TINKER_SPEND_ALLOWED=1` is set, which needs the owner's yes. Reading billing stays free.\n- **Disk:** today's two downloads, Ollama's `qwen3.5:4b` (6.6 GB) and the Qwen3.5-4B weights for mlx-lm (8.7 GB), took free disk from 30 GB to 15 GB. That is the floor, so no further model fits. Deleting either is the owner's call.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"974e67f5-6da0-44c4-8553-93b694a2a47a","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"submission","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":4,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"priv