{"parentUuid":"fdcd45e3-3b3d-49bb-a011-4b7ff385a923","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb5ztshpAB1fW8AYa6gK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Every pairing passes AA in both lights. Now `Docs/BRAND.md`:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":550,"cache_read_input_tokens":379601,"output_tokens":1526,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":15},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":550,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1526,"cache_read_input_tokens":379601,"cache_creation_input_tokens":550,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":550},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c313fefc-f799-45a8-bd31-9dd70076a2ac","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgb5zt84e7e6YjdRAqG4L","requestRef":"cdc04b98-5a78-41cb-83c5-1b2dcd5f564e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f266b416-7fc3-4d8f-8525-e86a60d95229","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:15:39.690Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"f266b416-7fc3-4d8f-8525-e86a60d95229","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb5ztshpAB1fW8AYa6gK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014QE9hLT5tWYd9gnx6vK5AY","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BRAND.md","content":"# Paper Ghosts: brand\n\n**Name:** Paper Ghosts. The site is **The Morgue**: the room where a newspaper keeps its clippings. The look comes from `Docs/UI-IDEAS.md`: a newspaper morgue after hours.\n\n## The mark\n- **What it is:** a newspaper page that is itself the ghost.\n  - The bottom edge is torn into a ghost's hem.\n  - Two hollow, drooping eyes and an open mouth sit in its columns.\n  - It has a nameplate bar, column rules and a dog-eared corner in oxblood.\n- **Files,** in `web/public/brand/`, all drawn by hand as SVG:\n  - `logo.svg`, the full-colour mark\n  - `logo-mono.svg`, one colour (`currentColor`), with the fold, eyes, mouth and rules cut out of the page\n  - `logo-16.png` to `logo-512.png`, rendered from `logo.svg`\n  - `social-card.svg` and `social-card.jpg`, 1200×630\n- **At 16 px** the eyes and mouth still read; the hem blurs into an edge.\n- **Never** add a glow, a gradient or a drop shadow to the mark.\n\n## Colour\nThe tokens are in `web/src/index.css`, for two lights: lights on, the archive by day, and lights off, the reading room.\n\n| Token | Lights on | Lights off | Where |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `--bg` | newsprint `#E9E2D0` | reading-room dark `#111214` | the page |\n| `--text` | ink `#1B1916` | newsprint `#E9E2D0` | reading text |\n| `--card` | `#F4EEDF` | `#1A1B1E` | an open case |\n| `--envelope` | manila `#D9C79F` | `#1D1C1A` | a closed report |\n| `--muted` | `#4A4339` | `#B9B09C` | labels and notes |\n| `--stamp-ink` | oxblood `#8A2920` | `#E0796D` | outcome stamps only |\n| `--link` | blue pencil `#2F5C9E` | `#8DAEE3` | links and the archive's notes |\n| `--lamp` | ghost light `#F0C987` | the same | the lamp, quote marks and focus rings |\n| `--rule` | foxing `#8C6A43` | `#6E5537` | thin rules |\n\n`uv run python scripts/check_contrast.py` checks every text pairing against WCAG AA (4.5:1). All 20 pass, from 5.17 to 15.15, and `tests/test_check_contrast.py` keeps them passing.\n\n## Type\nAll four are Google Fonts, self-hosted through Fontsource, so the page never calls Google:\n- **UnifrakturMaguntia,** blackletter, for the nameplate only\n- **Bodoni Moda** for headline decks\n- **Newsreader** for reading text and transcriptions\n- **Courier Prime** for labels, dates, filing numbers and stamps\n\n## Voice\nThe archive's librarian: plain, dry and exact.\n- Say what the paper printed and what it didn't: \"Story place not stated\", \"Outcome unknown\".\n- Never sensational: no \"spooky\", no puns, no \"chilling\".\n- Never say the site holds \"every ghost\". It holds the reports it has filed, and says how many.\n- A report of hearing voices or of insanity (`POLICY.md` rule 2) gets no ghostly framing, only what the text says.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":550,"cache_read_input_tokens":379601,"output_tokens":1526,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":15},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":550,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1526,"cache_read_input_tokens":379601,"cache_creation_input_tokens":550,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":550},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014QE9hLT5tWYd9gnx6vK5AY":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BRAND.md","content":"# Paper Ghosts: brand\n\n**Name:** Paper Ghosts. The site is **The Morgue**: the room where a newspaper keeps its clippings. The look comes from `Docs/UI-IDEAS.md`: a newspaper morgue after hours.\n\n## The mark\n- **What it is:** a newspaper page that is itself the ghost.\n  - The bottom edge is torn into a ghost's hem.\n  - Two hollow, drooping eyes and an open mouth sit in its columns.\n  - It has a nameplate bar, column rules and a dog-eared corner in oxblood.\n- **Files,** in `web/public/brand/`, all drawn by hand as SVG:\n  - `logo.svg`, the full-colour mark\n  - `logo-mono.svg`, one colour (`currentColor`), with the fold, eyes, mouth and rules cut out of the page\n  - `logo-16.png` to `logo-512.png`, rendered from `logo.svg`\n  - `social-card.svg` and `social-card.jpg`, 1200×630\n- **At 16 px** the eyes and mouth still read; the hem blurs into an edge.\n- **Never** add a glow, a gradient or a drop shadow to the mark.\n\n## Colour\nThe tokens are in `web/src/index.css`, for two lights: lights on, the archive by day, and lights off, the reading room.\n\n| Token | Lights on | Lights off | Where |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `--bg` | newsprint `#E9E2D0` | reading-room dark `#111214` | the page |\n| `--text` | ink `#1B1916` | newsprint `#E9E2D0` | reading text |\n| `--card` | `#F4EEDF` | `#1A1B1E` | an open case |\n| `--envelope` | manila `#D9C79F` | `#1D1C1A` | a closed report |\n| `--muted` | `#4A4339` | `#B9B09C` | labels and notes |\n| `--stamp-ink` | oxblood `#8A2920` | `#E0796D` | outcome stamps only |\n| `--link` | blue pencil `#2F5C9E` | `#8DAEE3` | links and the archive's notes |\n| `--lamp` | ghost light `#F0C987` | the same | the lamp, quote marks and focus rings |\n| `--rule` | foxing `#8C6A43` | `#6E5537` | thin rules |\n\n`uv run python scripts/check_contrast.py` checks every text pairing against WCAG AA (4.5:1). All 20 pass, from 5.17 to 15.15, and `tests/test_check_contrast.py` keeps them passing.\n\n## Type\nAll four are Google Fonts, self-hosted through Fontsource, so the page never calls Google:\n- **UnifrakturMaguntia,** blackletter, for the nameplate only\n- **Bodoni Moda** for headline decks\n- **Newsreader** for reading text and transcriptions\n- **Courier Prime** for labels, dates, filing numbers and stamps\n\n## Voice\nThe archive's librarian: plain, dry and exact.\n- Say what the paper printed and what it didn't: \"Story place not stated\", \"Outcome unknown\".\n- Never sensational: no \"spooky\", no puns, no \"chilling\".\n- Never say the site holds \"every ghost\". It holds the reports it has filed, and says how many.\n- A report of hearing voices or of insanity (`POLICY.md` rule 2) gets no ghostly framing, only what the text says.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c313fefc-f799-45a8-bd31-9dd70076a2ac","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgb5zt84e7e6YjdRAqG4L","requestRef":"cdc04b98-5a78-41cb-83c5-1b2dcd5f564e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"95260f1c-50f4-4730-8d5e-db20b2fa5dc7","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:15:50.282Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
