{"parentUuid":"7c0ae93f-effb-48b9-aded-b9026fe3b09e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6c483b0a-cf7c-4711-85d5-56f30a3e6823","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LqTzamv2LSE3g8kVt85syU","type":"tool_result","content":"5:Each rule names an example by article id, from items eval A and lexicon v2 judged (decisions 27, 30 and 31). The draw leaves out version 1's examples and their groups. Version 2's new examples were checked to be outside gold and dev, their groups and their reprints. An example's label here is this policy's, which can differ from the earlier judgment: rule 2 changes one.\n31:2. **Delusions and hallucinations, one rule.** A person's claim to have seen, heard or felt a ghost or spirit, on a particular occasion, is a report.\n33:   - Where the text calls the claim a delusion, a hallucination or insanity, the outcome is `explained`.\n35:   - 1909: a lunacy hearing, with spooks among a man's claims of persecution (`24_1909-08-31_p1_sn83025121_00294552327_1909083101_0987.json`): report, explained. **This overrules eval A's `other`.**\n36:   - With no ghost or spirit claimed, a delusion is `other`. 1917: an insane man believes he is an aeroplane (`32_1917-11-02_pna_sn84024827_00211104776_1917110201_0388.json`).\n✓ built in 218ms","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5552a998-9230-402e-8abc-d8ede4e1dcf9","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:15:53.192Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"5:Each rule names an example by article id, from items eval A and lexicon v2 judged (decisions 27, 30 and 31). The draw leaves out version 1's examples and their groups. Version 2's new examples were checked to be outside gold and dev, their groups and their reprints. An example's label here is this policy's, which can differ from the earlier judgment: rule 2 changes one.\n31:2. **Delusions and hallucinations, one rule.** A person's claim to have seen, heard or felt a ghost or spirit, on a particular occasion, is a report.\n33:   - Where the text calls the claim a delusion, a hallucination or insanity, the outcome is `explained`.\n35:   - 1909: a lunacy hearing, with spooks among a man's claims of persecution (`24_1909-08-31_p1_sn83025121_00294552327_1909083101_0987.json`): report, explained. **This overrules eval A's `other`.**\n36:   - With no ghost or spirit claimed, a delusion is `other`. 1917: an insane man believes he is an aeroplane (`32_1917-11-02_pna_sn84024827_00211104776_1917110201_0388.json`).\n✓ built in 218ms","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"c313fefc-f799-45a8-bd31-9dd70076a2ac","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"submission","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":3,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":3},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7c0ae93f-effb-48b9-aded-b9026fe3b09e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
