{"parentUuid":"299bffdf-94c2-4b4a-8a67-f2dcdafcd469","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb6S3gjb9VZKo65rFzvM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Each checkpoint holds the full transcript, about 120 MB, including the step-1.7 process list, so these sessions need the same redaction before embedding. I'm noting this for the owner and updating the README next.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":914,"cache_read_input_tokens":409950,"output_tokens":2009,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":182},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":914,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2009,"cache_read_input_tokens":409950,"cache_creation_input_tokens":914,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":914},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"06e384be-9724-4522-ae3f-ace708290902","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgb6S2nQcf2r5Cyt3epQM","requestRef":"8d813129-3b03-4235-b05e-fbbedc559657","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"cb31239b-088b-416d-b4a2-bd47aa084978","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:21:22.938Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"cb31239b-088b-416d-b4a2-bd47aa084978","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb6S3gjb9VZKo65rFzvM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015EgBuXQKkwnHm5V6eVPKuc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && cat > Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md <<'EOF'\n# Entire: the build's paper trail\n\nEntire records each commit's agent session as a checkpoint. A commit names its checkpoint in an\n`Entire-Checkpoint:` trailer, and the checkpoint is a ref, `refs/entire/checkpoints/<last two\ncharacters>/<id>`, pushed to origin. `scripts/article_numbers.py` counts them: 122 commits carry\nthe trailer, across 123 refs.\n\n## Two sessions that show the problem solving\n\n| What it shows | Commit | Checkpoint |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Reprint chaining, and its fix:** chained clusters grew through near matches, so a printing now joins a story only by matching its first printing directly | `1a2f8b7` | `01M67W8SMF2WGS6DNG76TSEAXP` |\n| **A judge ruling its own case, caught:** the first rulings were the first labeller's, so fresh judges re-ruled all 69 disputes blind, and the blind ruling was taken in 28 of the 30 that differed | `537e605`, `35e8a53` | `01M69P1PXCDRMN4FCBZRDQAGV2`, `01M69PCNVRXPX8DD1EWAHB57JF` |\n\n## Before either is published\n- **The secret scan has passed:** all history, all 123 checkpoint refs. No secret, and the hostname nowhere. The 4 MongoDB URIs are test fixtures. Two `.env` values appear, but they're plain names the docs print: the Sentry project and a model name.\n- **Not yet redacted:** each checkpoint holds the whole accumulated transcript (about 120 MB). Its `0/full.jsonl` includes step 1.7's process listing, which names another local account and its browsers' paths. It has to be redacted before a session is embedded or the repo goes public. That means rewriting the checkpoint refs and force-pushing them, so it's the owner's call.\n- **Publishing** a session as \"My Agent Session\" on DEV is the owner's step.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"README.md\"); s = p.read_text()\ns = s.replace(\"# Paper Ghosts\\n\", '# Paper Ghosts\\n\\n<img src=\"web/public/brand/logo.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\">\\n', 1)\nold = \"## The numbers\"\nassert old in s\ns = s.replace(old, \"\"\"### Its rooms\n- **The drawer:** search by town, state or word, and filter by decade, outcome and the state the paper was printed in.\n  - Each report opens into its clipping beside its transcription, with the verified quotes marked.\n  - An index card lists every field, VERIFIED or \"Not stated\".\n  - It gives the paper's own place, labelled as the paper's, not the story's.\n  - It lists the five ghosts like it.\n- **Paper samples:** the clearest scan for each outcome, captioned only with its verified quotes.\n- **How we know:** every figure from the numbers sheet, with its interval, including the teacher benchmark.\n\nDeploying is a static site: `render.yaml` builds `web/` and publishes `web/dist`. The bundle holds no keys.\n\n### MongoDB Atlas\n```bash\nuv run python scripts/load_demo_atlas.py               # upserts the 78 into paperghosts.reports; never deletes\nuv run python scripts/query_demo_atlas.py \"apparition\" # Atlas Search, fuzzy: finds the OCR's \"apparilion\"\nuv run python scripts/query_demo_atlas.py --like <article_id>   # ghosts like this one (moreLikeThis)\n```\n\nThe keys come from `MONGODB_URI` in `.env`.\n- The reports go in as the planned `Report` documents, and Atlas's own validator checks them.\n- The site's \"ghosts like this one\" is Atlas's answer, saved by `scripts/export_like.py`, so the static build works offline.\n- Sample outputs are in `Docs/demo/`.\n\n## The numbers\"\"\", 1)\nold = \"## Data and licences\"\ns = s.replace(old, \"\"\"## AI disclosure\n- **Claude** wrote the code, under the owner's direction, and labelled the 450 evaluation articles under the labelling policy, one at a time. The second pass and the blind re-rulings were done by separate Claude judges that couldn't see the first labels.\n- **Open-weight models do the reading:** Qwen3.5-397B through Tinker and gemma4:26b on this Mac were scored as teachers on dev. Training labels never come from Claude.\n- **Entire** recorded every agent session; `Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md` points to two of them.\n\n## Brand\n`Docs/BRAND.md` covers the brand: the hand-drawn mark (`web/public/brand/`), the colour tokens with their WCAG AA check (`scripts/check_contrast.py`), the type and the voice.\n\n## Data and licences\"\"\", 1)\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ngrep -n \"^## \\|^### \" README.md","description":"Write the Entire sessions note and extend the README"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":914,"cache_read_input_tokens":409950,"output_tokens":2009,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":182},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":914,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2009,"cache_read_input_tokens":409950,"cache_creation_input_tokens":914,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":914},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015EgBuXQKkwnHm5V6eVPKuc":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && cat > Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md <<'EOF'\n# Entire: the build's paper trail\n\nEntire records each commit's agent session as a checkpoint. A commit names its checkpoint in an\n`Entire-Checkpoint:` trailer, and the checkpoint is a ref, `refs/entire/checkpoints/<last two\ncharacters>/<id>`, pushed to origin. `scripts/article_numbers.py` counts them: 122 commits carry\nthe trailer, across 123 refs.\n\n## Two sessions that show the problem solving\n\n| What it shows | Commit | Checkpoint |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Reprint chaining, and its fix:** chained clusters grew through near matches, so a printing now joins a story only by matching its first printing directly | `1a2f8b7` | `01M67W8SMF2WGS6DNG76TSEAXP` |\n| **A judge ruling its own case, caught:** the first rulings were the first labeller's, so fresh judges re-ruled all 69 disputes blind, and the blind ruling was taken in 28 of the 30 that differed | `537e605`, `35e8a53` | `01M69P1PXCDRMN4FCBZRDQAGV2`, `01M69PCNVRXPX8DD1EWAHB57JF` |\n\n## Before either is published\n- **The secret scan has passed:** all history, all 123 checkpoint refs. No secret, and the hostname nowhere. The 4 MongoDB URIs are test fixtures. Two `.env` values appear, but they're plain names the docs print: the Sentry project and a model name.\n- **Not yet redacted:** each checkpoint holds the whole accumulated transcript (about 120 MB). Its `0/full.jsonl` includes step 1.7's process listing, which names another local account and its browsers' paths. It has to be redacted before a session is embedded or the repo goes public. That means rewriting the checkpoint refs and force-pushing them, so it's the owner's call.\n- **Publishing** a session as \"My Agent Session\" on DEV is the owner's step.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"README.md\"); s = p.read_text()\ns = s.replace(\"# Paper Ghosts\\n\", '# Paper Ghosts\\n\\n<img src=\"web/public/brand/logo.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\">\\n', 1)\nold = \"## The numbers\"\nassert old in s\ns = s.replace(old, \"\"\"### Its rooms\n- **The drawer:** search by town, state or word, and filter by decade, outcome and the state the paper was printed in.\n  - Each report opens into its clipping beside its transcription, with the verified quotes marked.\n  - An index card lists every field, VERIFIED or \"Not stated\".\n  - It gives the paper's own place, labelled as the paper's, not the story's.\n  - It lists the five ghosts like it.\n- **Paper samples:** the clearest scan for each outcome, captioned only with its verified quotes.\n- **How we know:** every figure from the numbers sheet, with its interval, including the teacher benchmark.\n\nDeploying is a static site: `render.yaml` builds `web/` and publishes `web/dist`. The bundle holds no keys.\n\n### MongoDB Atlas\n```bash\nuv run python scripts/load_demo_atlas.py               # upserts the 78 into paperghosts.reports; never deletes\nuv run python scripts/query_demo_atlas.py \"apparition\" # Atlas Search, fuzzy: finds the OCR's \"apparilion\"\nuv run python scripts/query_demo_atlas.py --like <article_id>   # ghosts like this one (moreLikeThis)\n```\n\nThe keys come from `MONGODB_URI` in `.env`.\n- The reports go in as the planned `Report` documents, and Atlas's own validator checks them.\n- The site's \"ghosts like this one\" is Atlas's answer, saved by `scripts/export_like.py`, so the static build works offline.\n- Sample outputs are in `Docs/demo/`.\n\n## The numbers\"\"\", 1)\nold = \"## Data and licences\"\ns = s.replace(old, \"\"\"## AI disclosure\n- **Claude** wrote the code, under the owner's direction, and labelled the 450 evaluation articles under the labelling policy, one at a time. The second pass and the blind re-rulings were done by separate Claude judges that couldn't see the first labels.\n- **Open-weight models do the reading:** Qwen3.5-397B through Tinker and gemma4:26b on this Mac were scored as teachers on dev. Training labels never come from Claude.\n- **Entire** recorded every agent session; `Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md` points to two of them.\n\n## Brand\n`Docs/BRAND.md` covers the brand: the hand-drawn mark (`web/public/brand/`), the colour tokens with their WCAG AA check (`scripts/check_contrast.py`), the type and the voice.\n\n## Data and licences\"\"\", 1)\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ngrep -n \"^## \\|^### \" README.md","description":"Write the Entire sessions note and extend the README"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"06e384be-9724-4522-ae3f-ace708290902","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgb6S2nQcf2r5Cyt3epQM","requestRef":"8d813129-3b03-4235-b05e-fbbedc559657","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"dc857193-caf0-48b0-8218-34b5c05d9457","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:21:37.768Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"dc857193-caf0-48b0-8218-34b5c05d9457","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6c483b0a-cf7c-4711-85d5-56f30a3e6823","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015EgBuXQKkwnHm5V6eVPKuc","type":"tool_result","content":"7:## The demo: the Morgue\n19:### Its rooms\n30:### MongoDB Atlas\n42:## The numbers\n54:## How it was made, and where it stands\n67:## What it can't do yet\n73:## AI disclosure\n78:## Brand\n81:## Data and licences\n89:## Development","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f0730da8-ee96-401e-81b4-42255acd8605","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:21:39.277Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"7:## The demo: the Morgue\n19:### Its rooms\n30:### MongoDB Atlas\n42:## The numbers\n54:## How it was made, and where it stands\n67:## What it can't do yet\n73:## AI disclosure\n78:## Brand\n81:## Data and licences\n89:## Development","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":18,"lines":["+# Entire: the build's paper trail","+","+Entire records each commit's agent session as a checkpoint. A commit names its checkpoint in an","+`Entire-Checkpoint:` trailer, and the checkpoint is a ref, `refs/entire/checkpoints/<last two","+characters>/<id>`, pushed to origin. `scripts/article_numbers.py` counts them: 122 commits carry","+the trailer, across 123 refs.","+","+## Two sessions that show the problem solving","+","+| What it shows | Commit | Checkpoint |","+|---|---|---|","+| **Reprint chaining, and its fix:** chained clusters grew through near matches, so a printing now joins a story only by matching its first printing directly | `1a2f8b7` | `01M67W8SMF2WGS6DNG76TSEAXP` |","+| **A judge ruling its own case, caught:** the first rulings were the first labeller's, so fresh judges re-ruled all 69 disputes blind, and the blind ruling was taken in 28 of the 30 that differed | `537e605`, `35e8a53` | `01M69P1PXCDRMN4FCBZRDQAGV2`, `01M69PCNVRXPX8DD1EWAHB57JF` |","+","+## Before either is published","+- **The secret scan has passed:** all history, all 123 checkpoint refs. No secret, and the hostname nowhere. The 4 MongoDB URIs are test fixtures. Two `.env` values appear, but they're plain names the docs print: the Sentry project and a model name.","+- **Not yet redacted:** each checkpoint holds the whole accumulated transcript (about 120 MB). Its `0/full.jsonl` includes step 1.7's process listing, which names another local account and its browsers' paths. It has to be redacted before a session is embedded or the repo goes public. That means rewriting the checkpoint refs and force-pushing them, so it's the owner's call.","+- **Publishing** a session as \"My Agent Session\" on DEV is the owner's step."]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":5,"newStart":1,"newLines":7,"lines":[" # Paper Ghosts"," ","+<img src=\"web/public/brand/logo.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\">","+"," A morgue of ghost reports from American newspapers, 1774–1963. Paper Ghosts reads the AmericanStories OCR of the Library of Congress's page scans, picks out the articles that report a ghost, and files each one with the exact words of the scan that state its place, what was seen and how it ended. The site never writes a ghost story: every value on it is a quote, and every report links to its clipping."," "," ## The demo: the Morgue"]},{"oldStart":14,"oldLines":6,"newStart":16,"newLines":29,"lines":[" "," `uv run python scripts/export_demo.py` rebuilds its data, `web/public/reports.json` and the clippings in `web/public/crops/`, from the frozen labels and the local crop cache, and fetches nothing."," ","+### Its rooms","+- **The drawer:** search by town, state or word, and filter by decade, outcome and the state the paper was printed in.","+  - Each report opens into its clipping beside its transcription, with the verified quotes marked.","+  - An index card lists every field, VERIFIED or \"Not stated\".","+  - It gives the paper's own place, labelled as the paper's, not the story's.","+  - It lists the five ghosts like it.","+- **Paper samples:** the clearest scan for each outcome, captioned only with its verified quotes.","+- **How we know:** every figure from the numbers sheet, with its interval, including the teacher benchmark.","+","+Deploying is a static site: `render.yaml` builds `web/` and publishes `web/dist`. The bundle holds no keys.","+","+### MongoDB Atlas","+```bash","+uv run python scripts/load_demo_atlas.py               # upserts the 78 into paperghosts.reports; never deletes","+uv run python scripts/query_demo_atlas.py \"apparition\" # Atlas Search, fuzzy: finds the OCR's \"apparilion\"","+uv run python scripts/query_demo_atlas.py --like <article_id>   # ghosts like this one (moreLikeThis)","+```","+","+The keys come from `MONGODB_URI` in `.env`.","+- The reports go in as the planned `Report` documents, and Atlas's own validator checks them.","+- The site's \"ghosts like this one\" is Atlas's answer, saved by `scripts/export_like.py`, so the static build works offline.","+- Sample outputs are in `Docs/demo/`.","+"," ## The numbers"," "," ```bash"]},{"oldStart":45,"oldLines":6,"newStart":70,"newLines":14,"lines":[" - The OCR is shown as printed. Some clippings are hard to read, and a quote is only as good as the scan's text."," - A place is the paper's own words. Nothing is geocoded or mapped yet."," ","+## AI disclosure","+- **Claude** wrote the code, under the owner's direction, and labelled the 450 evaluation articles under the labelling policy, one at a time. The second pass and the blind re-rulings were done by separate Claude judges that couldn't see the first labels.","+- **Open-weight models do the reading:** Qwen3.5-397B through Tinker and gemma4:26b on this Mac were scored as teachers on dev. Training labels never come from Claude.","+- **Entire** recorded every agent session; `Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md` points to two of them.","+","+## Brand","+`Docs/BRAND.md` covers the brand: the hand-drawn mark (`web/public/brand/`), the colour tokens with their WCAG AA check (`scripts/check_contrast.py`), the type and the voice.","+"," ## Data and licences"," "," - Article text: AmericanStories, from Harvard's Dell Research (`dell-research-harvard/AmericanStories`, CC-BY-4.0)"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md","/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/README.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"06e384be-9724-4522-ae3f-ace708290902","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"submission","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dc857193-caf0-48b0-8218-34b5c05d9457","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny