{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","prNumber":4,"prUrl":"https://github.com/Hotragn/Paperghosts/pull/4","prRepository":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:26:53.015Z"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","hash":"e4b856cb545671832727abab5c270d24ccdd62b377755243bbda5d61357335fa","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Those three use another tool's temporary profiles (`muster-gp-*`), not mine, so I'm leaving them alone. Sending the report to both sessions:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AX4pGdVZdnwf6cqDBiSrZH","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e","summary":"Report submission status: blocked on the Entire redaction","message":"SUBMISSION: BLOCKED — the Entire redaction needs the owner's yes. Everything else for a public release is done at 383742b on `submission` (pushed, ls-remote matches; 403 tests, lint, build and AA contrast pass; no secrets in the bundle).\n\nDone:\n- **Honest claims.** All 370,313,913 articles were screened, and 1,236,122 candidates were found. The Morgue shows 78 reports labelled under the policy; the reader is untrained (decision 39, now in DECISIONS.md). Draft title: \"Paper Ghosts: 370 million newspaper articles screened for ghosts, and the 78 reports we can prove\".\n- **Printed in.** Each report gives the paper's place, from its cached title record or its LoC title, labelled as the paper's. 55 have a town, the rest their state or LCCN. Searchable and filterable. Clearest scans list first, and garbled headlines get a plain title.\n- **Atlas.** The 78 are upserted into paperghosts.reports as real Report documents, and Atlas's validator accepted them (140 KB, nothing deleted).\n  - Fuzzy Atlas Search through the existing reports_search index: \"apparition\" finds the OCR's \"apparilion\".\n  - moreLikeThis gives \"ghosts like this one\", median 68 ms, saved into the static build.\n  - Scripts: load_demo_atlas.py and query_demo_atlas.py. Outputs in Docs/demo.\n- **Tinker.** The How we know page has the 397B against gemma4 with intervals, the format-against-judgment finding, $65–297 per 10,000 articles from round 3's tokens, and the $3.19–14.45 spend on a $0 balance.\n- **Brand.** Docs/BRAND.md, the hand-drawn logo (web/public/brand/logo.svg, logo-mono.svg, logo-16/64/512.png) and the social card (social-card.jpg).\n- **Numbers.** Every figure comes from scripts/article_numbers.py, now with Entire's 122 checkpoints, the 1850 Stratford probe (20 articles, 2 naming the Phelps family) and the 6,342-against-6,567 candidate gap. The gap fits the articles held out, but wasn't checked one by one.\n- **README.** Updated with the AI disclosure. render.yaml is ready for a static site.\n- **Screenshots.** Docs/demo/screenshots/: 16 shots, every page (drawer, report, samples, how) in both lights, desktop and true 390 px phone.\n\nNot done:\n- **Vector Search:** no embedding. The planned embedder runs through Ollama, which is off, and torch isn't installed. moreLikeThis stands in.\n- **No 2dsphere \"near\":** no report has coordinates.\n- **No FastAPI routes:** a static site can't call them.\n- **read_one never ran:** you said no Ollama, and the other session said run it at 12288. gemma4's recorded dev outputs are the proof of open weights.\n\nBlocking public release: step 1.7's process list (another account's name and browser paths) is in Entire's 123 checkpoint refs on origin, inside each ~120 MB transcript, including the two sessions picked in Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md. Redacting means rewriting those refs and force-pushing them. I need the owner's yes for that.\n\nOwner actions: 1) yes or no on the Entire redaction; 2) make the repo public; 3) deploy render.yaml on Render, then set og:image to the absolute URL; 4) publish the post and any Entire session."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HL4gUYxGQeQcTMXgvALTst","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"local_cbd6aed2-f42a-4724-8982-8a86e51899ae","summary":"Report steps 3–5 and Atlas status to the owner's session","message":"SUBMISSION: BLOCKED — the Entire redaction needs the owner's yes. Atlas and steps 4–5 are pushed at 383742b on `submission` (ls-remote matches; 403 tests pass); step 3 never ran.\n- **Atlas:** load_demo_atlas.py upserts the 78 into paperghosts.reports as Report documents. Atlas's validator accepted them, and nothing was deleted.\n  - query_demo_atlas.py \"<town or word>\" runs a fuzzy Atlas Search: \"apparition\" finds the OCR's \"apparilion\".\n  - `--like <id>` gives \"ghosts like this one\". Outputs are in Docs/demo.\n- **Also done:**\n  - render.yaml for a static site, never deployed by me; no keys in the bundle\n  - decision 39 in DECISIONS.md\n  - clearest scans first, plain titles for garbled headlines, and the paper's printed-in place\n  - the numbers sheet now has Tinker's tokens, dev scores and price per 10,000 articles, plus Entire's 122 checkpoint commits\n  - brand, logo, the How we know and Paper samples pages, and 16 screenshots in Docs/demo/screenshots\n- **Step 3 never ran:** you said run read_one at num_ctx 12288; the kickoff session says the owner forbids any Ollama. I kept it off. gemma4's recorded dev outputs stand in. If the owner wants the live run, say so and I'll run it once, alone, then stop the model.\n- **Blocking public release:** the other account's process list is in all 123 Entire checkpoint refs on origin. Redacting it means rewriting those refs and force-pushing. I won't do that without the owner's yes.\n- **Owner actions:**\n  - yes or no on the Entire redaction\n  - make the repo public\n  - deploy render.yaml\n  - publish the post"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X4CpCUBD32M31onzRn6Vxg","name":"mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up","input":{"recap":"The Morgue, its Atlas data and search, the brand, the numbers sheet, the README and the screenshots are all pushed on `submission` (383742b). Making the repo public is blocked on one owner decision: rewriting Entire's checkpoint refs to redact another account's process list. The live gemma4 run hasn't happened, because the two sessions gave conflicting orders.","blocked":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","id":"4a912a4b-dc2f-44ab-8be4-aa6e0995e32a","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:26:53.067Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"7b35af0d1ba22d1b1b7d4c91038d50b583ea5d544dd1607adac5368903cb8a35","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"5e3ff8dd-86ad-4c6b-a8c3-72ae0f3b1ebc","keep":429,"tail":["e4b856cb545671832727abab5c270d24ccdd62b377755243bbda5d61357335fa","02d923262193c989bbde7d0fc6828eda5170a759570025eba415903c3d9ca5e3"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",430,"content",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"1c4dc7abc3b4d95d119d9178915a1ffffae19a7289f2a0227914abc1c3e55ef4"}
{"parentUuid":"ece36578-92c0-4251-b22e-3a0cc54e282b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb6rhCNvmfyWV1ye5Hbk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"SUBMISSION: BLOCKED — the repo can't go public until another local account's process list is redacted from Entire's saved sessions, and that needs your yes. Everything else is built and pushed at 383742b on `submission`, with 403 tests, lint, the build and the contrast check passing. The built site contains no keys.\n\n**What's done:**\n- **The Morgue,** a static site that works offline, with three pages:\n  - **The drawer:** clearest scans first. Garbled headlines get a plain title, the raw headline is shown beneath, and the text is never rewritten.\n    - Each report says where its paper was printed, from its cached title record or its LoC title, labelled as the paper's place. 55 of 78 have a town.\n    - Filters cover town or word, decade, outcome and printed-in state.\n    - Each report lists five \"ghosts like this one\".\n  - **Paper samples:** the clearest clipping for each outcome, captioned only with its verified quotes.\n  - **How we know:** every figure comes from the numbers sheet, each with its interval, including the 397B (Tinker) against gemma4 (local) teacher comparison.\n- **MongoDB Atlas:** the 78 reports are loaded into `paperghosts.reports`, and Atlas's own validator accepted all of them. Nothing was deleted.\n  - Search is fuzzy, so \"apparition\" finds a report whose OCR reads \"apparilion\".\n  - \"Ghosts like this one\" comes from Atlas Search (median 68 ms) and is saved into the site.\n- **Brand:** a hand-drawn logo (a newspaper page whose torn hem is a ghost's), favicons from 16 to 512 px, a social card, and `Docs/BRAND.md`. All 20 text colour pairings pass the WCAG AA contrast check.\n- **Numbers sheet:** `uv run python scripts/article_numbers.py` now also covers the Tinker figures, Entire's 122 checkpoint commits, and the 1850 Stratford probe (20 articles, 2 naming the Phelps family). It also shows the 6,342-candidate gap between the archive and the training pool. That gap fits the 6,567 articles held out of the pool, but it wasn't checked one by one.\n- **Docs:** decision 39 is in `DECISIONS.md`. The README has the AI disclosure and how to run everything. `render.yaml` is ready for Render.\n- **Screenshots:** 16 in `Docs/demo/screenshots/`, covering every page in light and dark, on desktop and at true 390 px phone width.\n\n**Not done:**\n- **Vector search:** no embeddings. The planned embedding model runs through Ollama, which stays off, and torch isn't installed. Atlas's \"more like this\" search stands in.\n- **\"Near this town\" search:** no report has coordinates yet.\n- **Live API:** a static site can't call one.\n- **The live gemma4 reading demo:** it hasn't run. One session said to run it, the other said no Ollama at all, so I kept Ollama off. gemma4's recorded dev outputs are the proof that open models do the reading.\n\nYour steps:\n1. **Decide on the redaction.** Step 1.7's process list (that account's name and browser paths) is inside all 123 saved Entire sessions on GitHub, including the two picked to show off in `Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md`. Redacting it means rewriting those saved sessions and force-pushing them. That's hard to undo and may break Entire's own checks. Should I do it, or should the public copy leave Entire's sessions out?\n2. Make the repo public.\n3. Deploy `render.yaml` on Render, then change `og:image` in `web/index.html` to the full URL of `social-card.jpg`.\n4. Publish the post, and any Entire session you want to show."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3090,"cache_read_input_tokens":435623,"output_tokens":1263,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3090,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1263,"cache_read_input_tokens":435623,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3090,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3090},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"49c3cad2-9ef7-43a0-a737-3488c647bad6","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgb6rgRkWTgofKMXFZHp8","requestRef":"4a912a4b-dc2f-44ab-8be4-aa6e0995e32a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"83a24301-6e47-45cf-b640-0af32382be90","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:27:05.273Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
