{"parentUuid":"2a5d3407-5e7f-434c-af9e-2203616f246c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"98c3ee58-16ac-4e07-a418-568231f6b1de","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PDjNUAfAQ56gyTjs1NeMTv","type":"tool_result","content":"Scan for session issues and offer to fix them.\n\nChecks performed:\n  1. Disconnected metadata branches: detects when local and remote\n     entire/checkpoints/v1 branches share no common ancestor (caused by a\n     previous bug). Fixes by cherry-picking local checkpoints onto remote tip.\n\n  2. Operational logs: warn when .entire/logs cannot be written. Every other\n     diagnostic is delivered by writing there, and that write is silent about\n     its own failure, so an unwritable log directory looks exactly like a repo\n     where nothing ran.\n\n  When Codex hooks are installed:\n  3. Codex hook trust: warn when hooks declared in .codex/hooks.json\n     lack a trusted_hash entry in the user's Codex config (i.e. /hooks\n     review hasn't run yet on this machine, or a newer entire release\n     added a hook the user hasn't approved yet).\n\n  For each installed agent that reports hook-config drift:\n  4. Hook config: warn when the installed hooks no longer match what this\n     CLI writes (e.g. an older release wrote Claude Code tool matchers that\n     no longer fire, or a committed Pi/OpenCode extension has gone stale).\n     Fix by re-running 'entire enable --force'.\n\n  5. Retired Gemini CLI hooks: remove Entire hook entries left in\n  --session      Filter checkpoints by session ID (or prefix)\n  --short          Summary only (ID, session, timestamp, tokens, intent)\n  --full           Parsed full transcript (all prompts/responses from entire session)\n  --raw-transcript Raw transcript file (JSONL format)\n  --json           Metadata-only JSON. Lists checkpoints when no target is given;\n  --transcript     Stream stored checkpoint transcript bytes (JSONL) to stdout\n  --session-index  Pick a session within a multi-session checkpoint (0-based).\n                   --transcript or --raw-transcript.\n  --task           With --transcript, stream a subagent's stored transcript\n  --limit          Cap the number of checkpoints returned by the list view.\n  --generate    Generate an AI summary for the checkpoint. This is the only\n  --force       Regenerate even if a summary already exists (requires --generate)\n  - A preview of the next checkpoint for each session in this worktree with\n  - Subagent task records of other sessions on HEAD (not yet condensed).\n  - Logs-only resume points recovered from commits whose logs are already\n  --json             Machine-readable JSON instead of the human view.\n  --pending          Select the pending dataset described above.\n  --pending --json   The pending dataset as a JSON array.\n  -h, --help             help for list\n      --json             Output as JSON instead of the human view\n      --no-pager         Disable pager output\n      --pending          List pending work — a preview of the next checkpoint, uncondensed subagent task records, and logs-only resume points","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a19143d9-7198-4ec4-a789-c419603dcb53","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:31:05.900Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Scan for session issues and offer to fix them.\n\nChecks performed:\n  1. Disconnected metadata branches: detects when local and remote\n     entire/checkpoints/v1 branches share no common ancestor (caused by a\n     previous bug). Fixes by cherry-picking local checkpoints onto remote tip.\n\n  2. Operational logs: warn when .entire/logs cannot be written. Every other\n     diagnostic is delivered by writing there, and that write is silent about\n     its own failure, so an unwritable log directory looks exactly like a repo\n     where nothing ran.\n\n  When Codex hooks are installed:\n  3. Codex hook trust: warn when hooks declared in .codex/hooks.json\n     lack a trusted_hash entry in the user's Codex config (i.e. /hooks\n     review hasn't run yet on this machine, or a newer entire release\n     added a hook the user hasn't approved yet).\n\n  For each installed agent that reports hook-config drift:\n  4. Hook config: warn when the installed hooks no longer match what this\n     CLI writes (e.g. an older release wrote Claude Code tool matchers that\n     no longer fire, or a committed Pi/OpenCode extension has gone stale).\n     Fix by re-running 'entire enable --force'.\n\n  5. Retired Gemini CLI hooks: remove Entire hook entries left in\n  --session      Filter checkpoints by session ID (or prefix)\n  --short          Summary only (ID, session, timestamp, tokens, intent)\n  --full           Parsed full transcript (all prompts/responses from entire session)\n  --raw-transcript Raw transcript file (JSONL format)\n  --json           Metadata-only JSON. Lists checkpoints when no target is given;\n  --transcript     Stream stored checkpoint transcript bytes (JSONL) to stdout\n  --session-index  Pick a session within a multi-session checkpoint (0-based).\n                   --transcript or --raw-transcript.\n  --task           With --transcript, stream a subagent's stored transcript\n  --limit          Cap the number of checkpoints returned by the list view.\n  --generate    Generate an AI summary for the checkpoint. This is the only\n  --force       Regenerate even if a summary already exists (requires --generate)\n  - A preview of the next checkpoint for each session in this worktree with\n  - Subagent task records of other sessions on HEAD (not yet condensed).\n  - Logs-only resume points recovered from commits whose logs are already\n  --json             Machine-readable JSON instead of the human view.\n  --pending          Select the pending dataset described above.\n  --pending --json   The pending dataset as a JSON array.\n  -h, --help             help for list\n      --json             Output as JSON instead of the human view\n      --no-pager         Disable pager output\n      --pending          List pending work — a preview of the next checkpoint, uncondensed subagent task records, and logs-only resume points","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5141cbcc-4630-442a-8ad3-1126c9c2da40","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"submission","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2a5d3407-5e7f-434c-af9e-2203616f246c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
