{"parentUuid":"bd0591f9-0c03-4b2d-8307-7111fb0ed4d3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb8ch2ZPG1zBbrNsga8U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The token check showed about 60M tokens for the reprint-chaining fix and about 27M for the blind re-ruling, while the recap reported nothing since it needs server analysis this repo lacks. I'm skipping dispatch, since its cloud mode needs a published repo and its local mode would start another agent. Next I'll record these in the sessions note and commit without pushing, so I can check the new checkpoint for the name first.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":859,"cache_read_input_tokens":487558,"output_tokens":2129,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":554},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":859,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2129,"cache_read_input_tokens":487558,"cache_creation_input_tokens":859,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":859},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":4,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"d3a3433f-e3b9-4a2a-a6b5-855b8b973d1b","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgb8cgQbtDxENWrM4C6Ld","requestRef":"a72077e1-1003-4ad8-ac4f-2440a50c670a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"97bf47d0-80f9-486d-8606-dd848318b6f9","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:50:04.405Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"97bf47d0-80f9-486d-8606-dd848318b6f9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb8ch2ZPG1zBbrNsga8U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H8Hhh5p13mu7tp13cQDmcw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md\"); s = p.read_text()\ns = s.replace(\"## Before either is published\", \"\"\"## What they cost\nFrom `entire checkpoint tokens <id> --json`:\n- **The reprint chaining fix** (`01M67W8SMF2WGS6DNG76TSEAXP`): 59,983,120 tokens over 73 API calls. 48,106,921 were cache reads and 151,830 were output, plus 11,438,698 in subagents.\n- **The blind re-ruling** (`01M69PCNVRXPX8DD1EWAHB57JF`): 26,688,512 tokens over 34 calls. 24,916,651 were cache reads and 20,603 were output, plus 1,703,781 in subagents.\n\n`entire recap` shows no activity here, because its figures come from Entire's server analysis, which this repo doesn't use. `entire dispatch` was not run: its cloud mode needs a published repository, and its local mode starts another agent on this laptop.\n\n## Entire's own redaction\nEntire redacts secrets by itself, on by default, when it writes a checkpoint (docs.entire.com, \"Privacy and redaction\" and \"Security\"). Its layers:\n- an entropy check\n- Betterleaks' known secret formats\n- provider key prefixes\n- credentialed URLs and database connection strings\n- credential assignments\n- rules the user adds\n\nIt doesn't rewrite the raw agent session files, and the docs call it a safety net rather than a guarantee. This repo now has a personal rule pack in `.entire/redactors/local/` (gitignored, so it's never committed) that redacts the other local account's name from every new checkpoint.\n\n## Before either is published\"\"\", 1)\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"- **Not yet redacted:** each checkpoint holds the whole accumulated transcript (about 120 MB). Its `0/full.jsonl` includes step 1.7's process listing, which names another local account and its browsers' paths. It has to be redacted before a session is embedded or the repo goes public. That means rewriting the checkpoint refs and force-pushing them, so it's the owner's call.\"\"\", \"\"\"- **Redacted locally, not yet pushed:** each checkpoint holds the whole accumulated transcript, and its `0/full.jsonl` held step 1.7's process listing, which named another local account.\n  - 121 of the 127 refs had it, in 19 versions of the file. Each listing is now one `[redacted: another local account's process list]` line, with nothing else changed, and each `content_hash.txt` is recomputed.\n  - Tested on a clone: `entire checkpoint list`, `explain` on two rewritten and two untouched checkpoints (with their raw transcripts), and `doctor` all pass, and the name appears in no ref.\n  - The originals are kept in a verified git bundle.\n  - Force-pushing the 121 refs needs the owner's permission in this session.\"\"\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\nS=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad && git add Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md && nice -n 10 make lint >$S/lint.log 2>&1 && nice -n 10 make test >$S/test.log 2>&1 && git diff --cached > $S/staged-en.diff && uv run python $S/scan_staged.py .env $S/staged-en.diff && test \"$(grep -c -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\" $S/staged-en.diff)\" = 0 && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF' && echo committed $(git rev-parse --short HEAD); git log -1 --format='%(trailers:key=Entire-Checkpoint,valueonly)'\nEntire's trail: the sessions' real token figures and its own redaction\n\nDocs/demo/entire_sessions.md now gives the two picked sessions' token\nuse from entire checkpoint tokens, says what Entire redacts by itself,\nand records the local redaction of the other account's process list,\ntested on a clone and waiting on the owner's force-push.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF","description":"Record the Entire figures and commit without pushing"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":859,"cache_read_input_tokens":487558,"output_tokens":2129,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":554},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":859,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2129,"cache_read_input_tokens":487558,"cache_creation_input_tokens":859,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":859},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01H8Hhh5p13mu7tp13cQDmcw":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md\"); s = p.read_text()\ns = s.replace(\"## Before either is published\", \"\"\"## What they cost\nFrom `entire checkpoint tokens <id> --json`:\n- **The reprint chaining fix** (`01M67W8SMF2WGS6DNG76TSEAXP`): 59,983,120 tokens over 73 API calls. 48,106,921 were cache reads and 151,830 were output, plus 11,438,698 in subagents.\n- **The blind re-ruling** (`01M69PCNVRXPX8DD1EWAHB57JF`): 26,688,512 tokens over 34 calls. 24,916,651 were cache reads and 20,603 were output, plus 1,703,781 in subagents.\n\n`entire recap` shows no activity here, because its figures come from Entire's server analysis, which this repo doesn't use. `entire dispatch` was not run: its cloud mode needs a published repository, and its local mode starts another agent on this laptop.\n\n## Entire's own redaction\nEntire redacts secrets by itself, on by default, when it writes a checkpoint (docs.entire.com, \"Privacy and redaction\" and \"Security\"). Its layers:\n- an entropy check\n- Betterleaks' known secret formats\n- provider key prefixes\n- credentialed URLs and database connection strings\n- credential assignments\n- rules the user adds\n\nIt doesn't rewrite the raw agent session files, and the docs call it a safety net rather than a guarantee. This repo now has a personal rule pack in `.entire/redactors/local/` (gitignored, so it's never committed) that redacts the other local account's name from every new checkpoint.\n\n## Before either is published\"\"\", 1)\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"- **Not yet redacted:** each checkpoint holds the whole accumulated transcript (about 120 MB). Its `0/full.jsonl` includes step 1.7's process listing, which names another local account and its browsers' paths. It has to be redacted before a session is embedded or the repo goes public. That means rewriting the checkpoint refs and force-pushing them, so it's the owner's call.\"\"\", \"\"\"- **Redacted locally, not yet pushed:** each checkpoint holds the whole accumulated transcript, and its `0/full.jsonl` held step 1.7's process listing, which named another local account.\n  - 121 of the 127 refs had it, in 19 versions of the file. Each listing is now one `[redacted: another local account's process list]` line, with nothing else changed, and each `content_hash.txt` is recomputed.\n  - Tested on a clone: `entire checkpoint list`, `explain` on two rewritten and two untouched checkpoints (with their raw transcripts), and `doctor` all pass, and the name appears in no ref.\n  - The originals are kept in a verified git bundle.\n  - Force-pushing the 121 refs needs the owner's permission in this session.\"\"\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\nS=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad && git add Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md && nice -n 10 make lint >$S/lint.log 2>&1 && nice -n 10 make test >$S/test.log 2>&1 && git diff --cached > $S/staged-en.diff && uv run python $S/scan_staged.py .env $S/staged-en.diff && test \"$(grep -c -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\" $S/staged-en.diff)\" = 0 && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF' && echo committed $(git rev-parse --short HEAD); git log -1 --format='%(trailers:key=Entire-Checkpoint,valueonly)'\nEntire's trail: the sessions' real token figures and its own redaction\n\nDocs/demo/entire_sessions.md now gives the two picked sessions' token\nuse from entire checkpoint tokens, says what Entire redacts by itself,\nand records the local redaction of the other account's process list,\ntested on a clone and waiting on the owner's force-push.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF","description":"Record the Entire figures and commit without pushing"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d3a3433f-e3b9-4a2a-a6b5-855b8b973d1b","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgb8cgQbtDxENWrM4C6Ld","requestRef":"a72077e1-1003-4ad8-ac4f-2440a50c670a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"64092f0b-808a-4a4f-b50b-7a93faf1d1d2","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:50:16.868Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"64092f0b-808a-4a4f-b50b-7a93faf1d1d2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"98c3ee58-16ac-4e07-a418-568231f6b1de","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H8Hhh5p13mu7tp13cQDmcw","type":"tool_result","content":"checked 15 values against the staged diff; names hit: none\ncommitted c6fdab2\n01M6A2GPF65C2GKQ8EJ9YV94N0","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6fdf4452-e489-4c49-89b1-0ff1b5d5b280","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:50:41.570Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"checked 15 values against the staged diff; names hit: none\ncommitted c6fdab2\n01M6A2GPF65C2GKQ8EJ9YV94N0","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":12,"oldLines":7,"newStart":12,"newLines":29,"lines":[" | **Reprint chaining, and its fix:** chained clusters grew through near matches, so a printing now joins a story only by matching its first printing directly | `1a2f8b7` | `01M67W8SMF2WGS6DNG76TSEAXP` |"," | **A judge ruling its own case, caught:** the first rulings were the first labeller's, so fresh judges re-ruled all 69 disputes blind, and the blind ruling was taken in 28 of the 30 that differed | `537e605`, `35e8a53` | `01M69P1PXCDRMN4FCBZRDQAGV2`, `01M69PCNVRXPX8DD1EWAHB57JF` |"," ","+## What they cost","+From `entire checkpoint tokens <id> --json`:","+- **The reprint chaining fix** (`01M67W8SMF2WGS6DNG76TSEAXP`): 59,983,120 tokens over 73 API calls. 48,106,921 were cache reads and 151,830 were output, plus 11,438,698 in subagents.","+- **The blind re-ruling** (`01M69PCNVRXPX8DD1EWAHB57JF`): 26,688,512 tokens over 34 calls. 24,916,651 were cache reads and 20,603 were output, plus 1,703,781 in subagents.","+","+`entire recap` shows no activity here, because its figures come from Entire's server analysis, which this repo doesn't use. `entire dispatch` was not run: its cloud mode needs a published repository, and its local mode starts another agent on this laptop.","+","+## Entire's own redaction","+Entire redacts secrets by itself, on by default, when it writes a checkpoint (docs.entire.com, \"Privacy and redaction\" and \"Security\"). Its layers:","+- an entropy check","+- Betterleaks' known secret formats","+- provider key prefixes","+- credentialed URLs and database connection strings","+- credential assignments","+- rules the user adds","+","+It doesn't rewrite the raw agent session files, and the docs call it a safety net rather than a guarantee. This repo now has a personal rule pack in `.entire/redactors/local/` (gitignored, so it's never committed) that redacts the other local account's name from every new checkpoint.","+"," ## Before either is published"," - **The secret scan has passed:** all history, all 123 checkpoint refs. No secret, and the hostname nowhere. The 4 MongoDB URIs are test fixtures. Two `.env` values appear, but they're plain names the docs print: the Sentry project and a model name.","-- **Not yet redacted:** each checkpoint holds the whole accumulated transcript (about 120 MB). Its `0/full.jsonl` includes step 1.7's process listing, which names another local account and its browsers' paths. It has to be redacted before a session is embedded or the repo goes public. That means rewriting the checkpoint refs and force-pushing them, so it's the owner's call.","+- **Redacted locally, not yet pushed:** each checkpoint holds the whole accumulated transcript, and its `0/full.jsonl` held step 1.7's process listing, which named another local account.","+  - 121 of the 127 refs had it, in 19 versions of the file. Each listing is now one `[redacted: another local account's process list]` line, with nothing else changed, and each `content_hash.txt` is recomputed.","+  - Tested on a clone: `entire checkpoint list`, `explain` on two rewritten and two untouched checkpoints (with their raw transcripts), and `doctor` all pass, and the name appears in no ref.","+  - The originals are kept in a verified git bundle.","+  - Force-pushing the 121 refs needs the owner's permission in this session."," - **Publishing** a session as \"My Agent Session\" on DEV is the owner's step."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"d3a3433f-e3b9-4a2a-a6b5-855b8b973d1b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"submission","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"64092f0b-808a-4a4f-b50b-7a93faf1d1d2","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
