{"parentUuid":"4827c298-6627-4ca8-b2f6-9966925a4cec","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb8mkSwP1ZjrhN1jYsPJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sending the interim note after A, with the exact command for the owner:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1222,"cache_read_input_tokens":494075,"output_tokens":1969,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":635},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1222,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1969,"cache_read_input_tokens":494075,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1222,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1222},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"7d7e97cd-02cb-4122-8b6e-7dcf3fddf4c3","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgb8mjqDzgZBpybN83FBZ","requestRef":"fb4624e9-07f2-4769-b380-cf6613c82abc","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"51d0f550-1243-4516-aa86-28941df89e70","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:52:08.213Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"51d0f550-1243-4516-aa86-28941df89e70","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb8mkSwP1ZjrhN1jYsPJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C1UVvtQ7QAmwMZGzZzMex2","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e","summary":"Interim after A: redaction ready, force-push needs owner","message":"2C interim, A (Entire): the redaction is done and tested, but this session's permission check refused the force-push. The owner has to run it, or allow it here.\n- **Backup:** all 127 refs/entire refs, in a git bundle that verifies (1.88 GB), at data/entire-backup/entire-backup.bundle (gitignored), with refs-before.txt.\n- **Rewrite:** 121 refs, 19 versions of 0/full.jsonl (not 13: newer checkpoints carry the same transcript).\n  - Each process listing became one `[redacted: another local account's process list]` line. Only lines naming the account changed, and every edited line is still valid JSON.\n  - content_hash.txt is recomputed (it's sha256 of the transcript chunks joined by a newline), and all 127 hashes check. Authors, dates and messages are kept.\n- **Tested on a clone:**\n  - `entire checkpoint list` passes.\n  - `explain` passes on two rewritten checkpoints and two untouched ones, and their raw transcripts as Entire streams them don't contain the name.\n  - `doctor` passes. Its only difference is that the clone has no hooks.\n  - The name appears in no ref.\n- **New checkpoints stay clean:** a personal Entire rule pack in .entire/redactors/local/ (gitignored, never committed) redacts the name. The first new checkpoint, 01M6A2GPF65C2GKQ8EJ9YV94N0, has 0 hits and has been pushed.\n- **Not pushed:** GitHub still has the 121 originals. The redacted commits sit locally under refs/entire-redacted/*, which Entire doesn't push. No branch was touched; submission is at c6fdab2.\n- **For the owner to run in the repo,** each ref leased on its current GitHub value:\n  M=data/entire-backup/moved.txt; git push --no-verify origin $(awk '{printf \"--force-with-lease=%s:%s \", $1, $2}' $M) $(awk '{s=$1; sub(\"refs/entire/\",\"refs/entire-redacted/\",s); print s \":\" $1}' $M)\n  Afterwards: git fetch origin '+refs/entire/*:refs/entire/*', then the name scan.\n- **A5:** Entire redacts secrets itself, on by default, at checkpoint write: entropy, Betterleaks formats, key prefixes, credentialed URLs, DB strings, plus user rules. It doesn't rewrite raw session files, and the docs call it a safety net.\n- **A6:** `entire checkpoint tokens` works: the reprint-chaining fix used 59,983,120 tokens over 73 calls, the blind re-ruling 26,688,512 over 34. `recap` shows nothing without Entire's server analysis. I skipped `dispatch`: cloud mode needs a published repo, and local mode starts another agent. Recorded in Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md.\nNext: C (Sentry).","type":"message","recipient":"local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e","recipient_kind":"session","content":"2C interim, A (Entire): the redaction is done and…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1222,"cache_read_input_tokens":494075,"output_tokens":1969,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":635},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1222,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1969,"cache_read_input_tokens":494075,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1222,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1222},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01C1UVvtQ7QAmwMZGzZzMex2":{"to":"local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e","summary":"Interim after A: redaction ready, force-push needs owner","message":"2C interim, A (Entire): the redaction is done and tested, but this session's permission check refused the force-push. The owner has to run it, or allow it here.\n- **Backup:** all 127 refs/entire refs, in a git bundle that verifies (1.88 GB), at data/entire-backup/entire-backup.bundle (gitignored), with refs-before.txt.\n- **Rewrite:** 121 refs, 19 versions of 0/full.jsonl (not 13: newer checkpoints carry the same transcript).\n  - Each process listing became one `[redacted: another local account's process list]` line. Only lines naming the account changed, and every edited line is still valid JSON.\n  - content_hash.txt is recomputed (it's sha256 of the transcript chunks joined by a newline), and all 127 hashes check. Authors, dates and messages are kept.\n- **Tested on a clone:**\n  - `entire checkpoint list` passes.\n  - `explain` passes on two rewritten checkpoints and two untouched ones, and their raw transcripts as Entire streams them don't contain the name.\n  - `doctor` passes. Its only difference is that the clone has no hooks.\n  - The name appears in no ref.\n- **New checkpoints stay clean:** a personal Entire rule pack in .entire/redactors/local/ (gitignored, never committed) redacts the name. The first new checkpoint, 01M6A2GPF65C2GKQ8EJ9YV94N0, has 0 hits and has been pushed.\n- **Not pushed:** GitHub still has the 121 originals. The redacted commits sit locally under refs/entire-redacted/*, which Entire doesn't push. No branch was touched; submission is at c6fdab2.\n- **For the owner to run in the repo,** each ref leased on its current GitHub value:\n  M=data/entire-backup/moved.txt; git push --no-verify origin $(awk '{printf \"--force-with-lease=%s:%s \", $1, $2}' $M) $(awk '{s=$1; sub(\"refs/entire/\",\"refs/entire-redacted/\",s); print s \":\" $1}' $M)\n  Afterwards: git fetch origin '+refs/entire/*:refs/entire/*', then the name scan.\n- **A5:** Entire redacts secrets itself, on by default, at checkpoint write: entropy, Betterleaks formats, key prefixes, credentialed URLs, DB strings, plus user rules. It doesn't rewrite raw session files, and the docs call it a safety net.\n- **A6:** `entire checkpoint tokens` works: the reprint-chaining fix used 59,983,120 tokens over 73 calls, the blind re-ruling 26,688,512 over 34. `recap` shows nothing without Entire's server analysis. I skipped `dispatch`: cloud mode needs a published repo, and local mode starts another agent. Recorded in Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md.\nNext: C (Sentry)."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7d7e97cd-02cb-4122-8b6e-7dcf3fddf4c3","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgb8mjqDzgZBpybN83FBZ","requestRef":"fb4624e9-07f2-4769-b380-cf6613c82abc","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9a177fbf-fa62-41e7-a6a9-8cb74e95e990","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:52:18.061Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
