{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","prNumber":4,"prUrl":"https://github.com/Hotragn/Paperghosts/pull/4","prRepository":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:52:20.519Z"}
{"parentUuid":"fb32c32a-a376-4d8d-ab14-e5fe42ca8bc2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"98c3ee58-16ac-4e07-a418-568231f6b1de","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y6W6yT8mVpywZwMymBsRAj","type":"tool_result","content":"18:52\n\"\"\"make api: the read-only API over MongoDB Atlas. Phase 1 serves the walking skeleton.\"\"\"\n\nfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager\nfrom importlib.metadata import version\n\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom fastapi.responses import JSONResponse\nfrom pymongo import AsyncMongoClient\n\nfrom paperghosts.config import setting\nfrom paperghosts.observability.sentry import init_sentry\n\n\n@asynccontextmanager\nasync def lifespan(app):\n    init_sentry(\"api\")\n    client = AsyncMongoClient(\n        setting(\"MONGODB_URI\").get(), serverSelectionTimeoutMS=5_000\n    )\n    app.state.db = client[\"paperghosts\"]\n    yield\n    await client.close()\n\n\napp = FastAPI(title=\"Paper Ghosts\", lifespan=lifespan)\n\n\n@app.get(\"/api/health\")\nasync def health():\n    try:\n        await app.state.db.command(\"ping\")\n        atlas = True\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001  any failure means Atlas can't be reached from here\n        atlas = False\n    return {\"ok\": True, \"atlas\": atlas, \"version\": version(\"paperghosts\")}\n\n\n@app.get(\"/api/skeleton/{article_id}\")\nasync def skeleton(article_id: str):\n    article = await app.state.db.skeleton.find_one({\"_id\": article_id})\n    if article is None:\n        error = {\"code\": \"not_found\", \"message\": \"No skeleton article has that id.\"}\n        return JSONResponse({\"error\": error}, status_code=404)\n    return article\n\"\"\"Sentry setup and model-call spans.\"\"\"\n\"\"\"Sentry for the API and the pipeline: off without a DSN, and nothing personal or secret\nleaves this machine.\"\"\"\n\nimport re\n\nimport sentry_sdk\n\nfrom paperghosts.config import setting\n\n# a URL's query string, after scheme://host/path or a bare /path\nQUERY = re.compile(r\"((?:\\w+:/)?/[^\\s?#]*)\\?[^\\s#]*\")\nDROPPED_KEYS = {\n    \"query_string\",\n    \"http.query\",\n    \"lat\",\n    \"lon\",\n    \"lng\",\n    \"latitude\",\n    \"longitude\",\n    \"coordinates\",\n}\n\n\ndef scrub(value):\n    \"\"\"Strips query strings and coordinate fields anywhere in an event.\"\"\"\n    if isinstance(value, str):\n        return QUERY.sub(r\"\\1\", value)\n    if isinstance(value, dict):\n        return {\n            k: scrub(v) for k, v in value.items() if str(k).lower() not in DROPPED_KEYS\n        }\n    if isinstance(value, list):\n        return [scrub(v) for v in value]\n    return value\n\n\ndef init_sentry(component: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Starts Sentry for \"api\" or \"pipeline\". Without SENTRY_DSN it does nothing.\"\"\"\n    dsn = setting(\"SENTRY_DSN\")\n    if not dsn:\n        return False\n    sentry_sdk.init(\n        dsn=dsn.get(),\n        environment=component,  # the API and the pipeline share one project\n        server_name=component,  # the default is the host name, which can name its owner\n        traces_sample_rate=1.0,\n        # replaces the deprecated send_default_pii=False; fields left out default to on\n        data_collection={\n            \"user_info\": False,\n            \"cookies\": {\"mode\": \"off\"},\n            \"http_headers\": {\"request\": {\"mode\": \"off\"}},\n            \"http_bodies\": [],\n            \"url_query_params\": {\"mode\": \"off\"},\n            \"gen_ai\": {\"inputs\": False, \"outputs\": False},\n            \"database_query_data\": False,  # Mongo queries can hold near-me coordinates\n            \"stack_frame_variables\": False,  # locals can hold keys, URIs and coordinates\n        },\n        before_send=lambda event, hint: scrub(event),\n        before_send_transaction=lambda event, hint: scrub(event),\npyproject.toml:13:    \"sentry-sdk>=2.73.0\",","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3c96bfc9-fae0-4585-88f6-911298a83193","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:52:20.549Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"18:52\n\"\"\"make api: the read-only API over MongoDB Atlas. Phase 1 serves the walking skeleton.\"\"\"\n\nfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager\nfrom importlib.metadata import version\n\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom fastapi.responses import JSONResponse\nfrom pymongo import AsyncMongoClient\n\nfrom paperghosts.config import setting\nfrom paperghosts.observability.sentry import init_sentry\n\n\n@asynccontextmanager\nasync def lifespan(app):\n    init_sentry(\"api\")\n    client = AsyncMongoClient(\n        setting(\"MONGODB_URI\").get(), serverSelectionTimeoutMS=5_000\n    )\n    app.state.db = client[\"paperghosts\"]\n    yield\n    await client.close()\n\n\napp = FastAPI(title=\"Paper Ghosts\", lifespan=lifespan)\n\n\n@app.get(\"/api/health\")\nasync def health():\n    try:\n        await app.state.db.command(\"ping\")\n        atlas = True\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001  any failure means Atlas can't be reached from here\n        atlas = False\n    return {\"ok\": True, \"atlas\": atlas, \"version\": version(\"paperghosts\")}\n\n\n@app.get(\"/api/skeleton/{article_id}\")\nasync def skeleton(article_id: str):\n    article = await app.state.db.skeleton.find_one({\"_id\": article_id})\n    if article is None:\n        error = {\"code\": \"not_found\", \"message\": \"No skeleton article has that id.\"}\n        return JSONResponse({\"error\": error}, status_code=404)\n    return article\n\"\"\"Sentry setup and model-call spans.\"\"\"\n\"\"\"Sentry for the API and the pipeline: off without a DSN, and nothing personal or secret\nleaves this machine.\"\"\"\n\nimport re\n\nimport sentry_sdk\n\nfrom paperghosts.config import setting\n\n# a URL's query string, after scheme://host/path or a bare /path\nQUERY = re.compile(r\"((?:\\w+:/)?/[^\\s?#]*)\\?[^\\s#]*\")\nDROPPED_KEYS = {\n    \"query_string\",\n    \"http.query\",\n    \"lat\",\n    \"lon\",\n    \"lng\",\n    \"latitude\",\n    \"longitude\",\n    \"coordinates\",\n}\n\n\ndef scrub(value):\n    \"\"\"Strips query strings and coordinate fields anywhere in an event.\"\"\"\n    if isinstance(value, str):\n        return QUERY.sub(r\"\\1\", value)\n    if isinstance(value, dict):\n        return {\n            k: scrub(v) for k, v in value.items() if str(k).lower() not in DROPPED_KEYS\n        }\n    if isinstance(value, list):\n        return [scrub(v) for v in value]\n    return value\n\n\ndef init_sentry(component: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Starts Sentry for \"api\" or \"pipeline\". Without SENTRY_DSN it does nothing.\"\"\"\n    dsn = setting(\"SENTRY_DSN\")\n    if not dsn:\n        return False\n    sentry_sdk.init(\n        dsn=dsn.get(),\n        environment=component,  # the API and the pipeline share one project\n        server_name=component,  # the default is the host name, which can name its owner\n        traces_sample_rate=1.0,\n        # replaces the deprecated send_default_pii=False; fields left out default to on\n        data_collection={\n            \"user_info\": False,\n            \"cookies\": {\"mode\": \"off\"},\n            \"http_headers\": {\"request\": {\"mode\": \"off\"}},\n            \"http_bodies\": [],\n            \"url_query_params\": {\"mode\": \"off\"},\n            \"gen_ai\": {\"inputs\": False, \"outputs\": False},\n            \"database_query_data\": False,  # Mongo queries can hold near-me coordinates\n            \"stack_frame_variables\": False,  # locals can hold keys, URIs and coordinates\n        },\n        before_send=lambda event, hint: scrub(event),\n        before_send_transaction=lambda event, hint: scrub(event),\npyproject.toml:13:    \"sentry-sdk>=2.73.0\",","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"7d7e97cd-02cb-4122-8b6e-7dcf3fddf4c3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"submission","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fb32c32a-a376-4d8d-ab14-e5fe42ca8bc2","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","hash":"3585e658785a049792236191255c9a34b5a27a8dada44ad1df5ef95f7d5417c2","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Sending the interim note after A, with the exact command for the owner:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C1UVvtQ7QAmwMZGzZzMex2","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e","summary":"Interim after A: redaction ready, force-push needs owner","message":"2C interim, A (Entire): the redaction is done and tested, but this session's permission check refused the force-push. The owner has to run it, or allow it here.\n- **Backup:** all 127 refs/entire refs, in a git bundle that verifies (1.88 GB), at data/entire-backup/entire-backup.bundle (gitignored), with refs-before.txt.\n- **Rewrite:** 121 refs, 19 versions of 0/full.jsonl (not 13: newer checkpoints carry the same transcript).\n  - Each process listing became one `[redacted: another local account's process list]` line. Only lines naming the account changed, and every edited line is still valid JSON.\n  - content_hash.txt is recomputed (it's sha256 of the transcript chunks joined by a newline), and all 127 hashes check. Authors, dates and messages are kept.\n- **Tested on a clone:**\n  - `entire checkpoint list` passes.\n  - `explain` passes on two rewritten checkpoints and two untouched ones, and their raw transcripts as Entire streams them don't contain the name.\n  - `doctor` passes. Its only difference is that the clone has no hooks.\n  - The name appears in no ref.\n- **New checkpoints stay clean:** a personal Entire rule pack in .entire/redactors/local/ (gitignored, never committed) redacts the name. The first new checkpoint, 01M6A2GPF65C2GKQ8EJ9YV94N0, has 0 hits and has been pushed.\n- **Not pushed:** GitHub still has the 121 originals. The redacted commits sit locally under refs/entire-redacted/*, which Entire doesn't push. No branch was touched; submission is at c6fdab2.\n- **For the owner to run in the repo,** each ref leased on its current GitHub value:\n  M=data/entire-backup/moved.txt; git push --no-verify origin $(awk '{printf \"--force-with-lease=%s:%s \", $1, $2}' $M) $(awk '{s=$1; sub(\"refs/entire/\",\"refs/entire-redacted/\",s); print s \":\" $1}' $M)\n  Afterwards: git fetch origin '+refs/entire/*:refs/entire/*', then the name scan.\n- **A5:** Entire redacts secrets itself, on by default, at checkpoint write: entropy, Betterleaks formats, key prefixes, credentialed URLs, DB strings, plus user rules. It doesn't rewrite raw session files, and the docs call it a safety net.\n- **A6:** `entire checkpoint tokens` works: the reprint-chaining fix used 59,983,120 tokens over 73 calls, the blind re-ruling 26,688,512 over 34. `recap` shows nothing without Entire's server analysis. I skipped `dispatch`: cloud mode needs a published repo, and local mode starts another agent. Recorded in Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md.\nNext: C (Sentry)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y6W6yT8mVpywZwMymBsRAj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"date +%H:%M; cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && cat api/main.py | head -80; sed -n 1,60p paperghosts/observability/*.py | head -80; grep -n \"sentry\" pyproject.toml web/package.json","description":"Read the API and the existing Sentry setup"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
