{"parentUuid":"9aa237e3-a97b-4de0-834d-acacbfa345fb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb97m8BE73HSLUtzhFUx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BHumPeLVdrLkoLg156gR6A","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && S=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad && u=$(ls /Users | grep -v -E \"^(Shared|hotragn|Guest|\\..*)$\") && git add api/main.py tests/test_api.py scripts/sentry_latency.py eval/results/sentry_latency.json && nice -n 10 make lint >$S/lint.log 2>&1 && nice -n 10 make test >$S/test.log 2>&1 && git diff --cached > $S/staged-f.diff && uv run python $S/scan_staged.py .env $S/staged-f.diff && test \"$(grep -c -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\" $S/staged-f.diff)\" = 0 && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF' && cp=$(git log -1 --format='%(trailers:key=Entire-Checkpoint,valueonly)') && r=refs/entire/checkpoints/${cp: -2}/$cp && n=$(git grep -c -F \"$u\" $r 2>/dev/null | awk -F: '{s+=$NF} END {print s+0}') && echo \"checkpoint $cp name hits $n\" && test \"$n\" = 0 && git push -q origin submission 2>&1 | grep -v -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\"; tail -1 $S/test.log; git ls-remote origin submission; git rev-parse HEAD\nGhosts like this one reads each report from Atlas once\n\nSentry's spans for release c0a248f showed every ghosts-like-this-one\nrequest paying for two Atlas round trips: a find for the report's\nheadline and text (p50 41 ms, p95 48) before the moreLikeThis (p50 66\nms, p95 76), against 75 ms for a whole fuzzy search. The report never\nchanges within a release, so the API now keeps what it read, bounded\nat 1,024, and a repeat request makes one round trip.\nscripts/sentry_latency.py pulls p50 and p95 per query kind and release\nfrom Sentry into eval/results/sentry_latency.json.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com