{"parentUuid":"9345048b-9f2b-4eab-bd09-d887a9d90027","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbEFRsbe6cSf4HQnHPAs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Sentry's numbers agree with the earlier results: `$geoNear` at 525 ms median and fuzzy at 561 ms, both cold, and `moreLikeThis` at 68 ms warm. I'm now recording this as decision 40 in DECISIONS.md and adding the Sentry, places and vector-search status to the numbers sheet.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":791,"cache_read_input_tokens":578564,"output_tokens":1755,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":223},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":791,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1755,"cache_read_input_tokens":578564,"cache_creation_input_tokens":791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":791},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":3,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"7638d390-fd90-42d2-8981-f3ab7a5eb9aa","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgbEFRSZBjppVFox8buH7","requestRef":"6a904f65-6026-4887-9190-d1ccfb0c2fc5","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"04e430ee-e634-49ca-a629-867a6b887ceb","timestamp":"2026-11-01T00:03:53.513Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"04e430ee-e634-49ca-a629-867a6b887ceb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbEFRsbe6cSf4HQnHPAs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EY5Wq6Vxep8nQpJaxXnAH7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && cat >> Docs/DECISIONS.md <<'EOF'\n\n**40. Sentry traces each Atlas query, and what it showed was fixed: \"ghosts like this one\" now reads its report from Atlas once. Every Atlas query runs in a span of op `db.atlas.query` that carries its kind and latency, never the words searched for. `scripts/sentry_latency.py` pulls p50 and p95 per kind and release from Sentry into `eval/results/sentry_latency.json`.**\n\n- **The finding (release c0a248f, 40 requests of each kind):**\n  - Each \"ghosts like this one\" request made two Atlas round trips: a `find` for the report's headline and text (p50 41 ms, p95 48), then the `moreLikeThis` (p50 66, p95 76).\n  - A whole fuzzy search was 75 ms.\n- **The fix (release 19a6a4b):** a report doesn't change within a release, so the API keeps what it read, bounded at 1,024 reports.\n  - Over two passes of the same 40 reports, Sentry counts 80 `moreLikeThis` queries but only 40 `find`s. A repeat request is one round trip: p50 63 ms of Atlas time, against 107.\n  - Measured at the client, a repeat request's p50 went from 110 ms to 61, and its p95 from 123 to 68.\n- **The scripts (release b560aa2):** a script's first query pays to open its connection. A fuzzy search or a `$geoNear` takes p50 525–561 ms cold. A `moreLikeThis` that follows the script's own `find` takes 68 ms. The API's one long-lived client avoids that cost, and its searches run at p50 67–75 ms.\n- **The web app** (paperghosts-web) sends browser tracing and errors only when built with a DSN, and collects nothing about the reader.\n  - Its release is the commit, with hidden source maps uploaded, then deleted from the build.\n  - So far its page loads come from scripted loads in the browser pane and headless Chrome. LCP, CLS and INP need real visits that hide or use the page.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"scripts/article_numbers.py\"); s = p.read_text()\nold = '''        row(\n            \"decision 39: the disclosure\",'''\nassert old in s\ns = s.replace(old, '''        *sentry(),\n        row(\"Atlas: the papers' towns geocoded and loaded\", at(\"eval/results/atlas_places.json\", \"\", \"printed_in_towns\", \"geocoded\", \"reports_covered\", \"storage_kb\")),\n        {\n            \"name\": \"Atlas Vector Search: not built\",\n            \"value\": \"the Hugging Face token lacks the Inference Providers permission (HTTP 403), so no open-model embeddings; ghosts like this one uses Atlas Search's moreLikeThis\",\n            \"source\": \"scripts/load_demo_places.py session log, 2026-10-31 (not committed)\",\n            \"note\": \"hard-coded: a refusal leaves no results file\",\n        },\n        row(\n            \"decision 39: the disclosure\",''', 1)\ns = s.replace('''def submission() -> list:''', '''def sentry() -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sentry's p50 and p95 per Atlas query kind, for each release pulled (decision 40).\"\"\"\n    rel = \"eval/results/sentry_latency.json\"\n    found = json.loads((ROOT / rel).read_text())\n    return [\n        row(\n            f\"Sentry: Atlas query latency (ms), release {key[:7]}\",\n            ({q[\"query\"]: [q[\"p50_ms\"], q[\"p95_ms\"], q[\"count\"]] for q in v[\"spans\"]}, f\"{rel}: {key}.spans, as [p50, p95, count]\"),\n        )\n        for key, v in found.items()\n    ]\n\n\ndef submission() -> list:''', 1)\np.write_text(s)\nPY\nuv run ruff format scripts/article_numbers.py >/dev/null && uv run ruff check scripts/article_numbers.py && nice uv run python scripts/article_numbers.py 2>&1 | grep -E \"Sentry|papers' towns|Vector\" | cut -c1-260","description":"Write decision 40 and add Sentry and Atlas rows to the sheet"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":791,"cache_read_input_tokens":578564,"output_tokens":1755,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":223},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":791,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1755,"cache_read_input_tokens":578564,"cache_creation_input_tokens":791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":791},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01EY5Wq6Vxep8nQpJaxXnAH7":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && cat >> Docs/DECISIONS.md <<'EOF'\n\n**40. Sentry traces each Atlas query, and what it showed was fixed: \"ghosts like this one\" now reads its report from Atlas once. Every Atlas query runs in a span of op `db.atlas.query` that carries its kind and latency, never the words searched for. `scripts/sentry_latency.py` pulls p50 and p95 per kind and release from Sentry into `eval/results/sentry_latency.json`.**\n\n- **The finding (release c0a248f, 40 requests of each kind):**\n  - Each \"ghosts like this one\" request made two Atlas round trips: a `find` for the report's headline and text (p50 41 ms, p95 48), then the `moreLikeThis` (p50 66, p95 76).\n  - A whole fuzzy search was 75 ms.\n- **The fix (release 19a6a4b):** a report doesn't change within a release, so the API keeps what it read, bounded at 1,024 reports.\n  - Over two passes of the same 40 reports, Sentry counts 80 `moreLikeThis` queries but only 40 `find`s. A repeat request is one round trip: p50 63 ms of Atlas time, against 107.\n  - Measured at the client, 