{"parentUuid":"475d4cfd-a4ee-46ba-856e-076d91ef59ad","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbEHsWGJSmbkjwRnAXib","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the README: Sentry, \"near this town\", the vector-search status and the new mark:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":867,"cache_read_input_tokens":581911,"output_tokens":1923,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":191},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":867,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1923,"cache_read_input_tokens":581911,"cache_creation_input_tokens":867,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":867},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e415c7c0-1271-4828-8f62-927b69b107ae","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgbEHs6TTHwBhtNQK9FfC","requestRef":"98907297-1349-4d1f-a990-f7229d68f706","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"22007479-f1ed-45ba-b465-f2d72df63e51","timestamp":"2026-11-01T00:04:25.748Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"22007479-f1ed-45ba-b465-f2d72df63e51","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbEHsWGJSmbkjwRnAXib","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018269REhRZzWKKctzTy4pFP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"README.md\"); s = p.read_text()\nold = \"The keys come from `MONGODB_URI` in `.env`.\"\nassert old in s\ns = s.replace(old, \"\"\"```bash\nuv run python scripts/load_demo_places.py load                       # the papers' 46 towns, geocoded from GeoNames\nuv run python scripts/load_demo_places.py near Philadelphia Pennsylvania 250   # $geoNear: papers printed nearby\n```\n\nThe keys come from `MONGODB_URI` in `.env`.\n- \"Near this town\" is about where the papers were printed, never where the stories happened.\n- Atlas Vector Search isn't built yet. The index is there for 384-dimension vectors, but embedding the reports with an open model on Hugging Face needs a token with the Inference Providers permission. Until then, \"ghosts like this one\" is Atlas Search's moreLikeThis.\n\n### Sentry\n- **API:** `/api/search` and `/api/like/{id}` run each Atlas query in a span of op `db.atlas.query`, with its kind and latency, never the words searched for. The scripts' queries run the same way.\n- **Releases** are commits.\n- **Figures:** `uv run python scripts/sentry_latency.py [SINCE [RELEASE]]` pulls p50 and p95 per query kind with `SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN`. One real finding is fixed: decision 40.\n- **The web app** sends tracing and errors only when built with `VITE_SENTRY_DSN`.\n  - With `SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN` at build time, it uploads hidden source maps for the commit and deletes them from `dist`.\n  - On Render, set both in the service's environment.\"\"\", 1)\np.write_text(s)\nr = Path(\"render.yaml\"); t = r.read_text()\nt = t.replace(\"    staticPublishPath: web/dist\\n\", \"\"\"    staticPublishPath: web/dist\n    # set in Render's dashboard, never committed: the web DSN turns Sentry on, the token uploads\n    # source maps for the commit Render builds\n    envVars:\n      - key: VITE_SENTRY_DSN\n        sync: false\n      - key: SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN\n        sync: false\n\"\"\", 1)\nr.write_text(t)\nPY\nS=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad && u=$(ls /Users | grep -v -E \"^(Shared|hotragn|Guest|\\..*)$\") && git add README.md render.yaml Docs/DECISIONS.md scripts/article_numbers.py eval/results/numbers.json web/public/numbers.json eval/results/sentry_latency.json && nice -n 10 make lint >$S/lint.log 2>&1 && nice -n 10 make test >$S/test.log 2>&1 && git diff --cached > $S/staged-d40.diff && uv run python $S/scan_staged.py .env $S/staged-d40.diff && test \"$(grep -c -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\" $S/staged-d40.diff)\" = 0 && git commit -q -m \"Decision 40: what Sentry showed and the fix; the sheet and README catch up\n\nDecision 40 records Sentry's tracing of every Atlas query and the one\nreal finding it led to: ghosts-like-this-one paid a find before each\nmoreLikeThis, now read once per report (p50 107 ms of Atlas time to 63).\nThe numbers sheet adds Sentry's p50 and p95 per query kind and release,\nthe scripted page loads, the papers' towns in Atlas, and why Vector\nSearch isn't built yet. The README covers Atlas near-this-town and\nSentry, and render.yaml names the two keys Render must hold.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && cp=$(git log -1 --format='%(trailers:key=Entire-Checkpoint,valueonly)') && r=refs/entire/checkpoints/${cp: -2}/$cp && n=$(git grep -c -F \"$u\" $r 2>/dev/null | awk -F: '{s+=$NF} END {print s+0}') && echo \"checkpoint name hits $n\" && test \"$n\" = 0 && git push -q origin submission 2>&1 | grep -v -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\"; tail -1 $S/test.log; git ls-remote origin submission; git rev-parse HEAD","description":"Gate, commit and push decision 40, numbers and README"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":867,"cache_read_input_tokens":581911,"output_tokens":1923,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":191},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":867,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1923,"cache_read_input_tokens":581911,"cache_creation_input_tokens":867,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":867},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018269REhRZzWKKctzTy4pFP":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"README.md\"); s = p.read_text()\nold = \"The keys come from `MONGODB_URI` in `.env`.\"\nassert old in s\ns = s.replace(old, \"\"\"```bash\nuv run python scripts/load_demo_places.py load                       # the papers' 46 towns, geocoded from GeoNames\nuv run python scripts/load_demo_places.py near Philadelphia Pennsylvania 250   # $geoNear: papers printed nearby\n```\n\nThe keys come from `MONGODB_URI` in `.env`.\n- \"Near this town\" is about where the papers were printed, never where the stories happened.\n- Atlas Vector Search isn't built yet. The index is there for 384-dimension vectors, but embedding the reports with an open model on Hugging Face needs a token with the Inference Providers permission. Until then, \"ghosts like this one\" is Atlas Search's moreLikeThis.\n\n### Sentry\n- **API:** `/api/search` and `/api/like/{id}` run each Atlas query in a span of op `db.atlas.query`, with its kind and latency, never the words searched for. The scripts' queries run the same way.\n- **Releases** are commits.\n- **Figures:** `uv run python scripts/sentry_latency.py [SINCE [RELEASE]]` pulls p50 and p95 per query kind with `SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN`. One real finding is fixed: decision 40.\n- **The web app** sends tracing and errors only when built with `VITE_SENTRY_DSN`.\n  - With `SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN` at build time, it uploads hidden source maps for the commit and deletes them from `dist`.\n  - On Render, set both in the service's environment.\"\"\", 1)\np.write_text(s)\nr = Path(\"render.yaml\"); t = r.read_text()\nt = t.replace(\"    staticPublishPath: web/dist\\n\", \"\"\"    staticPublishPath: web/dist\n    # set in Render's dashboard, never committed: the web DSN turns Sentry on, the token uploads\n    # source maps for the commit Render builds\n    envVars:\n      - key: VITE_SENTRY_DSN\n        sync: false\n      - key: SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN\n        sync: false\n\"\"\", 1)\nr.write_text(t)\nPY\nS=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad && u=$(ls /Users | grep -v -E \"^(Shared|hotragn|Guest|\\..*)$\") && git add README.md render.yaml Docs/DECISIONS.md scripts/article_numbers.py eval/results/numbers.json web/public/numbers.json eval/results/sentry_latency.json && nice -n 10 make lint >$S/lint.log 2>&1 && nice -n 10 make test >$S/test.log 2>&1 && git diff --cached > $S/staged-d40.diff && uv run python $S/scan_staged.py .env $S/staged-d40.diff && test \"$(grep -c -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\" $S/staged-d40.diff)\" = 0 && git commit -q -m \"Decision 40: what Sentry showed and the fix; the sheet and README catch up\n\nDecision 40 records Sentry's tracing of every Atlas query and the one\nreal finding it led to: ghosts-like-this-one paid a find before each\nmoreLikeThis, now read once per report (p50 107 ms of Atlas time to 63).\nThe numbers sheet adds Sentry's p50 and p95 per query kind and release,\nthe scripted page loads, the papers' towns in Atlas, and why Vector\nSearch isn't built yet. The README covers Atlas near-this-town and\nSentry, and render.yaml names the two keys Render must hold.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && cp=$(git log -1 --format='%(trailers:key=Entire-Checkpoint,valueonly)') && r=refs/entire/checkpoints/${cp: -2}/$cp && n=$(git grep -c -F \"$u\" $r 2>/dev/null | awk -F: '{s+=$NF} END {print s+0}') && echo \"checkpoint name hits $n\" && test \"$n\" = 0 && git push -q origin submission 2>&1 | grep -v -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\"; tail -1 $S/test.log; git ls-remote origin submission; git rev-parse HEAD","description":"Gate, commit and push decision 40, numbers and README"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"e415c7c0-1271-4828-8f62-927b69b107ae","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgbEHs6TTHwBhtNQK9FfC","requestRef":"98907297-1349-4d1f-a990-f7229d68f706","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"91b3011d-9ea9-4b04-81d1-c8360944c7c9","timestamp":"2026-11-01T00:04:40.408Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
