{"parentUuid":"dd9d8092-fb65-4e47-9b19-0c66ee28204f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbENHJqmcPVeM8eNRkmN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GHa8MBaQ3uK7nS63BJHegr","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e","summary":"Final report: blocked only on the owner's force-push","message":"SUBMISSION: BLOCKED — only the Entire force-push remains, and it needs the owner to run it or allow it in this session. Everything else is pushed at a9eb97b on `submission` (ls-remote matches; 404 tests, lint and build pass; no Ollama or mlx-lm).\n- **Entire:** the redaction is ready, and all 121 leases still match GitHub. The command is in my interim note (data/entire-backup/moved.txt).\n  - Every new checkpoint since has had 0 hits for the name; the gitignored local rule pack covers it.\n  - The 121 originals on GitHub still hold the process list.\n- **Sentry:**\n  - API: `/api/search` and `/api/like/{id}`, with one `db.atlas.query` span per query (kind and latency, never the words). The scripts' fuzzy, moreLikeThis and $geoNear run as transactions too.\n  - Releases are commit SHAs. The web app (paperghosts-web) has browser tracing and errors, and its source maps are uploaded, then deleted from dist.\n  - The real finding, decision 40: each ghosts-like request paid a `find` (p50 41 ms) before its moreLikeThis (66). Now each report is read once, and a repeat request costs 63 ms of Atlas time against 107. At the client, p50 went from 110 to 61 ms and p95 from 123 to 68.\n  - Scripts' first queries pay for the connection: about 525–561 ms cold, against the API's 67–75.\n  - Web: 14 scripted page loads (pageload p50 102 ms) and the test error arrived. LCP, CLS and INP need real visits. All of it is in eval/results/sentry_latency.json and the numbers sheet.\n- **Near this town:** all 46 printed-in towns are geocoded from GeoNames into paperghosts.places (2dsphere), labelled as the papers' towns. $geoNear runs in about 0.5 s; outputs are in Docs/demo/atlas_near.txt.\n- **Vector Search not built:** HF_TOKEN lacks the \"Inference Providers\" permission (HTTP 403). The owner can enable it; the reports_vector index is ready for 384-dimension vectors. Until then, moreLikeThis stands in, as stated in the README and the numbers sheet.\n- **Logo:** a ragged torn hem, slit eyes, a jagged mouth and a dark shadow; it reads at 16 px. Before and after at 16, 64 and 512 px are in Docs/demo/logo-before-after.jpg. The favicons, social card and 16 screenshots are redrawn, and the phone nav is on one row.\n- **Not done:** a dedicated \"How it was built\" page. Entire is a paragraph on How we know plus Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md.\n- **Owner actions:**\n  1. Run or allow the Entire force-push.\n  2. Optionally give HF_TOKEN Inference Providers permission.\n  3. Make the repo public.\n  4. Deploy render.yaml, setting VITE_SENTRY_DSN and SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN in Render, and the absolute og:image.\n  5. Publish.","type":"message","recipient":"local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e","recipient_kind":"session","content":"SUBMISSION: BLOCKED — only the Entire force-push …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":813,"cache_read_input_tokens":584868,"output_tokens":1567,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":813,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1567,"cache_read_input_tokens":584868,"cache_creation_input_tokens":813,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":813},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01GHa8MBaQ3uK7nS63BJHegr":{"to":"local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e","summary":"Final report: blocked only on the owner's force-push","message":"SUBMISSION: BLOCKED — only the Entire force-push remains, and it needs the owner to run it or allow it in this session. Everything else is pushed at a9eb97b on `submission` (ls-remote matches; 404 tests, lint and build pass; no Ollama or mlx-lm).\n- **Entire:** the redaction is ready, and all 121 leases still match GitHub. The command is in my interim note (data/entire-backup/moved.txt).\n  - Every new checkpoint since has had 0 hits for the name; the gitignored local rule pack covers it.\n  - The 121 originals on GitHub still hold the process list.\n- **Sentry:**\n  - API: `/api/search` and `/api/like/{id}`, with one `db.atlas.query` span per query (kind and latency, never the words). The scripts' fuzzy, moreLikeThis and $geoNear run as transactions too.\n  - Releases are commit SHAs. The web app (paperghosts-web) has browser tracing and errors, and its source maps are uploaded, then deleted from dist.\n  - The real finding, decision 40: each ghosts-like request paid a `find` (p50 41 ms) before its moreLikeThis (66). Now each report is read once, and a repeat request costs 63 ms of Atlas time against 107. At the client, p50 went from 110 to 61 ms and p95 from 123 to 68.\n  - Scripts' first queries pay for the connection: about 525–561 ms cold, against the API's 67–75.\n  - Web: 14 scripted page loads (pageload p50 102 ms) and the test error arrived. LCP, CLS and INP need real visits. All of it is in eval/results/sentry_latency.json and the numbers sheet.\n- **Near this town:** all 46 printed-in towns are geocoded from GeoNames into paperghosts.places (2dsphere), labelled as the papers' towns. $geoNear runs in about 0.5 s; outputs are in Docs/demo/atlas_near.txt.\n- **Vector Search not built:** HF_TOKEN lacks the \"Inference Providers\" permission (HTTP 403). The owner can enable it; the reports_vector index is ready for 384-dimension vectors. Until then, moreLikeThis stands in, as stated in the README and the numbers sheet.\n- **Logo:** a ragged torn hem, slit eyes, a jagged mouth and a dark shadow; it reads at 16 px. Before and after at 16, 64 and 512 px are in Docs/demo/logo-before-after.jpg. The favicons, social card and 16 screenshots are redrawn, and the phone nav is on one row.\n- **Not done:** a dedicated \"How it was built\" page. Entire is a paragraph on How we know plus Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md.\n- **Owner actions:**\n  1. Run or allow the Entire force-push.\n  2. Optionally give HF_TOKEN Inference Providers permission.\n  3. Make the repo public.\n  4. Deploy render.yaml, setting VITE_SENTRY_DSN and SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN in Render, and the absolute og:image.\n  5. Publish."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"e3c8f999-027a-457f-9116-d453048488cd","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgbENGuYBwu1UU7FP7Gee","requestRef":"6a6f184e-4f8e-409f-902e-f6489dd78fa3","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"Claude Browser","attributionMcpTool":"preview_stop","type":"assistant","uuid":"096a4a9b-2a8a-4df8-a642-b1ac9e73c2ca","timestamp":"2026-11-01T00:05:33.826Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
