{"parentUuid":"6862d7df-12bc-47ee-a267-7ae49ca94cc0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbEPS8CuxvfmiiDXoiv6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"SUBMISSION: BLOCKED — the redacted Entire history is ready, but force-pushing it needs your permission. This session refused the force-push because your approval reached me through another session. Everything else is on GitHub at a9eb97b on `submission`, confirmed with ls-remote, with 404 tests, lint and the build passing. No Ollama or local model ran.\n\n**Entire:**\n- **Backup:** all 127 checkpoint refs are in a git bundle that verifies, at `data/entire-backup/` (gitignored).\n- **Redaction:** in 121 refs (19 versions of the transcript file), each listing of the other account's processes is now one `[redacted: another local account's process list]` line. Nothing else changed, and Entire's content hashes were recomputed and all check out.\n- **Tested on a local clone:** `entire checkpoint list`, `explain` on rewritten and untouched checkpoints, and `doctor` all pass, and the name appears nowhere.\n- **Not yet on GitHub:** the redacted commits are parked locally under `refs/entire-redacted/*`, which Entire doesn't push, and all 121 leases still match. The 121 originals on GitHub still hold the process list until the force-push.\n- **New checkpoints are clean:** a private, gitignored Entire rule now redacts the name. I checked every new checkpoint before each push: 0 hits.\n- **Entire's own redaction:** it strips keys, tokens, credentialed URLs and database strings on its own, on by default, and the docs call it a safety net.\n- **Token figures:** the reprint-chaining fix session used 59,983,120 tokens; the blind re-ruling 26,688,512.\n\n**Sentry:**\n- **API:** the search and \"ghosts like\" routes, and the scripts' queries, run each Atlas query in its own span with its kind and latency, never the search words. Releases are commit SHAs.\n- **Web app:** it sends tracing and errors only when built with a key, and source maps are uploaded, then removed from the build. The 14 page loads Sentry has came from my scripted test loads, not visitors. LCP, CLS and INP will need real visits.\n- **One real finding, fixed (decision 40):** each \"ghosts like this one\" request first re-read its report (41 ms median) before searching (66 ms). The API now reads each report once, so a repeat request takes 63 ms of Atlas time instead of 107. At the client, the median went from 110 to 61 ms and p95 from 123 to 68.\n\n**Atlas:**\n- **Near this town:** all 46 towns where the papers were printed are geocoded from the GeoNames files already in the repo. A `$geoNear` query finds them in about half a second, labelled as the papers' towns, never the stories'.\n- **Vector search isn't built:** your Hugging Face token lacks the \"Inference Providers\" permission, so the hosted embedding call returned 403. The index is ready for those vectors. Until then, \"ghosts like this one\" uses Atlas Search's own similarity matching.\n\n**The logo** has a torn, ragged hem, slit eyes, a jagged mouth and a dark shadow, and it still reads at 16 px. `Docs/demo/logo-before-after.jpg` shows old and new at 16, 64 and 512 px. The favicons, social card and screenshots are redrawn, and the phone nav fits on one row.\n\n**Not done:** a separate \"How it was built\" page. Entire is covered by a paragraph on the \"How we know\" page and by `Docs/demo/entire_sessions.md`.\n\n**If you'd rather run the push yourself,** run this from the repo. Each ref is leased on its current GitHub value, so a ref that moved since is refused:\n\n```bash\nM=data/entire-backup/moved.txt; git push --no-verify origin $(awk '{printf \"--force-with-lease=%s:%s \", $1, $2}' $M) $(awk '{s=$1; sub(\"refs/entire/\",\"refs/entire-redacted/\",s); print s \":\" $1}' $M)\n```\n\n**Your other steps:**\n1. Optionally, give the Hugging Face token the Inference Providers permission, which unlocks vector search.\n2. Make the repo public.\n3. Deploy `render.yaml`, adding `VITE_SENTRY_DSN` and `SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN` in Render's settings, and set the full `og:image` URL.\n4. Publish."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1876,"cache_read_input_tokens":585681,"output_tokens":1470,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1876,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1470,"cache_read_input_tokens":585681,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1876,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1876},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"ee3b1903-4428-413c-8204-1586bcfdbc21","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgbEPRjtAYnncrjr2uEVL","requestRef":"9d64b44f-b513-4c87-9c4b-a8b9db5b0f54","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"1551a8ad-2b42-489f-ba3f-ffabf3928de1","timestamp":"2026-11-01T00:05:50.908Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submission","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
