{"parentUuid":"6e6703f7-6a46-4e48-8c33-85e2c57c6dfa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbHpdVcKuRNUFibUjxxf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Po7WBgRR58VxoKgSwtuPWz","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e","summary":"Final submission report with PR and post path","message":"SUBMISSION: READY FOR OWNER — PR https://github.com/Hotragn/Paperghosts/pull/5 (submission → main; mergeable; not merged). Post draft: Docs/POST.md. Head ff15d58, pushed, ls-remote matches; 404 tests, lint and build pass.\n1. **Entire:** fetched all 137 refs; local equals GitHub, and the name scan gets 0 hits on every ref.\n2. **Vector Search not built:** with the permission granted, HF now answers 402 (\"no remaining credits\") for both all-MiniLM-L6-v2 and bge-small. Buying credits is spending, and a local embedder breaks the laptop rule. So moreLikeThis stays, stated in the README, the numbers sheet and the post.\n3. **No Sentry agent spans:** with no model calls running, a gen_ai span would trace nothing real, so none were added. The post says plainly what Sentry traces: every Atlas query, decision 40's fix (110 → 61 ms), and the web app.\n4. **The post** follows DEV's submission sections, with these points:\n   - Title: \"Paper Ghosts: 370 million newspaper articles screened for ghosts, and the 78 reports we can prove\".\n   - It opens on the 1879 Foos mansion report: robbers kept the curious away \"by means of a magic lantern\", a ghost in the machine. Every field verified.\n   - \"Why open matters\" is the $0 Tinker story: gemma4 24/32 (58–87%) against the 397B's 23/32 (55–84%); offline; nothing leaves the machine.\n   - One section per partner, plus disclosures. All numbers are from the sheet, with intervals. Tags: hf26challenge, devchallenge, opensource, ai.\n   - Images point at raw URLs on main, which work once the repo is public and the PR merged.\n   - I couldn't read your ARTICLE-DRAFT.md; it wasn't in the notes folder, so I wrote from the numbers sheet. Merge in anything you want from it.\n5. **QA:**\n   - Secret scan: 13.3 GB of history plus Entire. No keys, 0 hostname, 0 other-account hits, only the two known slugs.\n   - .env, IDEAS.md, data/entire-backup and the rule pack are ignored. MIT licence; data licences are in the README and the post.\n   - axe: 0 violations on all 4 pages in both lights, after fixing stamp opacity contrast, two heading levels and keyboard focus on the scrolling charts. 681 KB per load.\n   - Links: all 205 tile.loc.gov crops are 200. The loc.gov issue pages are behind a Cloudflare check I won't bypass; 2 are confirmed 200 from the cache, and the other 76 use the same pattern. GitHub and raw URLs 404 until public and merged.\n   - Deadline: the API's ends_at reads 2026-10-31 06:59 UTC, but the page text says 11:59 PM PDT on the 31st. Check the challenge page.\n6. **Owner actions:**\n   1. Review and merge PR #5.\n   2. Make the repo public.\n   3. Deploy render.yaml on Render, set VITE_SENTRY_DSN and SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN, then add the live URL to POST.md and an absolute og:image.\n   4. Click one loc.gov issue link to confirm.\n   5. Publish Docs/POST.md on DEV with #hf26challenge.\n   6. Optionally, a DevRelay session embed.","type":"message","recipient":"local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e","recipient_kind":"session","content":"SUBMISSION: READY FOR OWNER — PR https://github.c…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":384,"cache_read_input_tokens":634709,"output_tokens":1939,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":330},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":384,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1939,"cache_read_input_tokens":634709,"cache_creation_input_tokens":384,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":384},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Po7WBgRR58VxoKgSwtuPWz":{"to":"local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e","summary":"Final submission report with PR and post path","message":"SUBMISSION: READY FOR OWNER — PR https://github.com/Hotragn/Paperghosts/pull/5 (submission → main; mergeable; not merged). Post draft: Docs/POST.md. Head ff15d58, pushed, ls-remote matches; 404 tests, lint and build pass.\n1. **Entire:** fetched all 137 refs; local equals GitHub, and the name scan gets 0 hits on every ref.\n2. **Vector Search not built:** with the permission granted, HF now answers 402 (\"no remaining credits\") for both all-MiniLM-L6-v2 and bge-small. Buying credits is spending, and a local embedder breaks the laptop rule. So moreLikeThis stays, stated in the README, the numbers sheet and the post.\n3. **No Sentry agent spans:** with no model calls running, a gen_ai span would trace nothing real, so none were added. The post says plainly what Sentry traces: every Atlas query, decision 40's fix (110 → 61 ms), and the web app.\n4. **The post** follows DEV's submission sections, with these points:\n   - Title: \"Paper Ghosts: 370 million newspaper articles screened for ghosts, and the 78 reports we can prove\".\n   - It opens on the 1879 Foos mansion report: robbers kept the curious away \"by means of a magic lantern\", a ghost in the machine. Every field verified.\n   - \"Why open matters\" is the $0 Tinker story: gemma4 24/32 (58–87%) against the 397B's 23/32 (55–84%); offline; nothing leaves the machine.\n   - One section per partner, plus disclosures. All numbers are from the sheet, with intervals. Tags: hf26challenge, devchallenge, opensource, ai.\n   - Images point at raw URLs on main, which work once the repo is public and the PR merged.\n   - I couldn't read your ARTICLE-DRAFT.md; it wasn't in the notes folder, so I wrote from the numbers sheet. Merge in anything you want from it.\n5. **QA:**\n   - Secret scan: 13.3 GB of history plus Entire. No keys, 0 hostname, 0 other-account hits, only the two known slugs.\n   - .env, IDEAS.md, data/entire-backup and the rule pack are ignored. MIT licence; data licences are in the README and the post.\n   - axe: 0 violations on all 4 pages in both lights, after fixing stamp opacity contrast, two heading levels and keyboard focus on the scrolling charts. 681 KB per load.\n   - Links: all 205 tile.loc.gov crops are 200. The loc.gov issue pages are behind a Cloudflare check I won't bypass; 2 are confirmed 200 from the cache, and the other 76 use the same pattern. GitHub and raw URLs 404 until public and merged.\n   - Deadline: the API's ends_at reads 2026-10-31 06:59 UTC, but the page text says 11:59 PM PDT on the 31st. Check the challenge page.\n6. **Owner actions:**\n   1. Review and merge PR #5.\n   2. Make the repo public.\n   3. Deploy render.yaml on Render, set VITE_SENTRY_DSN and SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN, then add the live URL to POST.md and an absolute og:image.\n   4. Click one loc.gov issue link to confirm.\n   5. Publish Docs/POST.md on DEV with #hf26challenge.\n   6. Optionally, a DevRelay session embed."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"0be3b7ce-b50e-4c4f-af7c-329f792f21da","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgbHpcZJTZbtf7nVgyZW9","requestRef":"9f896edd-a7e0-4c87-a08c-5a4d6edd1ece","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5590657c-6666-4492-9218-8625bdf2cc2f","timestamp":"2026-11-01T00:50:56.195Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"submissi