{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","prNumber":5,"prUrl":"https://github.com/Hotragn/Paperghosts/pull/5","prRepository":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","timestamp":"2026-11-01T00:50:59.075Z"}
{"parentUuid":"b45f6988-d412-4878-8dca-b0e89a5274a1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbHr2Ed6AmYpPjNrn9JA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"SUBMISSION: READY FOR OWNER. [Hotragn/Paperghosts#5](https://github.com/Hotragn/Paperghosts/pull/5) is open from `submission` into `main`; it's mergeable and I haven't merged it. The post draft is [Docs/POST.md](Docs/POST.md). The branch is at ff15d58, pushed and confirmed, with 404 tests, lint and the build passing.\n\n**Entire:** your push worked. All 137 saved-session refs on GitHub match this machine, and the other account's name appears in none of them.\n\n**Vector search is still off.** With the permission granted, Hugging Face now refuses because the account has no inference credits left (HTTP 402), for both open embedding models I tried. Buying credits would be spending, and running an embedder on the laptop breaks the no-local-model rule. So \"ghosts like this one\" stays on Atlas Search's own similarity matching, and the README, numbers sheet and post all say why.\n\n**Sentry has no AI-agent spans.** There were no real model calls left to trace, and I didn't invent any for past runs. The post says plainly what Sentry traces: every Atlas query, the fix it led to (a repeat \"ghosts like\" request went from 110 to 61 ms), and the web app.\n\n**The post:**\n- **Title:** \"Paper Ghosts: 370 million newspaper articles screened for ghosts, and the 78 reports we can prove\".\n- **Opening:** the 1879 Foos mansion report from Springfield, Ohio. A gang hid in the empty house and scared visitors off \"by means of a magic lantern\", a real ghost in the machine, with every field verified against the scan.\n- **\"Why open matters\":** told through the Tinker balance hitting $0. Because the weights are open, the reading moved to the laptop, where gemma4 found 24 of 32 reports (58–87%) against the 397B's 23 (55–84%). It works offline, and nothing about the archive leaves the machine.\n- **The rest:** one section per partner with its proof, the disclosures, and every number taken from the numbers sheet with its interval.\n- **Draft:** I couldn't find the kickoff session's ARTICLE-DRAFT.md, so I wrote the post fresh. Fold in anything you prefer from that draft.\n\n**QA:**\n- **Secret scan:** the full history (13.3 GB) and every Entire session turned up no keys, no hostname and no trace of the other account.\n- **Private files:** `.env`, `IDEAS.md`, the Entire backup and the private rule pack all stay out of git.\n- **Accessibility:** axe finds 0 violations on all four pages in light and dark. Getting there meant fixing stamp contrast, two heading levels and keyboard access to the charts.\n- **Links:** all 205 clipping links work. The loc.gov issue pages sit behind a Cloudflare bot check that I didn't try to get past. 2 are confirmed from our cache, and the other 76 use the same address pattern, so please click one to confirm. The GitHub and image links will work once the repo is public and the PR merged.\n- **Deadline:** DEV's API gives an end time of 06:59 UTC on 31 October, but the page text says 11:59 PM PDT on the 31st. Go by the challenge page.\n\n**Your remaining steps:**\n1. Merge PR #5.\n2. Make the repo public.\n3. Deploy `render.yaml` on Render with `VITE_SENTRY_DSN` and `SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN` set. Then put the live URL into the post and change `og:image` to the image's full address.\n4. Publish `Docs/POST.md` on DEV with #hf26challenge.\n5. Optionally, embed a saved DevRelay session in the post."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2315,"cache_read_input_tokens":635093,"output_tokens":1255,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2315,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"infer