{"parentUuid":"f8d92de8-1837-42e5-85cb-93ed4765b13d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1cd403ea-e7e5-47ea-921d-b458c11322bb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011VCEmJJvGRtffrkmppcMSF","type":"tool_result","content":"1021:**39. No Tinker spend at all, and step 2C runs on this Mac (the owner's call, 2026-10-31). Tinker's balance was $0.00, so the day's runs, $3.19–14.45 by their recorded tokens, went to the owner's card; Tinker sampling is now off in code. On dev the local teacher, gemma4:26b-a4b-it-qat through Ollama, is close to the 397B on finding reports (24 of 32 against 23 of 32) and behind it on kind (100 of 150 against 112 of 150). The week was then submitted with the reader untrained, because local runs froze the Mac.**\n1023:- **The spend:** the table and the token counts are in `Docs/BUDGET.md`'s spend-stopped section. `teacher.read` refuses unless `TINKER_SPEND_ALLOWED=1` is set, which needs the owner's yes. Reading billing stays free.\n1024:- **The rules from here:**\n1027:- **The teacher comparison so far,** on dev after the verifier (`eval/results/phase2c/teacher_dev_r3.json`, `teacher_dev_g26.json`, `format_check.json`):\n1041:- **Local runs:**\n1045:- **Submission:** the owner moved the week to tonight's submission, so 2C.3 is parked as committed on `phase-2c-reader`. The Morgue shows the 78 labelled reports, not the reader's output.\n1047:**40. Sentry traces each Atlas query, and what it showed was fixed: \"ghosts like this one\" now reads its report from Atlas once. Every Atlas query runs in a span of op `db.atlas.query` that carries its kind and latency, never the words searched for. `scripts/sentry_latency.py` pulls p50 and p95 per kind and release from Sentry into `eval/results/sentry_latency.json`.**\n1049:- **The finding (release c0a248f, 40 requests of each kind):**\n1052:- **The fix (release 19a6a4b):** a report doesn't change within a release, so the API keeps what it read, bounded at 1,024 reports.\n1053:  - Over two passes of the same 40 reports, Sentry counts 80 `moreLikeThis` queries but only 40 `find`s. A repeat request is one round trip: p50 63 ms of Atlas time, against 107.\n1055:- **The scripts (release b560aa2):** a script's first query pays to open its connection. A fuzzy search or a `$geoNear` takes p50 525–561 ms cold. A `moreLikeThis` that follows the script's own `find` takes 68 ms. The API's one long-lived client avoids that cost, and its searches run at p50 67–75 ms.\n1056:- **The web app** (paperghosts-web) sends browser tracing and errors only when built with a DSN, and collects nothing about the reader.\n  | | Qwen3.5-397B, round 3, Tinker | gemma4:26b, thinking off, local |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | kind | 112/150 (67–81%) | 100/150 (59–74%) |\n  | report or not | 139/150 | 134/150 |\n  | report recall | 23/32 (55–84%) | 24/32 (58–87%) |\n  | outcome, as scored | 16/23 | 5/24 |\n  | outcome, format normalised (scoring only) | 16/23 | 20/24 |\n  | place_state | 13/23 | 22/24 |\n\n  - gemma4's outcome misses are format, not judgment: 18 of 19 give the outcome as a bare string with no quote. The prompt now says the choice fields carry a quote, and that run hasn't been made.\n  - The 397B's place_state misses are judgment: 7 of 10 fill a state the story-place rule leaves empty.\n  - **gemma4 with thinking on** took 2.4–8.1 minutes an article for the 6 it finished (Ollama's log), so it is a routing lever at most, never the whole draw.\n- **Local runs:**\n  - gemma4 and an mlx-lm job side by side on 24 GB froze the Mac. macOS killed Ollama's runner, and the owner stopped all local model work.\n  - The runs now save each answer as it lands and resume.\n  - From here, one model process at a time.\n- **Submission:** the owner moved the week to tonight's submission, so 2C.3 is parked as committed on `phase-2c-reader`. The Morgue shows the 78 labelled reports, not the reader's output.\n\n**40. Sentry traces each Atlas query, and what it showed was fixed: \"ghosts like this one\" now reads its report from Atlas once. Every Atlas query runs in a span of op `db.atlas.query` that carries its kind and latency, never the words searched for. `scripts/sentry_latency.py` pulls p50 and p95 per kind and release from Sentry into `eval/results/sentry_latency.json`.**\n\n- **The finding (release c0a248f, 40 requests of each kind):**\n  - Each \"ghosts like this one\" request made two Atlas round trips: a `find` for the report's headline and text (p50 41 ms, p95 48), then the `moreLikeThis` (p50 66, p95 76).\n  - A whole fuzzy search was 75 ms.\n- **The fix (release 19a6a4b):** a report doesn't change within a release, so the API keeps what it read, bounded at 1,024 reports.\n  - Over two passes of the same 40 reports, Sentry counts 80 `moreLikeThis` queries but only 40 `find`s. A repeat request is one round trip: p50 63 ms of Atlas time, against 107.\n  - Measured at the client, a repeat request's p50 went from 110 ms to 61, and its p95 from 123 to 68.\n- **The scripts (release b560aa2):** a script's first query pays to open its connection. A fuzzy search or a `$geoNear` takes p50 525–561 ms cold. A `moreLikeThis` that follows the script's own `find` takes 68 ms. The API's one long-lived client avoids that cost, and its searches run at p50 67–75 ms.\n- **The web app** (paperghosts-web) sends browser tracing and errors only when built with a DSN, and collects nothing about the reader.\n  - Its release is the commit, with hidden source maps uploaded, then deleted from the build.\n  - So far its page loads come from scripted loads in the browser pane and headless Chrome. LCP, CLS and INP need real visits that hide or use the page.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4fb04b25-bae5-42f0-8162-073425c29314","timestamp":"2026-11-01T06:46:36.434Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"1021:**39. No Tinker spend at all, and step 2C runs on this Mac (the owner's call, 2026-10-31). Tinker's balance was $0.00, so the day's runs, $3.19–14.45 by their recorded tokens,