{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","prNumber":8,"prUrl":"https://github.com/Hotragn/Paperghosts/pull/8","prRepository":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","timestamp":"2026-11-01T06:49:00.645Z"}
{"parentUuid":"472bb71b-0f38-4382-ba73-fdd3d62e76fc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgbm9XJyB6wjXrP1AL8HK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've opened [Hotragn/Paperghosts#8](https://github.com/Hotragn/Paperghosts/pull/8) from `onboarding-motion` at 4f90a89. It is not merged or deployed. Lint, the 404 tests and the build pass locally, but CI hadn't reported when I checked, so that gate is still open.\n\n**Onboarding:**\n- A first-visit note sits above the request slip. It says what a morgue is, with the report count and years read from `reports.json`.\n- The note shows one real report: the 1879 Springfield haunting, a hoax done with a magic lantern, with its two verified quotes. Its one button is \"Read this report\".\n- The note gives each of the three rooms one line.\n- An opened report shows a hint once, explaining the marked quotes and \"Not stated\".\n- A search that finds nothing suggests apparition, haunted or knocking (8, 14 and 2 reports), or clearing the slip.\n- Each note can be put away, and that's remembered across reloads.\n\n**Motion:**\n- Lenis smooths wheel scrolling only.\n- From React Bits:\n  - SplitText fades the tagline in from a blur.\n  - FadeContent brings in the featured report and the paper samples like a developing print.\n  - Noise adds a still paper grain that never redraws.\n- The React Bits code is copied unchanged into `web/src/bits/`, with its licence notice.\n- The drawer's report list doesn't animate, so search and filter work as before.\n- There's no WebGL.\n- With reduced motion, Lenis doesn't start, the tagline is plain text, content shows at once and GSAP is never downloaded. The still grain stays, since it doesn't move; decision 41 says so.\n\n**Bundle:** the main JS went from 75.76 to 84.84 kB gzipped. Putting GSAP straight into the main bundle would have made it 136 kB gzipped, so it loads separately (52.38 kB gzipped). Only motion visitors download it, after the page has appeared.\n\n**What I checked:**\n- axe finds 0 violations on 5 views, in both lights, at desktop and phone width, with and without reduced motion. It caught one problem of mine first: GSAP's SplitText puts a label on the tagline that a `<p>` isn't allowed, so screen readers might skip it. They now get a plain copy and the animated one is hidden from them.\n- In headless Chrome, with and without reduced motion:\n  - The skip link is the first Tab stop and lands on the content.\n  - The `#drawer` link and the rooms nav work with Lenis on.\n  - The hint, the suggestions and putting the notes away all work.\n- The secret scan of the diff and its Entire checkpoint found no keys, no hostname and no other-account hits.\n\nDecision 41 is in `Docs/DECISIONS.md`. The eight before-and-after first-view screenshots are in `Docs/demo/screenshots/first-*.jpg` and also in the PR body.\n\nI didn't run a brainstorming step or the DEV library survey, since the EM had already chosen Lenis and React Bits. I haven't watched the motion in a visible browser window: the app's browser pane was hidden, so animations couldn't run there and I checked them in headless Chrome only."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":469,"cache_read_input_tokens":215015,"output_tokens":1073,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":469,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1073,"cache_read_input_tokens":215015,"cache_creation_input_tokens":469,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":469},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierReques